ese leaves is known to refresh a tired body.',50,NULL,'Petilil','13','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-14','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,'Petilil','Even veteran Trainers face a challenge in getting its beautiful flower to bloom. This Pokémon is popular with celebrities.',90,NULL,'Lilligant','14','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-15','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The turning of the seasons changes the color and scent of this Pokémon\'s fur. People use it to mark the seasons.',60,NULL,'Deerling','15','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-16','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Deerling','The plants growing on its horns change according to the season. The leaders of the herd possess magnificent horns.',100,NULL,'Sawsbuck','16','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-17','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon fought humans in order to protect its friends. Legends about it continue to be passed down.',100,NULL,'Virizion','17','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('bw2-18','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon lives in caves in volcanoes. The fire within the tuft on its head can reach 600º F.',70,NULL,'Pansear','18','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-19','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,1,'Pansear','A flame burns inside its body. It scatters embers from its head and tail to sear its opponents.',90,NULL,'Simisear','19','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-2','match',NULL,NULL,2,'Pansage','Ill tempered, it fights by swinging its barbed tail around wildly. The leaf growing on its head is very bitter.',90,NULL,'Simisage','2','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-20','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'When its internal fire is burning, it cannot calm down and it runs around. When the fire diminishes, it falls asleep.',70,NULL,'Darumaka','20','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-21','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,3,'Darumaka','Its internal fire burns at 2,500º F, making enough power that it can destroy a dump truck with one punch.',100,NULL,'Darmanitan','21','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-22','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It does not thrive in dry environments. It keeps itself damp by shooting water stored in its head tuft from its tail.',70,NULL,'Panpour','22','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-23','Sumiyoshi Kizuki',NULL,NULL,1,'Panpour','The tuft on its head holds water. When the level runs low, it replenishes the tuft by siphoning up water with its tail.',90,NULL,'Simipour','23','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-24','match',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Red and blue Basculin get along so poorly, they\'ll start fighting instantly. These Pokémon are very hostile.',80,NULL,'Basculin','24','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-25','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Red and blue Basculin usually do not get along, but sometimes members of one school mingle with the other\'s school.',80,NULL,'Basculin','25','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-26','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When attacked, it uses its feathers to splash water, escaping under cover of the spray.',60,NULL,'Ducklett','26','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-27','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,'Ducklett','It administers sharp, powerful pecks with its bill. It whips its long neck to deliver forceful repeated strikes.',90,NULL,'Swanna','27','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-28','sui',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'When it is not feeling well, its mucus gets watery and the power of its Ice-type moves decreases.',70,NULL,'Cubchoo','28','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-29','Kanako Eo',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its nose is always running. It sniffs the snot back up because the mucus provides the raw material for its moves.',70,NULL,'Cubchoo','29','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-3','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Leavanny dress it in clothes they made for it when it hatched. It hides its head in its hood while it is sleeping.',40,NULL,'Sewaddle','3','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-30','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,3,'Cubchoo','It can make its breath freeze at will. Very able in the water, it swims around in northern seas and catches prey.',130,NULL,'Beartic','30','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('bw2-31','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Cubchoo','It freezes its breath to create fangs and claws of ice to fight with. Cold northern areas are its habitat.',130,NULL,'Beartic','31','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-32','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The energy made in its cheeks\' electric pouches is stored inside its membranes and released while it is gliding.',70,NULL,'Emolga','32','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-33','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Joltik that live in cities have learned a technique for sucking electricity from the outlets in houses.',40,NULL,'Joltik','33','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-34','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Joltik','When attacked, they create an electric barrier by spitting out many electrically charged threads.',80,NULL,'Galvantula','34','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-35','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The spikes on its tail discharge immense bolts of lightning. It flies around the Unova region firing off lightning bolts.',110,NULL,'Thundurus','35','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('bw2-36','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its habitat is dark forests and caves. It emits ultrasonic waves from its nose to learn about its surroundings.',60,NULL,'Woobat','36','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-37','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,'Woobat','Anyone who comes into contact with the ultrasonic waves emitted by a courting male experiences a positive mood shift.',90,NULL,'Swoobat','37','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-38','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It discovers what is going on around it by using the feelers on its head and tail. It is brutally aggressive.',70,NULL,'Venipede','38','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-39','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,'Venipede','It is usually motionless, but when attacked, it rotates at high speed and then crashes into its opponent.',90,NULL,'Whirlipede','39','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-4','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon makes clothes for itself. It chews up leaves and sews them with sticky thread extruded from its mouth.',50,NULL,'Sewaddle','4','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-40','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,'Whirlipede','With quick movements, it chases down its foes, attacking relentlessly with its horns until it prevails.',140,NULL,'Scolipede','40','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-41','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The guardians of an ancient city, they use their psychic power to attack enemies that invade their territory.',90,NULL,'Sigilyph','41','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-42','match',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They never vary the route they fly, because their memories of guarding an ancient city remain steadfast.',90,NULL,'Sigilyph','42','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-43','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Their ribbonlike feelers increase their psychic power. They are always staring at something.',60,NULL,'Gothita','43','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-44','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They intently observe both Trainers and Pokémon. Apparently, they are looking at something that only Gothita can see.',60,NULL,'Gothita','44','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-45','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,'Gothita','They use hypnosis to control people and Pokémon. Tales of Gothorita leading people astray are told in every corner.',80,NULL,'Gothorita','45','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-46','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,'Gothita','Starlight is the source of their power. At night, they mark star positions by using psychic power to float stones.',80,NULL,'Gothorita','46','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-47','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Gothorita','Starry skies thousands of light-years away are visible in the space distorted by their intense psychic power.',130,NULL,'Gothitelle','47','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('bw2-48','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Gothorita','They can predict the future from the placement and movement of the stars. They can see Trainers\' life spans.',120,NULL,'Gothitelle','48','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-49','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its ear is hexagonal in shape. Compressed underground, its body is as hard as steel.',60,NULL,'Roggenrola','49','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-5','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,'Sewaddle','It protects itself from the cold by wrapping up in leaves. It stays on the move, eating leaves in forests.',80,NULL,'Swadloon','5','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-50','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'They were discovered a hundred years ago in an earthquake fissure. Inside each one is an energy core.',60,NULL,'Roggenrola','50','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-51','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,3,'Roggenrola','When it overflows with power, the orange crystal on its body glows. It looks for underground water in caves.',90,NULL,'Boldore','51','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-52','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,3,'Roggenrola','Because its energy was too great to be contained, the energy leaked and formed orange crystals.',90,NULL,'Boldore','52','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-53','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,4,'Boldore','The solar energy absorbed by its body\'s orange crystals is magnified internally and fired from its mouth.',140,NULL,'Gigalith','53','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-54','match',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It can dig through the ground at a speed of 30 mph. It could give a car running aboveground a good race.',70,NULL,'Drilbur','54','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-55','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It makes its way swiftly through the soil by putting both claws together and rotating at high speed.',60,NULL,'Drilbur','55','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-56','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Drilbur','It can help in tunnel construction. Its drill has evolved into steel strong enough to bore through iron plates.',110,NULL,'Excadrill','56','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('bw2-57','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Drilbur','More than 300 feet below the surface, they build mazelike nests. Their activity can be destructive to subway tunnels.',120,NULL,'Excadrill','57','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-58','match',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'When it tightens its belt, it becomes stronger. Wild Throh use vines to weave their own belts.',90,NULL,'Throh','58','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-59','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Tying their belts gets them pumped and makes their punches more destructive. Disturbing their training angers them.',90,NULL,'Sawk','59','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-6','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,2,'Sewaddle','Forests where Swadloon live have superb foliage because the nutrients they make from fallen leaves nourish the plant life.',70,NULL,'Swadloon','6','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-60','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'They live buried in the sands of the desert. The sun-warmed sands prevent their body temperature from dropping.',70,NULL,'Sandile','60','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-61','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Sandile','They live in groups of a few individuals. Protective membranes shield their eyes from sandstorms.',90,NULL,'Krokorok','61','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-62','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,3,'Krokorok','They never allow prey to escape. Their jaws are so powerful, they can crush the body of an automobile.',140,NULL,'Krookodile','62','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-63','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'This Pokémon came to the defense of Pokémon that had lost their homes in a war among humans.',120,NULL,'Terrakion','63','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('bw2-64','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They steal from people for fun, but their victims can\'t help but forgive them. Their deceptively cute act is perfect.',60,NULL,'Purrloin','64','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-65','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,'Purrloin','These Pokémon vanish and appear unexpectedly. Many Trainers are drawn to their beautiful form and fur.',80,NULL,'Liepard','65','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-66','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It changes into the forms of others to surprise them. Apparently, it often transforms into a silent child.',50,NULL,'Zorua','66','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-67','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Zorua','Bonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents.',100,NULL,'Zoroark','67','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('bw2-68','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They tend to guard their posteriors with suitable bones they have found. They pursue weak Pokémon.',50,NULL,'Vullaby','68','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-69','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,1,'Vullaby','Watching from the sky, they swoop to strike weakened Pokémon on the ground. They decorate themselves with bones.',90,NULL,'Mandibuzz','69','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-7','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Swadloon','Upon finding a small Pokémon, it weaves clothing for it from leaves, using the cutters on its arms and sticky silk.',130,NULL,'Leavanny','7','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-70','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'They stick their spikes into cave walls and absorb the minerals they find in the rock.',60,NULL,'Ferroseed','70','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-71','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'When threatened, it attacks by shooting a barrage of spikes, which gives it a chance to escape by rolling away.',50,NULL,'Ferroseed','71','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-72','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Ferroseed','They attach themselves to cave ceilings, firing steel spikes at targets passing beneath them.',90,NULL,'Ferrothorn','72','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-73','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,3,'Ferroseed','It fights by swinging around its three spiky feelers. A hit from these steel spikes can reduce a boulder to rubble.',90,NULL,'Ferrothorn','73','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-74','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Interlocking two bodies and spinning around generates the energy they need to live.',60,NULL,'Klink','74','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-75','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Klink','Spinning minigears are rotated at high speed and repeatedly fired away. It is dangerous if the gears don\'t return.',80,NULL,'Klang','75','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-76','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,4,'Klang','The gear with the red core is rotated at high speed for a rapid energy charge.',150,NULL,'Klinklang','76','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-77','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This legendary Pokémon battled against humans to protect Pokémon. Its personality is calm and composed.',110,NULL,'Cobalion','77','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('bw2-78','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Extremely cautious, they take shifts to maintain a constant watch of their nest. They feel insecure without a lookout.',60,NULL,'Patrat','78','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-79','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,'Patrat','When they see an enemy, their tails stand high, and they spit the seeds of berries stored in their cheek pouches.',90,NULL,'Watchog','79','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-8','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,'Swadloon','It keeps its eggs warm with heat from fermenting leaves. It also uses leaves to make warm wrappings for Sewaddle.',130,NULL,'Leavanny','8','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-80','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Each follows its Trainer\'s orders as best it can, but they sometimes fail to understand complicated commands.',50,NULL,'Pidove','80','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-81','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,'Pidove','Many people believe that, deep in the forest where Tranquill live, there is a peaceful place where there is no war.',70,NULL,'Tranquill','81','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-82','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tranquill','Males have plumage on their heads. They will never let themselves fell close to anyone other than their Trainers.',120,NULL,'Unfezant','82','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw2-83','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its auditory sense is astounding. It has a radar-like ability to understand its surrounding through slight sounds.',90,NULL,'Audino','83','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-84','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'These Pokémon prefer a tidy habitat. They are always sweeping and dusting, using their tails as brooms.',60,NULL,'Minccino','84','Common','Pokémon'),('bw2-85','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,'Minccino','Their white fur feels amazing to touch. Their fur repels dust and prevents static electricity from building up.',90,NULL,'Cinccino','85','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw2-86','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They will challenge anything, even strong opponents, without fear. Their frequent fights help them become stronger.',60,NULL,'Rufflet','86','Common','Pokémon'),(