LL,'Yamask','44','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-45','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'These Pokémon arose from the spirits of people interred in graves in past ages. Each retains memories of its former life.',60,NULL,'Yamask','45','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-46','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,3,'Yamask','It has been said that they swallow those who get too close and turn them into mummies. They like to eat gold nuggets.',90,NULL,'Cofagrigus','46','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-47','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Yamask','They pretend to be elaborate coffins to teach lessons to grave robbers. Their bodies are covered in pure gold.',90,NULL,'Cofagrigus','47','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-48','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The combination of garbage bags and industrial waste caused the chemical reaction that created this Pokémon.',60,NULL,'Trubbish','48','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-49','match',NULL,NULL,3,'Trubbish','They absorb garbage and make it part of their bodies. They shoot poisonous liquid from their right-hand fingertips.',100,NULL,'Garbodor','49','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw3-5','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,'Petilil','The fragrance of the garland on its head has a relaxing effect. It withers if a Trainer does not take good care of it.',80,NULL,'Lilligant','5','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-50','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They drive away attackers by unleashing psychic power. They can use telepathy to talk with others.',30,NULL,'Solosis','50','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-51','sui',NULL,NULL,1,'Solosis','Since they have two divided brains, at times they suddenly try to take two different actions at once.',60,NULL,'Duosion','51','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw3-52','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Duosion','When Reuniclus shake hands, a network forms between their brains, increasing their psychic power.',90,NULL,'Reuniclus','52','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-53','Mizue',NULL,NULL,2,'Duosion','These remarkably intelligent Pokémon fight by controlling arms that can grip with rock-crushing power.',90,NULL,'Reuniclus','53','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-54','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon had never been seen until it appeared from far in the desert 50 years ago.',60,NULL,'Elgyem','54','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-55','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It uses its strong psychic power to squeeze its opponent\'s brain, causing unendurable headaches.',60,NULL,'Elgyem','55','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-56','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,'Elgyem','It uses psychic power to control an opponent\'s brain and tamper with its memories.',80,NULL,'Beheeyem','56','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-57','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Litwick shines a light that absorbs the life energy of people and Pokémon, which becomes the fuel it burns.',50,NULL,'Litwick','57','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-58','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'While shining a light and pretending to be a guide, it leaches off the life force of any who follow it.',50,NULL,'Litwick','58','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-59','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,'Litwick','This ominous Pokémon is feared. Through cities it wanders, searching for the spirits of the fallen.',80,NULL,'Lampent','59','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw3-6','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The Pokémon can easily melt holes in hard rocks with a liquid secreted from its mouth.',60,NULL,'Dwebble','6','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-60','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,2,'Lampent','It absorbs a spirit, which it then burns. By waving the flames on its arms, it puts its foes into a hypnotic trance.',130,NULL,'Chandelure','60','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-61','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,4,'Boldore','Compressing the energy from its internal core lets it fire off an attack capable of blowing away a mountain.',150,NULL,'Gigalith','61','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-62','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It fights by swinging a piece of lumber around. It is close to evolving when it can handle the lumber without difficulty.',60,NULL,'Timburr','62','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-63','Sumiyoshi Kizuki',NULL,NULL,3,'Timburr','This Pokémon is so muscular and strongly built that even a group of wrestlers could not make it budge an inch.',80,NULL,'Gurdurr','63','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw3-64','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,4,'Gurdurr','It it thought that Conkeldurr taught humans how to make concrete more than 2,000 years ago.',140,NULL,'Conkeldurr','64','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('bw3-65','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,3,'Gurdurr','They use concrete pillars as walking canes. They know moves that enable them to swing the pillars freely in battle.',140,NULL,'Conkeldurr','65','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-66','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,'Plume Fossil','Said to be an ancestor of bird Pokémon, they were unable to fly and moved about by hopping from one branch to another.',80,NULL,'Archen','66','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw3-67','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Archen','They are intelligent and will cooperate to catch prey. From the ground, they use a running start to take flight.',130,NULL,'Archeops','67','Rare','Pokémon'),('bw3-68','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It conceals itself in the mud of the seashore. Then it waits. When prey touch it, it delivers a volt of electricity.',90,NULL,'Stunfisk','68','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw3-69','match',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'In fights, they dominate with onslaughts of flowing, continuous attack. With their sharp claws, they cut enemies.',50,NULL,'Mienfoo','69','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-7','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,3,'Dwebble','Competing for territory, Crustle fight viciously. The one whose boulder is broken is the loser of the battle.',100,NULL,'Crustle','7','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw3-70','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,'Mienfoo','It wield the fur on its arms like a whip. Its arms attacks come with such rapidity that they cannot even be seen.',90,NULL,'Mienshao','70','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('bw3-71','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'These Pokémon are thought to have been created by the science of an ancient and mysterious civilization.',80,NULL,'Golett','71','Common','Pokémon'),('bw3-72','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,4,'Golet