powerful Pokémon, its sharp claws can leave its Trainer\'s whole body covered in scratches.',80,NULL,'Torracat','28','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-29','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,2,'Torracat','Although it\'s rough mannered and egotistical, it finds beating down unworthy opponents boring. It gets motivated for stronger opponents.',160,NULL,'Incineroar','29','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-3','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,3,'Caterpie','Its shell is filled with a thick liquid. All of the cells throughout its body are being rebuilt in preparation for evolution.',70,NULL,'Metapod','3','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-30','Yusuke Ohmura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The males will do whatever the females tell them. They give the females most of their food. Due to malnutrition, the males can\'t evolve.',70,NULL,'Salandit','30','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-31','hatachu',NULL,NULL,1,'Salandit','Salazzle lives deep in caves and forces the Salandit it has attracted with its pheromones to serve it.',100,NULL,'Salazzle','31','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-32','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It slithers toward people. Then, without warning, it triggers the explosion of its own head. It\'s apparently one kind of Ultra Beast.',120,NULL,'Blacephalon','32','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-33','tetsuya koizumi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It shelters itself in its shell, then strikes back with spouts of water at every opportunity.',60,NULL,'Squirtle','33','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-34','Hiroki Asanuma',NULL,NULL,2,'Squirtle','When tapped, this Pokémon will pull in its head, but its tail will still stick out a little bit.',70,NULL,'Wartortle','34','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-35','sadaji',NULL,NULL,3,'Wartortle',NULL,240,NULL,'Blastoise-GX','35','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm10-36','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Despite the danger, it wants to come up on land. So it does its best to waddle along, but when an enemy finds it, it rushes back to the water.',50,NULL,'Poliwag','36','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-37','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Despite the danger, it wants to come up on land. So it does its best to waddle along, but when an enemy finds it, it rushes back to the water.',60,NULL,'Poliwag','37','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-38','Yukiko Baba',NULL,NULL,2,'Poliwag','Although it has become capable of living on land, it spends its time in the water, where its prey, fish Pokémon, are plentiful.',90,NULL,'Poliwhirl','38','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-39','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,3,'Poliwhirl','It\'s quite a gifted swimmer, even among Water-type Pokémon, but it normally spends its time on land.',150,NULL,'Poliwrath','39','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-4','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,'Metapod','Its wings are covered in toxic scales. If it finds bird Pokémon going after Caterpie, Butterfree sprinkles its scales on them to drive them off.',130,NULL,'Butterfree','4','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-40','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It drifts through the sea searching for prey. Its poisonous tentacles break off sometimes, but after a while, they grow back.',60,NULL,'Tentacool','40','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-41','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,'Tentacool','It fires off ultrasonic waves from its red orbs to weaken its prey, and then it wraps them up in its 80 tentacles.',100,NULL,'Tentacruel','41','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-42','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'There are some places where Slowpoke is worshiped because of a long-standing belief that whenever Slowpoke yawns, it rains.',70,NULL,'Slowpoke','42','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-43','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,2,'Slowpoke','Spacing out is basically all it does. It turns back into Slowpoke if its tail, along with Shellder, breaks off.',120,NULL,'Slowbro','43','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm10-44','Sumiyoshi Kizuki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It has always been supposed that Seel live only in cold seas. Their having shown up in Alola is a mystery.',80,NULL,'Seel','44','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-45','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Seel','It swims through the ocean at a speed of eight knots, searching for Pokémon that will become its prey. It\'s especially fond of Wishiwashi.',120,NULL,'Dewgong','45','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-46','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'If it senses danger approaching, it cloaks itself with bubbles from its mouth so it will look bigger.',70,NULL,'Krabby','46','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-47','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,4,'Krabby','Its large and hard pincer has 10,000-horsepower strength. However, being so big, it is unwieldy to move.',130,NULL,'Kingler','47','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-48','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Although known for their splendid tail fins, Goldeen apparently compete among themselves to see whose horn is thickest and sharpest.',60,NULL,'Goldeen','48','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-49','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,'Goldeen','Its horn spins like a drill to steadily hollow out rocks—even harder ones. The coloration of the male is more vivid.',100,NULL,'Seaking','49','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-5','0313',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'During the day, It stays in the cold underground to avoid the sun. It grows by bathing in moonlight.',50,NULL,'Oddish','5','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-50','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This legendary ice Pokémon waits for a hero to fill in the missing parts of its body with truth or ideals.',130,NULL,'Kyurem','50','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm10-51','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It secretes flexible bubbles from its chest and back. The bubbles reduce the damage it would otherwise take when attacked.',60,NULL,'Froakie','51','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-52','Satoshi Shirai',NULL,NULL,1,'Froakie','It can throw bubble-covered pebbles with precise control, hitting empty cans up to a hundred feet away.',80,NULL,'Frogadier','52','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-53','Asako Ito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The tradition known as Pyukumuku chucking started from the custom of throwing Pyukumuku back into the sea after they wash onshore.',70,NULL,'Pyukumuku','53','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-54','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its nature is to store up electricity. Forests where nests of Pikachu live are dangerous, since the trees are so often struck by lightning.',70,NULL,'Pikachu','54','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-55','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Pikachu','As electricity builds up inside its body, it becomes more aggressive. One theory is that the electricity buildup is actually causing stress.',120,NULL,'Raichu','55','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-56','sowsow',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Its skin is very hard, so it is unhurt even if stepped on by sumo wrestlers. It smiles when transmitting electricity.',110,NULL,'Stunfisk','56','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-57','PLANETA Igarashi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,160,NULL,'Dedenne-GX','57','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm10-58','Sekio',NULL,NULL,3,'Grubbin','It buries itself in fallen leaves and barely moves, munching away on humus. If you accidentally step on one, you\'ll get a shock!',80,NULL,'Charjabug','58','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-59','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,2,'Charjabug','It has an organ that generates electricity in its abdomen. It concentrates energy in its strong jaws and fires off powerful jolts of electricity.',150,NULL,'Vikavolt','59','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm10-6','Asako Ito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'During the day, It stays in the cold underground to avoid the sun. It grows by bathing in moonlight.',60,NULL,'Oddish','6','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-60','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It electrifies its claws and tears its opponents apart with them. Even if they dodge its attack, they\'ll be electrocuted by the flying sparks.',120,NULL,'Zeraora','60','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-61','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,270,NULL,'Muk & Alolan Muk-GX','61','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm10-62','Yumi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'By dislocating its jaw, it can swallow prey larger than itself. After a meal, it curls up and rests.',70,NULL,'Ekans','62','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-63','Yukiko Baba',NULL,NULL,2,'Ekans','The latest research has determined that there are over 20 possible arrangements of the patterns on its stomach.',120,NULL,'Arbok','63','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-64','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has no eyeballs, so it can\'t see. It checks its surroundings via the ultrasonic waves it emits from its mouth.',50,NULL,'Zubat','64','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-65','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,'Zubat','Every once in a while, you\'ll see a Golbat that\'s missing some fangs. This happens when hunger drives it to try biting a Steel-type Pokémon.',80,NULL,'Golbat','65','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-66','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Golbat','Its fangs are so sharp, if it bites you in the dark and sucks your blood, you won\'t notice any pain or realize you\'ve been bitten.',130,NULL,'Crobat','66','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm10-67','chibi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s said that gas emanating from a graveyard was possessed by the grievances of the deceased and thus became a Pokémon.',40,NULL,'Gastly','67','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-68','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s said that gas emanating from a graveyard was possessed by the grievances of the deceased and thus became a Pokémon.',60,NULL,'Gastly','68','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-69','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,'Gastly','On moonless nights, Haunter searches for someone to curse, so it\'s best not to go out walking around.',70,NULL,'Haunter','69','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-7','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,'Oddish','Smells incredibly foul! However, around one out of a thousand people enjoy sniffing its nose-bending stink.',80,NULL,'Gloom','7','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-70','so-taro',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Haunter','You can hear tales told all over the world about how Gengar will pay a visit to children who are naughty.',130,NULL,'Gengar','70','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-71','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It can be spotted near recreational facilities, intending to eat the pleasant dreams of children who enjoyed themselves there that day.',70,NULL,'Drowzee','71','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-72','sui',NULL,NULL,2,'Drowzee','In Alola, Komala is Hypno\'s main target. It rarely harms people.',110,NULL,'Hypno','72','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-73','Mizue',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its thin, balloon-like body is inflated by horribly toxic gases. It reeks when it is nearby.',70,NULL,'Koffing','73','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-74','OOYAMA',NULL,NULL,3,'Koffing','If one of the twin Koffing inflates, the other one deflates. It constantly mixes its poisonous gases.',120,NULL,'Weezing','74','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-75','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It was created by a scientist after years of horrific gene-splicing and DNA-engineering experiments.',120,NULL,'Mewtwo','75','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-76','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Because it can use all kinds of moves, many scientists believe Mew to be the ancestor of Pokémon.',60,NULL,'Mew','76','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm10-77','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'What gives meaning to its life is surprising others. If you set your ear against the red orbs around its neck, you can hear shrieking.',60,NULL,'Misdreavus','77','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-78','sui',NULL,NULL,1,'Misdreavus','Feared for its wrath and the curses it spreads, this Pokémon will also, on a whim, cast spells that help people.',110,NULL,'Mismagius','78','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-79','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The organ that emits its intense psychic power is sheltered by its ears to keep power from leaking out.',60,NULL,'Espurr','79','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-8','Suwama Chiaki',NULL,NULL,3,'Gloom','The larger its petals, the more toxic pollen it contains. Its big head is heavy and hard to hold up.',140,NULL,'Vileplume','8','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm10-80','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,'Espurr','When in danger, it raises its ears and releases enough psychic power to grind a 10-ton truck into dust.',90,NULL,'Meowstic','80','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-81','chibi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It slips into the shadows of others and mimics their powers and movements. As it improves, it becomes stronger than those it\'s imitating.',80,NULL,'Marshadow','81','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm10-82','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,270,NULL,'Marshadow & Machamp-GX','82','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm10-83','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It lives in areas of limited rainfall. When danger approaches, it curls up into a ball to protect its soft stomach.',70,NULL,'Sandshrew','83','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-84','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,'Sandshrew','Its claws and horns often break off. The broken claws and horns can be used to carve plows for tilling farm fields.',110,NULL,'Sandslash','84','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-85','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It travels through tunnels that it digs underground. It hates sunlight, so it comes out only after the sun goes down.',50,NULL,'Diglett','85','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-86','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,'Diglett','While the three of them normally get along splendidly, on rare occasions a huge fight will break out over which head gets to eat first.',90,NULL,'Dugtrio','86','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm10-87','Sumiyoshi Kizuki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Geodude that have lived a long life have had all their edges smoothed out until they\'re totally round. They also have a calm, quiet disposition.',70,NULL,'Geodude','87','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-88','Ayaka Yoshida',NULL,NULL,4,'Geodude','It climbs up cliffs as it heads toward the peak of a mountain. As soon as it reaches the summit, it rolls back down the way it came.',110,NULL,'Graveler','88','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm10-89','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,4,'Graveler','When Golem grow old, they stop shedding their shells. Those that have lived a long, long time have shells green with moss.',180,NULL,'Golem','89','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm10-9','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its big eyes are actually clusters of tiny eyes. At night, its kind is drawn by light.',60,NULL,'Venonat','9','Common','Pokémon'),('sm10-90','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'At night, it weeps loudly for its dead mother, but those crie