 give the females most of their food. Due to malnutrition, the males can\'t evolve.',70,NULL,'Salandit','33','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-34','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,'Salandit','Salazzle lives deep in caves and forces the Salandit it has attracted with its pheromones to serve it.',100,NULL,'Salazzle','34','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm11-35','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,250,NULL,'Slowpoke & Psyduck-GX','35','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm11-36','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It likes swimming around with people on its back. In the Alola region, it\'s an important means of transportation over water.',110,NULL,'Lapras','36','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-37','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It feeds mainly on ice and snow. It\'s only able to survive in a limited number of places in the warm Alola region.',50,NULL,'Snorunt','37','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-38','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,'Snorunt','It freezes hikers who have come to climb snowy mountains and carries them back to its home. It only goes after men it thinks are handsome.',80,NULL,'Froslass','38','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm11-39','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When night falls, their pink patterns begin to shine. They\'re popular with divers, so there are resorts that feed them to keep them close.',50,NULL,'Finneon','39','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-4','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon wanders across time. Grass and trees flourish in the forests in which it has appeared.',80,NULL,'Celebi','4','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm11-40','Sekio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Finneon','Deep down at the bottom of the ocean, prey is scarce. Lumineon get into fierce disputes with Lanturn over food.',90,NULL,'Lumineon','40','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-41','otumami',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'During cold seasons, it migrates to the mountain\'s lower reaches. It returns to the snow-covered summit in the spring.',90,NULL,'Snover','41','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-42','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,4,'Snover','It blankets wide areas in snow by whipping up blizzards. It is also known as \"The Ice Monster.\"',140,NULL,'Abomasnow','42','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm11-43','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Savage, violent Pokémon, red and blue Basculin are always fighting each other over territory.',80,NULL,'Basculin','43','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-44','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,3,'Unidentified Fossil','It was restored from an ancient fossil. Tirtouga lived in the sea but came up onto the land to search for prey.',100,NULL,'Tirtouga','44','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-45','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,3,'Tirtouga','Its jaws are terrifyingly powerful. It could eat Omastar and Omanyte whole and not be bothered in the slightest by their shells.',160,NULL,'Carracosta','45','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-46','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They are born in snow clouds. They use chains made of ice crystals to capture prey.',90,NULL,'Cryogonal','46','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-47','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,170,NULL,'Keldeo-GX','47','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm11-48','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When two Dewpider meet, they display their water bubbles to each other. Then the one with the smaller bubble gets out of the other\'s way.',60,NULL,'Dewpider','48','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-49','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,'Dewpider','It usually passes its time in the water. When its belly is full, it stores its subdued prey in the water bubble on its head.',100,NULL,'Araquanid','49','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm11-5','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It prefers damp places. By day it remains still in the forest shade. It releases toxic powder from its head.',60,NULL,'Shroomish','5','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-50','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It will pick up anything it finds on the ground. Sometimes it finds coins, so Murkrow and Meowth will go after it.',70,NULL,'Wimpod','50','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-51','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,4,'Wimpod','The shell covering its body is as hard as diamond. This Pokémon will do anything it takes to win.',140,NULL,'Golisopod','51','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm11-52','OOYAMA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The tradition known as Pyukumuku chucking started from the custom of throwing Pyukumuku back into the sea after they wash onshore.',80,NULL,'Pyukumuku','52','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-53','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This guardian deity of Poni Island manipulates water. Because it lives deep within a thick fog, it came to be both feared and revered.',120,NULL,'Tapu Fini','53','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm11-54','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,260,NULL,'Raichu & Alolan Raichu-GX','54','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm11-55','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its nature is to store up electricity. Forests where nests of Pikachu live are dangerous, since the trees are so often struck by lightning.',60,NULL,'Pikachu','55','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-56','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its nature is to store up electricity. Forests where nests of Pikachu live are dangerous, since the trees are so often struck by lightning.',70,NULL,'Pikachu','56','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-57','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Pikachu','It focuses psychic energy into its tail and rides it like it\'s surfing. Another name for this Pokémon is \"hodad.\"',110,NULL,'Alolan Raichu','57','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm11-58','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s frequently the cause of power outages, which is why some power plants send out electrical signals that it can\'t stand.',60,NULL,'Magnemite','58','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-59','Yumi',NULL,NULL,2,'Magnemite','Delicate equipment can malfunction in areas inhabited by Magneton, which send out mysterious electrical signals.',90,NULL,'Magneton','59','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-6','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon makes clothes for itself. It chews up leaves and sews them with sticky thread extruded from its mouth.',50,NULL,'Sewaddle','6','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-60','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,'Magneton','It uses radar to monitor its territory. Intruders are quickly disposed of with a hyper beam.',160,NULL,'Magnezone','60','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm11-61','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Since it can\'t generate its own electricity, it sticks onto large-bodied Pokémon and absorbs static electricity.',40,NULL,'Joltik','61','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-62','Yumi',NULL,NULL,1,'Joltik','They employ an electrically charged web to trap their prey. While it is immobilized by shock, they leisurely consume it.',90,NULL,'Galvantula','62','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm11-63','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'While one alone doesn\'t have much power, a chain of many Tynamo can be as powerful as lightning.',30,NULL,'Tynamo','63','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-64','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'While one alone doesn\'t have much power, a chain of many Tynamo can be as powerful as lightning.',40,NULL,'Tynamo','64','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-65','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,2,'Tynamo','It wraps itself around its prey and paralyzes it with electricity from the round spots on its sides. Then it chomps.',90,NULL,'Eelektrik','65','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-66','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,3,'Eelektrik','With their sucker mouths, they suck in prey. Then they use their fangs to shock the prey with electricity.',150,NULL,'Eelektross','66','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm11-67','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its skin is very hard, so it is unhurt even if stepped on by sumo wrestlers. It smiles when transmitting electricity.',90,NULL,'Stunfisk','67','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-68','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The spikes on its tail discharge immense bolts of lightning. It flies around the Unova region firing off lightning bolts.',120,NULL,'Thundurus','68','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-69','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Although it\'s called a guardian deity, if a person or Pokémon puts it in a bad mood, it will become a malevolent deity and attack.',120,NULL,'Tapu Koko','69','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm11-7','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon makes clothes for itself. It chews up leaves and sews them with sticky thread extruded from its mouth.',50,NULL,'Sewaddle','7','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-70','Satoshi Shirai',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Although it\'s alien to this world and a danger here, it\'s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.',120,NULL,'Xurkitree','70','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm11-71','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,270,NULL,'Mewtwo & Mew-GX','71','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm11-72','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,260,NULL,'Espeon & Deoxys-GX','72','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm11-73','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Six of them form a single Pokémon. Should one of the six be lost, the next morning there will once more be six.',50,NULL,'Exeggcute','73','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-74','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,3,'Exeggcute','It engages its enemies using psychic powers. Each of its three heads fires off psychokinetic energy, tripling its power.',140,NULL,'Exeggutor','74','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm11-75','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,2,'Cubone','The rich greenery of the Alola region is hard on Marowak. It controls fire to stay alive.',120,NULL,'Alolan Marowak','75','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm11-76','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It sways its hips to a rhythm all its own. The precise movements of Jynx living in Alola are truly wonderful.',80,NULL,'Jynx','76','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-77','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'It tends to move in a pack with others. They cluster in a tight group to sleep in a cave.',60,NULL,'Wynaut','77','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-78','Yoshinobu Saito',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,170,NULL,'Latios-GX','78','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm11-79','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,160,NULL,'Jirachi-GX','79','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm11-79a','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,160,NULL,'Jirachi-GX','79a','Rare Ultra','Pokémon'),('sm11-8','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,2,'Sewaddle','Forests where Swadloon live have superb foliage because the nutrients they make from fallen leaves nourish the plant life.',70,NULL,'Swadloon','8','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-80','ryoma uratsuka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its round body is stuffed with souls and expands each time it leads someone away.',70,NULL,'Drifloon','80','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-81','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,'Drifloon','There\'s a rumor that if you catch a Drifblim floating on the wind at dusk, you\'ll be carried away to the afterlife.',100,NULL,'Drifblim','81','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm11-82','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It grips prey with its tail claws and injects poison. It tenaciously hangs on until the poison takes.',70,NULL,'Skorupi','82','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-83','kodama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Known as \"The Being of Knowledge.\" It is said that it can wipe out the memory of those who see its eyes.',70,NULL,'Uxie','83','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm11-84','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Known as \"The Being of Emotion.\" It taught humans the nobility of sorrow, pain, and joy.',60,NULL,'Mesprit','84','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-85','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Known as \"The Being of Willpower.\" It sleeps at the bottom of a lake to keep the world in balance.',70,NULL,'Azelf','85','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-86','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is said to live in a world on the reverse side of ours, where common knowledge is distorted and strange.',130,NULL,'Giratina','86','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm11-87','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Shiny particles are released from its wings like a veil. It is said to represent the crescent moon.',130,NULL,'Cresselia','87','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-88','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon appears before people and Pokémon who are having nightmares and eats those dreams.',60,NULL,'Munna','88','Common','Pokémon'),('sm11-89','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,2,'Munna','The mist emanating from their foreheads is packed with the dreams of people and Pokémon.',100,NULL,'Musharna','89','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm11-9','K