cret','Energy'),('sm2-167',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Grass Energy','167','Rare Secret','Energy'),('sm2-168',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Lightning Energy','168','Rare Secret','Energy'),('sm2-169',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Fighting Energy','169','Rare Secret','Energy'),('sm2-17','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'The shell on its back is chemically unstable and explodes violently if struck. The hole in its stomach is its weak point.',110,NULL,'Turtonator','17','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-18','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,190,NULL,'Turtonator-GX','18','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-19','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It lives on snowy mountains. Its steel shell is very hard—so much so, it can\'t roll its body up into a ball.',60,NULL,'Alolan Sandshrew','19','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-19a','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It lives on snowy mountains. Its steel shell is very hard—so much so, it can\'t roll its body up into a ball.',60,NULL,'Alolan Sandshrew','19a','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-2','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,2,'Bellsprout','The leafy parts act as cutters for slashing foes. It spits a fluid that dissolves everything.',80,NULL,'Weepinbell','2','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-20','TOKIYA',NULL,NULL,2,'Alolan Sandshrew','Fleeing a volcanic eruption, it settled on a snowy mountain. As it races through the snowfields, it sends up a spray of snow.',110,NULL,'Alolan Sandslash','20','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-21','You Iribi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It exhales air colder than -58 degrees Fahrenheit. Elderly people in Alola call this Pokémon by an older name—Keokeo.',60,NULL,'Alolan Vulpix','21','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-21a','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It exhales air colder than -58 degrees Fahrenheit. Elderly people in Alola call this Pokémon by an older name—Keokeo.',60,NULL,'Alolan Vulpix','21a','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-22','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,'Alolan Vulpix',NULL,210,NULL,'Alolan Ninetales-GX','22','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-23','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They can be found lying dehydrated on beaches, but they are often still alive. When soaked in water, they will revive.',60,NULL,'Tentacool','23','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-24','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,2,'Tentacool','Normally, it has 80 poisonous tentacles. The longer one has been alive, the fewer tentacles it will have.',110,NULL,'Tentacruel','24','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-25','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,'Poliwhirl','They gather on moonlit nights to form a large chorus. Their cries sound angry and not at all pleasant, but they are certainly distinctive.',130,NULL,'Politoed','25','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-26','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Although it naturally prefers colder locales, Delibird in Alola seem able to withstand the heat to a certain extent.',90,NULL,'Delibird','26','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-27','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Each school has its own territory. Any intruders are mercilessly attacked with fangs bared.',50,NULL,'Carvanha','27','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-28','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Carvanha','It pursues its prey at speeds of 75 mph and finishes them off with fangs that can crush iron. It is known as the bully of the sea.',90,NULL,'Sharpedo','28','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-29','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It loves to startle people. It fills itself up with seawater and plays by bouncing around like a ball.',120,NULL,'Wailmer','29','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-3','TOKIYA',NULL,NULL,2,'Weepinbell','Said to live in huge colonies deep in jungles, although no one has ever returned from there.',140,NULL,'Victreebel','3','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-30','OOYAMA',NULL,NULL,4,'Wailmer','Wailord pursue their prey in pods. With their large mouths, they can swallow entire schools of Wishiwashi whole.',200,NULL,'Wailord','30','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-31','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Their numbers seem to have rapidly increased in Alola. Custom has it that houses where Snorunt live will be prosperous for generations to come.',60,NULL,'Snorunt','31','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-32','so-taro',NULL,NULL,3,'Snorunt','Legend says a boulder on an icy mountain absorbed the distress and regrets of a stranded mountaineer, giving rise to Glalie.',120,NULL,'Glalie','32','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-33','OOYAMA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Born of an icicle, this Pokémon uses its frosty breath to make ice crystals, causing snow to fall.',50,NULL,'Vanillite','33','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-34','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,2,'Vanillite','Hot days cause its body to melt. It can be restored by refreezing it, but the process leaves its body slightly warped.',80,NULL,'Vanillish','34','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-35','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,'Vanillish','Each of its two heads has a brain, and when they are in agreement, it attacks its enemies by exhaling a violent blizzard.',140,NULL,'Vanilluxe','35','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-36','Aya Kusube',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It uses its special mucus to close the wounds of injured Pokémon. The reason for this behavior remains unknown.',110,NULL,'Alomomola','36','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-37','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'When it\'s in trouble, its eyes moisten and begin to shine. The shining light attracts its comrades, and they stand together against their enemies.',30,NULL,'Wishiwashi','37','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-38','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,210,NULL,'Wishiwashi-GX','38','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-39','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It plunges the poison spike on its head into its prey. When the prey has weakened, Mareanie deals the finishing blow with its 10 tentacles.',60,NULL,'Mareanie','39','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-4','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Although the leaves on its head are bitter enough to cause dizziness, they provide relief from weariness—even more so when boiled.',50,NULL,'Petilil','4','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-40','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its body is a magnetic stone. Iron sand attaches firmly to the portions of its body that are particularly magnetic.',70,NULL,'Alolan Geodude','40','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-41','match',NULL,NULL,4,'Alolan Geodude','Its preferred food is dravite. After it has eaten this mineral, crystals form inside the Pokémon, rising to the surface of part of its body.',110,NULL,'Alolan Graveler','41','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-42','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,4,'Alolan Graveler','It fires rocks charged with electricity. Even if the rock isn\'t fired that accurately, just grazing an opponent will cause numbness and fainting.',160,NULL,'Alolan Golem','42','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-43','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They make their home in deserts. They can generate their energy from basking in the sun, so eating food is not a requirement.',60,NULL,'Helioptile','43','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-44','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,'Helioptile','They flare their frills and generate energy. A single Heliolisk can generate sufficient electricity to power a skyscraper.',100,NULL,'Heliolisk','44','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-45','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,'Charjabug',NULL,240,NULL,'Vikavolt-GX','45','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-46','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Oricorio has sipped bright yellow nectar. Its bright, cheerful dance melts the hearts of its enemies.',90,NULL,'Oricorio','46','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-47','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,170,NULL,'Tapu Koko-GX','47','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-48','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Its long tail often breaks off. It doesn\'t really feel any pain, though, and the tail grows back, so Slowpoke isn\'t particularly bothered.',70,NULL,'Slowpoke','48','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-49','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,3,'Slowpoke','It spaces out while gazing at the sea. With Shellder\'s poison flowing through its body, it becomes even spacier.',110,NULL,'Slowbro','49','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-5','You Iribi',NULL,NULL,1,'Petilil','No matter how much time and money is spent raising it, its flowers are the most beautiful when they bloom in the wild.',90,NULL,'Lilligant','5','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-50','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Unsanitary places are what they like best. They can be spotted in Alola, often with Grimer in hot pursuit.',70,NULL,'Trubbish','50','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-51','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,3,'Trubbish','Beware the poisonous liquid it shoots from its right arm. If even a little of it gets on you, you\'ll experience the effects of the unidentified toxin.',120,NULL,'Garbodor','51','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-51a','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,3,'Trubbish','Beware the poisonous liquid it shoots from its right arm. If even a little of it gets on you, you\'ll experience the effects of the unidentified toxin.',120,NULL,'Garbodor','51a','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-52','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Their ribbonlike feelers increase their psychic power. They are always staring at something.',60,NULL,'Gothita','52','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-53','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,'Gothita','Starlight is the source of their power. At night, they mark star positions by using psychic power to float stones.',80,NULL,'Gothorita','53','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-54','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,'Gothorita','Starry skies thousands of light-years away are visible in the space distorted by their intense psychic power.',140,NULL,'Gothitelle','54','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-55','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Oricorio relaxes by swaying gently. This increases its psychic energy, which it then fires at its enemies.',90,NULL,'Oricorio','55','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-56','TOKIYA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Oricorio has sipped purple nectar. Its elegant, attractive dance will send the minds and hearts of its enemies to another world.',90,NULL,'Oricorio','56','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-57','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Mareanie',NULL,210,NULL,'Toxapex-GX','57','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-58','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its actual appearance is unknown. A scholar who saw what was under its rag was overwhelmed by horror and died of the shock.',70,NULL,'Mimikyu','58','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-59','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Swinging its massive anchor, it can KO Wailord in a single blow. What appears to be green seaweed is actually its body.',120,NULL,'Dhelmise','59','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-6','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'These Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died in the forest. Their cries sound like eerie screams.',60,NULL,'Phantump','6','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-60','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,170,NULL,'Tapu Lele-GX','60','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-60a','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,170,NULL,'Tapu Lele-GX','60a','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-61','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Cosmoem','It is said to be a female evolution of Cosmog. When its third eye activates, away it flies to another world.',160,NULL,'Lunala','61','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-62','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It loves working out. As it gazes at its muscles, which continue to swell day by day, it becomes more and more dedicated to its training.',70,NULL,'Machop','62','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-63','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It loves working out. As it gazes at its muscles, which continue to swell day by day, it becomes more and more dedicated to its training.',60,NULL,'Machop','63','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-64','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,3,'Machop','As a result of its continual workouts, it has developed tremendous power. It uses that power to help people with their work.',100,NULL,'Machoke','64','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-65','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,3,'Machoke','It unleashes megaton-level punches that send opponents flying clear over the horizon.',160,NULL,'Machamp','65','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-66','Hajime Kusajima',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'To avoid attack, it mimics a tree. It will run off if splashed with water, which it hates.',100,NULL,'Sudowoodo','66','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-67','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It usually clings to cliffs. When it spots its prey, it spreads its wings and glides down to attack.',70,NULL,'Gligar','67','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-68','Yoshinobu Saito',NULL,NULL,1,'Gligar','It observes prey while hanging inverted from branches. When the chance presents itself, it swoops!',110,NULL,'Gliscor','68','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-69','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'The magnet in Nosepass\'s nose provides an unerring compass, making it an excellent partner for Trainers going on a journey.',80,NULL,'Nosepass','69','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-7','Hiroyuki Yamamoto',NULL,NULL,2,'Phantump','This Pokémon is said to devour anyone daring to ravage the forest. To the creatures dwelling in the forest, it offers great kindness.',120,NULL,'Trevenant','7','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-70','sui',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its two whiskers provide a sensitive radar. Even in muddy waters, it can detect its prey\'s location.',60,NULL,'Barboach','70','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-71','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,3,'Barboach','A glutton that devours anything that moves, it quietly lurks at the bottom of swamps, lying in wait for prey.',130,NULL,'Whiscash','71','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-72','TOKIYA',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It grows up imitating the behavior of Pangoro, which it looks up to as a leader.',60,NULL,'Pancham','72','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-73','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s considered to be a good Pokémon for beginners because of its friendliness, but its disposition grows rougher as it grows up.',60,NULL,'Rockruff','73','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-74','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Rockruff',NULL,200,NULL,'Lycanroc-GX','74','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-75','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The mud stuck to Mudbray\'s hooves enhances its grip and its powerful running gait.',80,NULL,'Mudbray','75','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-76','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,4,'Mudbray','It spits a mud that provides resistance to both wind and rain, so the walls of old houses were often coated with it.',140,NULL,'Mudsdale','76','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-77','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It eats dust in the atmosphere. The composition of the dust determines the color of its core.',70,NULL,'Minior','77','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-78','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They awaken at dusk and take wing in the twilight, leading to the expression, \"Get home before the Murkrow fly.\"',70,NULL,'Murkrow','78','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-79','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,1,'Murkrow','A single cry from this nocturnal Pokémon, and more than a hundred of its Murkrow cronies will assemble.',110,NULL,'Honchkrow','79','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-8','match',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon is a coward. As it desperately dashes off, the flailing of its many legs leaves a sparkling clean path in its wake.',70,NULL,'Wimpod','8','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-80','Aya Kusube',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s a fiend for gemstones, so it stalks Carbink. Unfortunately, Gabite almost always grabs them first.',60,NULL,'Sableye','80','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-81','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Long ago, superstitions were spread about it, saying it brought disaster. This fed a hatred of it, and it was driven deep into the mountains.',100,NULL,'Absol','81','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-82','kodama',NULL,NULL,3,'Pancham','It boasts superb physical strength. Those who wish to become Pangoro\'s Trainer have no choice but to converse with their fists.',130,NULL,'Pangoro','82','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-83','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its cells are all magnets. It uses magnetism to communicate with others of its kind.',60,NULL,'Beldum','83','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-84','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,3,'Beldum','When two Beldum link together, their psychic power is doubled. Their intelligence, however, remains unchanged.',90,NULL,'Metang','84','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-85','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Metang',NULL,250,NULL,'Metagross-GX','85','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-86','Yoshinobu Saito',NULL,NULL,4,'Nosepass','It radiates such a powerful magnetic field that nearby electrical appliances become unusable.',130,NULL,'Probopass','86','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-87','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Cosmoem','It is said to live in another world. The intense light it radiates from the surface of its body can make the darkest of nights light up like midday.',160,NULL,'Solgaleo','87','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm2-88','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its adorable behavior and appearance make it popular with men and women, young and old. Its numbers are few, however.',60,NULL,'Clefairy','88','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-89','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,'Clefairy','They don\'t like to reveal themselves in front of people. They live quietly in packs deep in the mountains.',100,NULL,'Clefable','89','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-9','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Wimpod','With a flashing slash of its giant sharp claws, it cleaves seawater—or even air—right in two.',130,NULL,'Golisopod','9','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-90','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When it finds others of its kind, they all stick together. When enough of them have collected, the mass resembles a cumulonimbus cloud.',50,NULL,'Cottonee','90','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-91','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Cottonee','It rides on the wind and slips into people\'s homes. After it has turned a room into a cotton-filled mess, it giggles to itself and takes off.',80,NULL,'Whimsicott','91','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-92','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Eevee',NULL,200,NULL,'Sylveon-GX','92','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-92a','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Eevee',NULL,200,NULL,'Sylveon-GX','92a','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm2-93','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It attaches flowers to its highly nutritious vine. This revitalizes the flowers, and they give off an aromatic scent.',70,NULL,'Comfey','93','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-94','Asako Ito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The weakest of all Dragon-type Pokémon, it\'s unable to breathe if its skin dries out, so it sticks to shady places.',50,NULL,'Goomy','94','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-95','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,3,'Goomy','It has trouble drawing a line between friends and food. It will calmly try to melt and eat even those it gets along well with.',70,NULL,'Sliggoo','95','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm2-96','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,3,'Sliggoo','An amazingly friendly Pokémon, but if left to itself, loneliness overcomes it, and it oozes gooey tears.',160,NULL,'Goodra','96','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-97','match',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It has a compassionate personality, but if it is angered, it will completely destroy its surroundings with its intense breath.',120,NULL,'Drampa','97','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm2-98','match',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It expresses its feelings by smacking its scales. Metallic sounds echo through the tall mountains where Jangmo-o lives.',60,NULL,'Jangmo-o','98','Common','Pokémon'),('sm2-99','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Jangmo-o','It leaps at its prey with a courageous shout. Its scaly punches tear its opponents to shreds.',90,NULL,'Hakamo-o','99','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm3-1','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When attacked by bird Pokémon, it resists by releasing a terrifically strong odor from its antennae, but it often becomes their prey.',50,NULL,'Caterpie','1','Common','Pokémon'),('sm3-10','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,'Ledyba','While it\'s believed that starlight provides it with energy, this Pokémon also loves to eat berries. In the daytime, it curls up in the grass to sleep.',90,NULL,'Ledian','10','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm3-100','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'This is Zygarde\'s form at times when it uses its overwhelming power to suppress those who endanger the ecosystem.',150,NULL,'Zygarde','100','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm3-101','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It lies around all day, becoming active near dusk. At night, it wanders the city in search of loose change.',60,NULL,'Meowth','101','Common','Pokémon'),('sm3-102','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,'Meowth','It has a violent temperament. It will attack anything that looks it in the eye. Its sharp claws inflict deep wounds.',90,NULL,'Persian','102','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm3-103','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Roughly 20 years ago, it was artificially created, utilizing the latest technology of the time.',60,NULL,'Porygon','103','Common','Pokémon'),('sm3-104','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,'Porygon','For the purposes of planetary development, Porygon was updated with the most cutting-edge technology available.',80,NULL,'Porygon2','104','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm3-105','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,2,'Porygon2','In order to create a more advanced Pokémon, an additional program was installed, but apparently it contained a defect that makes it move oddly.',130,NULL,'Porygon-Z','105','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm3-105a','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Porygon2','In order to create a more advanced Pokémon, an additional program was installed, but apparently it contained a defect that makes it move oddly.',130,NULL,'Porygon-Z','105a','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm3-106','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has a perfect sense of time. Whatever happens, it keeps rhythm by precisely tilting its head in time.',60,NULL,'Hoothoot','106','Common','Pokémon'),('sm3-107','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,'Hoothoot','Its eyes are specially adapted. They concentrate even faint light and enable it to see in the dark.',90,NULL,'Noctowl','107','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm3-108','TOKIYA',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'They charge wildly and headbutt everything. Their headbutts have enough destructive force to derail a train.',120,NULL,'Bouffalant','108','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm3-109','Yumi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They live in pitch black caves. Their enormous ears can emit ultrasonic waves of 200,000 hertz.',50,NULL,'Noibat','109','Common','Pokémon'),('sm3-11','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This powerful Pokémon thrusts its prized horn under its enemies\' bellies, then lifts and throws them.',110,NULL,'Heracross','11','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm3-110'