dancer, it strikes with whips that are densely lined with poison thorns.',100,NULL,'Roserade','5','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm5-50','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its body is composed of plasma. It is known to infiltrate electronic devices and wreak havoc.',70,NULL,'Rotom','50','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-51','Asako Ito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'If for some reason its body bursts, its soul spills out with a screaming sound.',60,NULL,'Drifloon','51','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-52','Yumi',NULL,NULL,1,'Drifloon','Even while under careful observation, large flocks of Drifblim flying at dusk will inexplicably disappear from view.',110,NULL,'Drifblim','52','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-53','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It was bound to a fissure in an Odd Keystone as punishment for misdeeds 500 years ago.',70,NULL,'Spiritomb','53','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-54','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It burrows under the sand to lie in wait for prey. Its tail claws can inject its prey with a savage poison.',80,NULL,'Skorupi','54','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-55','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,3,'Skorupi','It has the power in its clawed arms to make scrap of a car. The tips of its claws release poison.',130,NULL,'Drapion','55','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm5-56','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Inflating its poison sacs, it fills the area with an odd sound and hits flinching opponents with a poison jab.',60,NULL,'Croagunk','56','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-57','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,2,'Croagunk','Its knuckle claws secrete a toxin so vile that even a scratch could prove fatal.',100,NULL,'Toxicroak','57','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm5-58','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It was banished for its violence. It silently gazed upon the old world from the Distortion World.',160,NULL,'Giratina ◇','58','Rare Prism Star','Pokémon'),('sm5-59','chibi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Those who sleep holding Cresselia\'s feather are assured of joyful dreams. It is said to represent the crescent moon.',120,NULL,'Cresselia','59','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm5-6','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It undertakes photosynthesis with its body, making oxygen. The leaf on its head wilts if it is thirsty.',70,NULL,'Turtwig','6','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-60','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its body is gaseous and frail. It slowly grows as it collects dust from the atmosphere.',60,NULL,'Cosmog','60','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-61','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,3,'Cosmog','There\'s something accumulating around the black core within its hard shell. People think this Pokémon may come from another world.',90,NULL,'Cosmoem','61','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-62','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Said to live in another world, this Pokémon devours light, drawing the moonless dark veil of night over the brightness of day.',160,NULL,'Lunala ◇','62','Rare Prism Star','Pokémon'),('sm5-63','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,180,NULL,'Dawn Wings Necrozma-GX','63','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm5-64','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Unidentified Fossil','In rock layers where Cranidos fossils are found, the fossilized trunks of trees snapped in two are also often found.',90,NULL,'Cranidos','64','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-65','Yoshinobu Saito',NULL,NULL,2,'Cranidos','Records exist of a revived fossil that evolved into Rampardos. It proceeded to escape and then destroy a skyscraper with a headbutt.',150,NULL,'Rampardos','65','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm5-66','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s tough enough to run right through the night, and it\'s also a hard worker, but it\'s still just a youngster.',70,NULL,'Riolu','66','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-67','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,1,'Riolu','They can detect the species of a living being—and its emotions—from over half a mile away. They control auras and hunt their prey in packs.',110,NULL,'Lucario','67','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm5-68','Yumi',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It enshrouds itself with sand to protect itself from germs. It does not enjoy getting wet.',90,NULL,'Hippopotas','68','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-69','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,4,'Hippopotas','It blasts internally stored sand from ports on its body to create a towering twister for attack.',140,NULL,'Hippowdon','69','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm5-7','OOYAMA',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It undertakes photosynthesis with its body, making oxygen. The leaf on its head wilts if it is thirsty.',80,NULL,'Turtwig','7','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-70','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They battle with hard berries for weapons. Their techniques are passed from the boss to the group, generation upon generation.',110,NULL,'Passimian','70','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-71','match',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Seen as a symbol of bad luck, it\'s generally disliked. Yet it gives presents—objects that sparkle or shine—to Trainers it\'s close to.',70,NULL,'Murkrow','71','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-72','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,1,'Murkrow','If its Murkrow cronies fail to catch food for it, or if it feels they have betrayed it, it will hunt them down wherever they are and punish them.',110,NULL,'Honchkrow','72','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-73','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It uses its claws to poke holes in eggs so it can slurp out the insides. Breeders consider it a scourge and will drive it away or eradicate it.',70,NULL,'Sneasel','73','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-74','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,'Sneasel','They dwell in cold places. This Pokémon\'s main food source in Alola is Vulpix and Sandshrew, which they carefully divide among their group.',90,NULL,'Weavile','74','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm5-75','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It protects itself by spraying a noxious fluid from its rear. The stench lingers for 24 hours.',70,NULL,'Stunky','75','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-76','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,3,'Stunky','It sprays a stinky fluid from its tail. The fluid smells worse the longer it is allowed to fester.',120,NULL,'Skuntank','76','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-77','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It can lull people to sleep and make them dream. It is active during nights of the new moon.',160,NULL,'Darkrai ◇','77','Rare Prism Star','Pokémon'),('sm5-78','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its golden hairs function as sensors. It pokes them out of its burrow to monitor its surroundings.',50,NULL,'Alolan Diglett','78','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-79','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,1,'Alolan Diglett','These Pokémon are cherished in the Alola region, where they are thought to be feminine deities of the land incarnate.',60,NULL,'Alolan Dugtrio','79','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-8','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,4,'Turtwig','It knows where pure water wells up. It carries fellow Pokémon there on its back.',110,NULL,'Grotle','8','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-80','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It sends out electromagnetic waves, which let it float through the air. Touching it while it\'s eating electricity will give you a full-body shock.',60,NULL,'Magnemite','80','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-81','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It sends out electromagnetic waves, which let it float through the air. Touching it while it\'s eating electricity will give you a full-body shock.',60,NULL,'Magnemite','81','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-82','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,2,'Magnemite','It has about three times the electrical power of Magnemite. For some reason, outbreaks of this Pokémon happen when lots of sunspots appear.',90,NULL,'Magneton','82','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-83','Yoshinobu Saito',NULL,NULL,2,'Magneton','As it zooms through the sky, this Pokémon seems to be receiving signals of unknown origin, while transmitting signals of unknown purpose.',150,NULL,'Magnezone','83','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm5-84','so-taro',NULL,NULL,2,'Unidentified Fossil','This Pokémon lived in primeval jungles. Few enemies would have been willing to square off against its heavily armored face, so it\'s thought.',100,NULL,'Shieldon','84','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-85','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,3,'Shieldon','It lived in the same environments as Rampardos. Their fossils have been found together—seemingly from after they\'d fought to the finish.',160,NULL,'Bastiodon','85','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm5-86','Sumiyoshi Kizuki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Implements shaped like it were discovered in ancient tombs. It is unknown if they are related.',60,NULL,'Bronzor','86','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-87','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,3,'Bronzor','Ancient people believed that petitioning Bronzong for rain was the way to make crops grow.',110,NULL,'Bronzong','87','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-88','tetsuya koizumi',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Boiling blood, like magma, circulates through its body. It makes its dwelling place in volcanic caves.',130,NULL,'Heatran','88','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm5-89','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'This Pokémon is said to be a male evolution of Cosmog. At the activation of its third eye, it departs for another world.',160,NULL,'Solgaleo ◇','89','Rare Prism Star','Pokémon'),('sm5-9','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,4,'Grotle','Small Pokémon occasionally gather on its unmoving back to begin building their nests.',180,NULL,'Torterra','9','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm5-90','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,190,NULL,'Dusk Mane Necrozma-GX','90','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm5-91','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This artificial Pokémon, constructed more than 500 years ago, can understand human speech but cannot itself speak.',90,NULL,'Magearna','91','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm5-92','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It scatters spores that flicker and glow. Anyone seeing these lights falls into a deep slumber.',60,NULL,'Morelull','92','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-93','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,'Morelull','Forests where Shiinotic live are treacherous to enter at night. People confused by its strange lights can never find their way home again.',100,NULL,'Shiinotic','93','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm5-94','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This guardian deity of Akala is guilelessly cruel. The fragrant aroma of flowers is the source of its energy.',110,NULL,'Tapu Lele','94','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm5-95','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,3,'Exeggcute','Alola is the best environment for this Pokémon. Local people take pride in its appearance, saying this is how Exeggutor ought to look.',130,NULL,'Alolan Exeggutor','95','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm5-96','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It skulks in caves, and when prey or an enemy passes by, it leaps out and chomps them. The force of its attack sometimes chips its teeth.',50,NULL,'Gible','96','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-97','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It skulks in caves, and when prey or an enemy passes by, it leaps out and chomps them. The force of its attack sometimes chips its teeth.',60,NULL,'Gible','97','Common','Pokémon'),('sm5-98','Sumiyoshi Kizuki',NULL,NULL,1,'Gible','Shiny objects are its passion. It can be found in its cave, scarcely moving, its gaze fixed on the jewels it\'s amassed or Carbink it has caught.',80,NULL,'Gabite','98','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm5-99','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Gabite','The protuberances on its head serve as sensors. It can even detect distant prey.',150,NULL,'Garchomp','99','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm6-1','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Six of them together form a full-fledged Pokémon. It\'s often hunted by Crabrawler, but uses psychokinesis to drive it off.',40,NULL,'Exeggcute','1','Common','Pokémon'),('sm6-10','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,'Skiddo','They inhabit mountainous regions. The leader of the herd is decided by a battle of clashing horns.',120,NULL,'Gogoat','10','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm6-100','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Even a robust wrestler will become dizzy and unable to stand when exposed to its 200,000-hertz ultrasonic waves.',50,NULL,'Noibat','100','Common','Pokémon'),('sm6-101','You Iribi',NULL,NULL,1,'Noibat','The ultrasonic waves it emits from its ears can reduce a large boulder to pebbles. It swoops out of the dark to attack.',120,NULL,'Noivern','101','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm6-102','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Beast Ring','10