,'Blastoise','25','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-26','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Using psychokinesis gives it a headache, so it normally passes the time spacing out and doing as little as possible.',60,NULL,'Psyduck','26','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-27','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,'Psyduck','Even fast-swimming fish Pokémon can be disabled by Golduck. It brings them to a standstill and seizes them.',110,NULL,'Golduck','27','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-28','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'In many places, there are folktales of stardust falling into the ocean and becoming Staryu.',50,NULL,'Staryu','28','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-29','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'In the distant past, they were fairly strong, but they have become gradually weaker over time.',30,NULL,'Magikarp','29','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-3','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Often found in forests and grasslands. It has a sharp, toxic barb of around two inches on top of its head.',50,NULL,'Weedle','3','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-30','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,4,'Magikarp','It fires hyper beams in all directions, burning the surrounding area to ash. There are some regions where it\'s called \"the deity of destruction.\"',150,NULL,'Gyarados','30','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-31','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It likes swimming around with people on its back. In the Alola region, it\'s an important means of transportation over water.',130,NULL,'Lapras','31','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-32','Yusuke Ohmura',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'A legendary bird Pokémon. It can create blizzards by freezing moisture in the air.',110,NULL,'Articuno','32','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-33','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,240,NULL,'Pikachu & Zekrom-GX','33','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm9-34','Yukiko Baba',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'If you mistake it for a rock and step on it, it will headbutt you in anger. In addition to the pain, it will also zap you with a shock.',60,NULL,'Alolan Geodude','34','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-35','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'If you mistake it for a rock and step on it, it will headbutt you in anger. In addition to the pain, it will also zap you with a shock.',70,NULL,'Alolan Geodude','35','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-36','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,4,'Alolan Geodude','When two Graveler fight each other, it fills the surroundings with flashes of light and sound. People call it the \"fireworks of the earth.\"',100,NULL,'Alolan Graveler','36','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-37','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,4,'Alolan Graveler','It\'s grumpy and stubborn. If you upset it, it discharges electricity from the surface of its body and growls with a voice like thunder.',180,NULL,'Alolan Golem','37','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-38','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It was discovered when Poké Balls were introduced. It is said that there is some connection.',50,NULL,'Voltorb','38','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-39','Asako Ito',NULL,NULL,1,'Voltorb','It explodes in response to even minor stimuli. It is feared, with the nickname of \"The Bomb Ball.\"',90,NULL,'Electrode','39','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-4','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,3,'Weedle','Almost incapable of moving, this Pokémon can only harden its shell to protect itself when it is in danger.',80,NULL,'Kakuna','4','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-40','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'A legendary Pokémon that is said to live in thunderclouds. It freely controls lightning bolts.',110,NULL,'Zapdos','40','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-41','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It stores lots of air in its soft fur, allowing it to stay cool in summer and warm in winter.',60,NULL,'Mareep','41','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-42','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,2,'Mareep','If its coat becomes fully charged with electricity, its tail lights up. It fires hair that zaps on impact.',90,NULL,'Flaaffy','42','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-43','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Flaaffy',NULL,240,NULL,'Ampharos-GX','43','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm9-44','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its mane shines when it discharges electricity. They use the frequency and rhythm of these flashes to communicate.',60,NULL,'Blitzle','44','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-45','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,'Blitzle','They have lightning-like movements. When Zebstrika run at full speed, the sound of thunder reverberates.',120,NULL,'Zebstrika','45','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-46','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'It grills berries and bug Pokémon with electric shocks and makes a meal of them. It usually nests in the holes gouged in trees by Pikipek.',60,NULL,'Emolga','46','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-47','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They attach themselves to large-bodied Pokémon and absorb static electricity, which they store in an electric pouch.',40,NULL,'Joltik','47','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-48','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,1,'Joltik','When attacked, they create an electric barrier by spitting out many electrically charged threads.',90,NULL,'Galvantula','48','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-49','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The frills on either side of its head have cells that generate electricity when exposed to sunlight.',60,NULL,'Helioptile','49','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-5','You Iribi',NULL,NULL,1,'Kakuna','It has three poisonous stingers on its forelegs and its tail. They are used to jab its enemy repeatedly.',130,NULL,'Beedrill','5','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-50','Sumiyoshi Kizuki',NULL,NULL,1,'Helioptile','It stimulates its muscles with electricity, boosting the strength in its legs and enabling it to run 100 yards in five seconds.',100,NULL,'Heliolisk','50','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-51','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It confuses its enemies by flying too quickly for the eye to follow. It has a hair-trigger temper but forgets what made it angry an instant later.',130,NULL,'Tapu Koko ◇','51','Rare Prism Star','Pokémon'),('sm9-52','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It electrifies its claws and tears its opponents apart with them. Even if they dodge its attack, they\'ll be electrocuted by the flying sparks.',120,NULL,'Zeraora','52','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-53','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,240,NULL,'Gengar & Mimikyu-GX','53','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm9-54','miki kudo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Although small, its venomous barbs render this Pokémon dangerous. The female has smaller horns.',60,NULL,'Nidoran ♀','54','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-55','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Nidoran ♀','The female has a gentle temperament. It emits ultrasonic cries that have the power to befuddle foes.',90,NULL,'Nidorina','55','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-56','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,3,'Nidorina','It uses its scaly, rugged body to seal the entrance of its nest and protect its young from predators.',160,NULL,'Nidoqueen','56','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-57','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It scans its surroundings by raising its ears out of the grass. Its toxic horn is for protection.',60,NULL,'Nidoran ♂','57','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-58','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Nidoran ♂','It raises its big ears to check its surroundings. If it senses anything, it attacks immediately.',90,NULL,'Nidorino','58','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-59','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,3,'Nidorino','It is recognized by its rock-hard hide and its extended horn. Be careful with the horn, as it contains venom.',160,NULL,'Nidoking','59','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-6','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Whether it\'s due to a lack of moisture or a lack of nutrients, in Alola the mushrooms on Paras don\'t grow up quite right.',70,NULL,'Paras','6','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-60','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It drifts through the sea searching for prey. Its poisonous tentacles break off sometimes, but after a while, they grow back.',60,NULL,'Tentacool','60','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-61','kodama',NULL,NULL,1,'Tentacool','It fires off ultrasonic waves from its red orbs to weaken its prey, and then it wraps them up in its 80 tentacles.',100,NULL,'Tentacruel','61','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-62','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It was born from sludge on the ocean floor. In a sterile environment, the germs within its body can\'t multiply, and it dies.',80,NULL,'Grimer','62','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-63','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,4,'Grimer','Their food sources have decreased, and their numbers have declined sharply. Sludge ponds are being built to prevent their extinction.',130,NULL,'Muk','63','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-64','miki kudo',NULL,NULL,2,'Cubone','Its custom is to mourn its lost companions. Mounds of dirt by the side of the road mark the graves of the Marowak.',120,NULL,'Alolan Marowak','64','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-65','Mizue',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Staryu','Its sparkling core is called \"the gem of the sea.\" This core can be made into high-priced accessories that are traded in secret.',80,NULL,'Starmie','65','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-66','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its pantomime skills are wonderful. You may become enraptured while watching it, but next thing you know, Mr. Mime has made a real wall.',80,NULL,'Mr. Mime','66','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-67','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,150,NULL,'Mr. Mime-GX','67','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm9-68','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It sways its hips to a rhythm all its own. The precise movements of Jynx living in Alola are truly wonderful.',90,NULL,'Jynx','68','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-69','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'In ages past, it was called the child of the stars. It\'s said to be a Pokémon from another world, but no specific details are known.',50,NULL,'Cosmog','69','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-7','Satoshi Shirai',NULL,NULL,2,'Paras','The bug is mostly dead, with the mushroom on its back having become the main body. If the mushroom comes off, the bug stops moving.',100,NULL,'Parasect','7','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-70','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,3,'Cosmog','There\'s something accumulating around the black core within its hard shell. People think this Pokémon may come from another world.',100,NULL,'Cosmoem','70','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-71','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The smallest of things could cause it to lose its temper. Because it doesn\'t hold in its stress, this Pokémon can live a long time.',50,NULL,'Mankey','71','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-72','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,'Mankey','It will never forgive opponents who have angered it. Even after it has beaten them down until they can\'t move, it never ever forgives.',90,NULL,'Primeape','72','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-73','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The legs freely contract and stretch. The stretchy legs allow it to hit a distant foe with a rising kick.',100,NULL,'Hitmonlee','73','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-74','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The arm-twisting punches it throws pulverize even concrete. It rests after three minutes of fighting.',90,NULL,'Hitmonchan','74','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-75','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,'Unidentified Fossil','Omanyte lived in the seas of antiquity. Its fossils have been found bearing bite marks from Archeops, so apparently Archeops preyed on it.',90,NULL,'Omanyte','75','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-76','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,2,'Omanyte','Its heavy shell is thought to be the reason this ancient Pokémon died out. It\'s apparently a distant ancestor of Octillery.',130,NULL,'Omastar','76','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-77','sui',NULL,NULL,1,'Unidentified Fossil','This Pokémon thrived 300 million years ago. It\'s said that living specimens can still be seen in a certain region—a rare sight.',90,NULL,'Kabuto','77','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-78','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Kabuto','Its body had begun to change so it could function on land. But it didn\'t adapt in time and went extinct.',140,NULL,'Kabutops','78','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-79','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Born deep underground, it comes aboveground and becomes a pupa once it has finished eating the surrounding soil.',70,NULL,'Larvitar','79','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-8','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Six of them form a single Pokémon. Should one of the six be lost, the next morning there will once more be six.',50,NULL,'Exeggcute','8','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-80','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,'Larvitar','Its shell is as hard as sheet rock, and it is also very strong. Its thrashing can topple a mountain.',80,NULL,'Pupitar','80','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-81','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'There\'s no point to the leaf in its mouth, aside from an effort to look cool. It\'s mischievous, so it\'s not well suited to inexperienced Trainers.',60,NULL,'Pancham','81','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-82','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Rockruff',NULL,200,NULL,'Lycanroc-GX','82','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm9-83','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'The crystals on Grimer\'s body are lumps of toxins. If one falls off, lethal poisons leak out.',70,NULL,'Alolan Grimer','83','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-84','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,3,'Alolan Grimer','While it\'s unexpectedly quiet and friendly, if it\'s not fed any trash for a while, it will smash its Trainer\'s furnishings and eat up the fragments.',120,NULL,'Alolan Muk','84','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-85','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,4,'Pupitar','If it rampages, it knocks down mountains and buries rivers. Maps must be redrawn afterward.',170,NULL,'Tyranitar','85','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-86','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has a very tenacious nature. Its acute sense of smell lets it chase a chosen prey without ever losing track.',70,NULL,'Poochyena','86','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-87','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,'Poochyena','It chases down prey in a pack of around ten. They defeat foes with perfectly coordinated teamwork.',100,NULL,'Mightyena','87','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-88','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Although it\'s said to bring disaster, in actuality, this Pokémon possesses a calm disposition and warns people of any crises that loom.',100,NULL,'Absol','88','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-89','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It was bound to a fissure in an odd keystone as punishment for misdeeds 500 years ago',70,NULL,'Spiritomb','89','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sm9-9','Eri Yamaki',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It gets into territorial disputes with Vikavolt. For some reason, it apparently gets along well with Heracross in Alola.',120,NULL,'Pinsir','9','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-90','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'To protect themselves from danger, they hide their true identities by transforming into people and Pokémon.',60,NULL,'Zorua','90','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-91','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,2,'Zorua','Bonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents.',110,NULL,'Zoroark','91','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-92','Eri Yamaki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It can\'t fly yet and must wait until its wings have developed more. Since it\'s still at a playful age, it hops around friskily.',60,NULL,'Vullaby','92','Common','Pokémon'),('sm9-93','Ayaka Yoshida',NULL,NULL,2,'Vullaby','It circles in the sky, keeping a keen eye out for Pokémon in a weakened state. Its choicest food is Cubone.',120,NULL,'Mandibuzz','93','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-94','Satoshi Shirai',NULL,NULL,4,'Pancham','From the slight twitches of its bamboo leaf, it deduces its opponent\'s movements. It\'s eager to tussle but kindhearted toward its companions.',140,NULL,'Pangoro','94','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-95','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'When its life comes to an end, it absorbs the life energy of every living thing and turns into a cocoon once more.',110,NULL,'Yveltal','95','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sm9-96','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,190,NULL,'Hoopa-GX','96','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm9-97','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Torracat',NULL,250,NULL,'Incineroar-GX','97','Rare Holo GX','Pokémon'),('sm9-98','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its metal body is sturdy, but it does rust rather easily. So on rainy days, this Pokémon prefers to stay put in its nest.',110,NULL,'Skarmory','98','Rare','Pokémon'),('sm9-99','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is said to have the ability to grant any wish for just one week every thousand years.',70,NULL,'Jirachi','99','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('sma-SV1','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'While young, they live together deep in the mountains, training themselves in how to fight with their scythes and move at high speeds.',70,NULL,'Scyther','SV1','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV10','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,2,'Wooper','This carefree Pokémon has an easygoing nature. While swimming, it always bumps into boat hulls.',120,NULL,'Quagsire','SV10','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV11','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It protects its skin by covering its body in delicate bubbles. Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it keeps a watchful eye on its surroundings.',50,NULL,'Froakie','SV11','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV12','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,'Froakie','Its swiftness is unparalleled. It can scale a tower of more than 2,000 feet in a minute\'s time.',80,NULL,'Frogadier','SV12','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV13','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Usually found in power plants. Easily mistaken for a Poké Ball, it has zapped many people.',50,NULL,'Voltorb','SV13','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV14','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole. It raided a power plant, so people think it energizes itself with electricity.',120,NULL,'Xurkitree','SV14','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV15','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'In battle, it uses its bladed tail to counter any Zangoose. It secretes a deadly venom in its tail.',100,NULL,'Seviper','SV15','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV16','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It loves vengeful emotions and hangs in rows under the eaves of houses where vengeful people live.',60,NULL,'Shuppet','SV16','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV17','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It flashes the light-emitting spots on its body, which drains its opponent\'s will to fight. It takes the opportunity to scuttle away and hide.',60,NULL,'Inkay','SV17','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV18','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Inkay','It lures prey close with hypnotic motions, then wraps its tentacles around it before finishing it off with digestive fluids.',90,NULL,'Malamar','SV18','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV19','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Ultra Beast is well enough liked to be chosen as a first partner in its own world.',70,NULL,'Poipole','SV19','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV2','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This wary Pokémon uses photosynthesis to store up energy during the day, while becoming active at night.',60,NULL,'Rowlet','SV2','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV20','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'To avoid attack, it mimics a tree. It will run off if splashed with water, which it hates.',100,NULL,'Sudowoodo','SV20','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV21','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s tough enough to run right through the night, and it\'s also a hard worker, but it\'s still just a youngster.',70,NULL,'Riolu','SV21','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV22','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Riolu','They can detect the species of a living being—and its emotions—from over half a mile away. They control auras and hunt their prey in packs.',110,NULL,'Lucario','SV22','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV23','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon has lived with people since times long ago. It can sense when its Trainer is in the dumps and will stick close by its Trainer\'s side.',70,NULL,'Rockruff','SV23','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV24','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'A mysterious life-form called an Ultra Beast. Witnesses saw it pulverize a dump truck with a single punch.',130,NULL,'Buzzwole','SV24','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV25','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It changes so it looks like its foe, tricks it, and then uses that opportunity to flee.',60,NULL,'Zorua','SV25','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV26','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'A dangerous Ultra Beast, it appears to be eating constantly, but for some reason its droppings have never been found.',160,NULL,'Guzzlord','SV26','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV27','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It sends out electromagnetic waves, which let it float through the air. Touching it while it\'s eating electricity will give you a full-body shock.',60,NULL,'Magnemite','SV27','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV28','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,2,'Magnemite','It has about three times the electrical power of Magnemite. For some reason, outbreaks of this Pokémon happen when lots of sunspots appear.',90,NULL,'Magneton','SV28','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV29','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,2,'Magneton','As it zooms through the sky, this Pokémon seems to be receiving signals of unknown origin, while transmitting signals of unknown purpose.',150,NULL,'Magnezone','SV29','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV3','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,'Rowlet','A bit of a dandy, it spends its free time preening its wings. Its preoccupation with any dirt on its plumage can leave it unable to battle.',80,NULL,'Dartrix','SV3','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV30','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its cells are all magnets. It uses magnetism to communicate with others of its kind.',60,NULL,'Beldum','SV30','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV31','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,3,'Beldum','When two Beldum link together, their psychic power is doubled. Their intelligence, however, remains unchanged.',90,NULL,'Metang','SV31','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV32','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'One kind of Ultra Beast. Witnesses have seen it burn down a forest by expelling gas from its two arms.',140,NULL,'Celesteela','SV32','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV33','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'One of the Ultra Beast life-forms, it was observed cutting down a gigantic steel tower with one stroke of its blade.',60,NULL,'Kartana','SV33','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV34','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'If its horns capture the warm feelings of people or Pokémon, its body warms up slightly.',60,NULL,'Ralts','SV34','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV35','Sumiyoshi Kizuki',NULL,NULL,1,'Ralts','The cheerful spirit of its Trainer gives it energy for its psychokinetic power. It spins and dances when happy.',80,NULL,'Kirlia','SV35','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV36','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A sudden transformation of Carbink, its pink, glimmering body is said to be the loveliest sight in the whole world.',90,NULL,'Diancie','SV36','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV37','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,'Swablu','On sunny days, it flies freely through the sky and blends into the clouds. It sings in a beautiful soprano.',80,NULL,'Altaria','SV37','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV38','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It skulks in caves, and when prey or an enemy passes by, it leaps out and chomps them. The force of its attack sometimes chips its teeth.',50,NULL,'Gible','SV38','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV39','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,'Gible','Shiny objects are its passion. It can be found in its cave, scarcely moving, its gaze fixed on the jewels it\'s amassed or Carbink it has caught.',80,NULL,'Gabite','SV39','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV4','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'This Pokémon is a coward. As it desperately dashes off, the flailing of its many legs leaves a sparkling clean path in its wake.',70,NULL,'Wimpod','SV4','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV40','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Gabite','The protuberances on its head serve as sensors. It can even detect distant prey.',150,NULL,'Garchomp','SV40','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV41','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Current studies show it can evolve into an incredible eight different species of Pokémon.',60,NULL,'Eevee','SV41','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV42','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It constantly grooms its cotton-like wings. It takes a shower to clean itself if it becomes dirty.',50,NULL,'Swablu','SV42','Rare Shiny','Pokémon'),('sma-SV43','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They live in pitch black caves