hics',NULL,NULL,3,'Growlithe','It\'s very friendly and faithful to people. It will try to repel enemies by barking and biting.',280,'G','Arcanine ex','32','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-33','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It uses different kinds of cries for communicating with others of its kind and for pursuing its prey.',70,'G','Houndour','33','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-34','hncl',NULL,NULL,2,'Houndour','Upon hearing its eerie howls, other Pokémon get the shivers and head straight back to their nests.',120,'G','Houndoom','34','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-35','Kurata So',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It burns coal inside its shell for energy. It blows out black soot if it is endangered.',130,'G','Torkoal','35','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-36','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its flame sac is small, so energy is always leaking out. This energy is released from the dent atop Fuecoco\'s head and flickers to and fro.',80,'G','Fuecoco','36','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-37','kantaro',NULL,NULL,3,'Fuecoco','The valve in Crocalor\'s flame sac is closely connected to its vocal cords. This Pokémon utters a guttural cry as it spews flames every which way.',100,'G','Crocalor','37','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-38','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,3,'Crocalor','Skeledirge\'s gentle singing soothes the souls of all that hear it. It burns its enemies to a crisp with flames of over 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit.',180,'G','Skeledirge','38','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-39','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Burnt charcoal came to life and became a Pokémon. Possessing a fiery fighting spirit, Charcadet will battle even tough opponents.',60,'G','Charcadet','39','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-4','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,1,'Shroomish','It scatters poisonous spores and throws powerful punches while its foe is hampered by inhaled spores.',110,'G','Breloom','4','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-40','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Burnt charcoal came to life and became a Pokémon. Possessing a fiery fighting spirit, Charcadet will battle even tough opponents.',70,'G','Charcadet','40','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-41','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,2,'Charcadet','Armarouge evolved through the use of a set of armor that belonged to a distinguished warrior. This Pokémon is incredibly loyal.',130,'G','Armarouge','41','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-42','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It is always vacantly lost in thought, but no one knows what it is thinking about. It is good at fishing with its tail.',70,'G','Slowpoke','42','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-43','Shinji Kanda',NULL,NULL,3,'Slowpoke','If the tail-biting Shellder is thrown off in a harsh battle, this Pokémon reverts to being an ordinary Slowpoke.',100,'G','Slowbro','43','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-44','KIYOTAKA OSHIYAMA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'An underpowered, pathetic Pokémon. It may jump high on rare occasions but never more than seven feet.',30,'G','Magikarp','44','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-45','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,4,'Magikarp','An underpowered, pathetic Pokémon. It may jump high on rare occasions but never more than seven feet.',300,'G','Gyarados ex','45','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-46','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It spins its two tails like a screw to propel itself through water. The tails also slice clinging seaweed.',70,'G','Buizel','46','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-47','Gemi',NULL,NULL,1,'Buizel','With its flotation sac inflated, it can carry people on its back. It deflates the sac before it dives.',120,'G','Floatzel','47','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-48','Shinji Kanda',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It gently holds injured and weak Pokémon in its fins. Its special membrane heals their wounds.',120,'G','Alomomola','48','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-49','miki kudo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Clauncher\'s claws will regrow if they fall off. The meat inside the claws is edible, but it has a distinct flavor that doesn\'t appeal to all tastes.',70,'G','Clauncher','49','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-5','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It prefers harsh environments, such as deserts. It can survive for 30 days on water stored in its body.',60,'G','Cacnea','5','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-50','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,'Clauncher','The cannonballs of seawater that Clawitzer launches from its claw are powerful enough to punch through tanker hulls.',120,'G','Clawitzer','50','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-51','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It grinds its teeth with great force to stimulate its brain. It fires the psychic energy created by this process from the protuberance on its head.',100,'G','Bruxish','51','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-52','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon migrated to Paldea from distant lands long ago. The gel secreted by its feathers repels water and grime.',70,'G','Quaxly','52','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-53','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,'Quaxly','These Pokémon constantly run through shallow waters to train their legs, then compete with each other to see which of them kicks most gracefully.',100,'G','Quaxwell','53','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-54','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Quaxwell','A single kick from a Quaquaval can send a truck rolling. This Pokémon uses its powerful legs to perform striking dances from far-off lands.',170,'G','Quaquaval','54','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-55','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand.',50,'G','Wiglett','55','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-56','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand.',60,'G','Wiglett','56','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-57','KIYOTAKA OSHIYAMA',NULL,NULL,2,'Wiglett','It has a vicious temperament, contrary to what its appearance may suggest. It wraps its long bodies around prey, then drags the prey into its den.',90,'G','Wugtrio','57','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-58','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It lives in frigid regions in pods of five or so individuals. It loves the minerals found in snow and ice.',80,'G','Cetoddle','58','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-59','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It lives in frigid regions in pods of five or so individuals. It loves the minerals found in snow and ice.',100,'G','Cetoddle','59','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-6','DOM',NULL,NULL,2,'Cacnea','Packs of them follow travelers through the desert until the travelers can no longer move.',130,'G','Cacturne','6','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-60','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,3,'Cetoddle','Ice energy builds up in the horn on its upper jaw, causing the horn to reach cryogenic temperatures that freeze its surroundings.',180,'G','Cetitan','60','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-61','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'This Pokémon is a glutton, but it\'s bad at getting food. It teams up with a Tatsugiri to catch prey.',160,'G','Dondozo','61','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-62','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This is a small dragon Pokémon. It lives inside the mouth of Dondozo to protect itself from enemies on the outside.',70,'G','Tatsugiri','62','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-63','KIYOTAKA OSHIYAMA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It moves while constantly hovering. It discharges electromagnetic waves and so on from the units at its sides.',60,'G','Magnemite','63','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-64','Shiburingaru',NULL,NULL,2,'Magnemite','They\'re formed by several Magnemite linked together. They frequently appear when sunspots flare up.',90,'G','Magneton','64','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-65','hncl',NULL,NULL,3,'Magneton','They\'re formed by several Magnemite linked together. They frequently appear when sunspots flare up.',330,'G','Magnezone ex','65','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-66','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its fleece grows continually. In the summer, the fleece is fully shed, but it grows back in a week.',60,'G','Mareep','66','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-67','Kurata So',NULL,NULL,2,'Mareep','Because of its rubbery, electricity-resistant skin, it can store lots of electricity in its fur.',90,'G','Flaaffy','67','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-68','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A pair may be seen rubbing their cheek pouches together in an effort to share stored electricity.',70,'G','Pachirisu','68','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-69','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Research continues on this Pokémon, which could be the power source of a unique motor.',60,'G','Rotom','69','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-7','aoki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It lives in tropical jungles. The bunch of fruit around its neck is delicious. The fruit grows twice a year.',100,'G','Tropius','7','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-70','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Research continues on this Pokémon, which could be the power source of a unique motor.',80,'G','Rotom','70','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-71','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This selfish, attention-seeking Pokémon stores poison and electricity in two different sacs inside its body.',70,'G','Toxel','71','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-72','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Toxel','The jolts of electricity it launches by violently strumming the protrusions on its chest easily exceed 15,000 volts.',130,'G','Toxtricity','72','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-73','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The pads of its paws are electricity-discharging organs. Pawmi fires electricity from its forepaws while standing unsteadily on its hind legs.',50,'G','Pawmi','73','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-74','kantaro',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The pads of its paws are electricity-discharging organs. Pawmi fires electricity from its forepaws while standing unsteadily on its hind legs.',60,'G','Pawmi','74','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-75','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,'Pawmi','Pawmo uses a unique fighting technique in which it uses its forepaws to strike foes and zap them with electricity from its paw pads simultaneously.',90,'G','Pawmo','75','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-76','Mizue',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Pawmo','Pawmot\'s fluffy fur acts as a battery. It can store the same amount of electricity as an electric car.',130,'G','Pawmot','76','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-77','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When its wings catch the wind, the bones within produce electricity. This Pokémon dives into the ocean, catching prey by electrocuting them.',50,'G','Wattrel','77','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-78','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When its wings catch the wind, the bones within produce electricity. This Pokémon dives into the ocean, catching prey by electrocuting them.',60,'G','Wattrel','78','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-79','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Wattrel','Kilowattrel inflates its throat sac to amplify its electricity. By riding the wind, this Pokémon can fly over 430 miles in a day.',120,'G','Kilowattrel','79','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-8','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon scatters poisonous powder to repel enemies. It will eat different plants depending on where it lives.',30,'G','Scatterbug','8','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-80','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Much remains unknown about this creature. It resembles Cyclizar, but it is far more ruthless and powerful.',120,'G','Miraidon','80','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-81','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Much remains unknown about this creature. It resembles Cyclizar, but it is far more ruthless and powerful.',220,'G','Miraidon ex','81','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-82','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When it twitches its nose, it can tell where someone is sleeping and what that person is dreaming about.',70,'G','Drowzee','82','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-83','Toshinao Aoki',NULL,NULL,2,'Drowzee','Always holding a pendulum that it swings at a steady rhythm, it causes drowsiness in anyone nearby.',110,'G','Hypno','83','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-84','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The horns on its head provide a strong power that enables it to sense people\'s emotions.',70,'G','Ralts','84','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-85','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,'Ralts','It has a psychic power that enables it to distort the space around it and see into the future.',90,'G','Kirlia','85','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-86','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,2,'Kirlia','It has a psychic power that enables it to distort the space around it and see into the future.',310,'G','Gardevoir ex','86','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-87','Jerky',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It feeds on the dark emotions of sadness and hatred, which make it grow steadily stronger.',60,'G','Shuppet','87','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-88','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,2,'Shuppet','It feeds on the dark emotions of sadness and hatred, which make it grow steadily stronger.',250,'G','Banette ex','88','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-89','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is whispered that any child who mistakes Drifloon for a balloon and holds on to it could wind up missing.',70,'G','Drifloon','89','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-9','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,3,'Scatterbug','Spewpa doesn\'t live in a fixed location. It roams where it pleases across the fields and mountains, building up the energy it needs to evolve.',70,'G','Spewpa','9','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-90','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,'Drifloon','It can generate and release gas within its body. That\'s how it can control the altitude of its drift.',110,'G','Drifblim','90','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-91','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Flabébé rides a red flower. Immediately after birth, this Pokémon begins flying around in search of a flower it likes.',40,'G','Flabébé','91','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-92','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,'Flabébé','This Pokémon uses red wavelengths of light to pour its own energy into flowers and draw forth their latent potential.',70,'G','Floette','92','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-93','Haru Akasaka',NULL,NULL,2,'Floette','They say that flower gardens created by Florges are constantly showered with a power that can heal both body and spirit.',140,'G','Florges','93','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv1-94','zig',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s small and its electricity-generating organ is not fully developed, so it uses its tail to absorb electricity from people\'s homes and charge itself.',70,'G','Dedenne','94','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-95','Nelnal',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s small and its electricity-generating organ is not fully developed, so it uses its tail to absorb electricity from people\'s homes and charge itself.',70,'G','Dedenne','95','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-96','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'In the past, noble families entrusted their vault keys to a Klefki. They passed the Klefki down through the generations, taking good care of it.',70,'G','Klefki','96','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv1-97','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is smooth and moist to the touch. Yeast in Fidough\'s breath induces fermentation in the Pokémon\'s vicinity.',50,'G','Fidough','97','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-98','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon is smooth and moist to the touch. Yeast in Fidough\'s breath induces fermentation in the Pokémon\'s vicinity.',60,'G','Fidough','98','Common','Pokémon'),('sv1-99','You Iribi',NULL,NULL,1,'Fidough','The pleasant aroma that emanates from this Pokémon\'s body helps wheat grow, so Dachsbun has been treasured by farming villages.',90,'G','Dachsbun','99','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-1','Yukiko Baba',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is blown across vast distances by the wind. It is unclear where the Hoppip of Paldea originally came from.',50,'G','Hoppip','1','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-10','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'During cold seasons, it migrates to the mountain\'s lower reaches. It returns to the snow-covered summit in the spring.',90,'G','Snover','10','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-100','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It swings its handmade hammer around to protect itself, but the hammer is often stolen by Pokémon that eat metal.',60,'G','Tinkatink','100','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-101','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It swings its handmade hammer around to protect itself, but the hammer is often stolen by Pokémon that eat metal.',60,'G','Tinkatink','101','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-102','Pani Kobayashi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It swings its handmade hammer around to protect itself, but the hammer is often stolen by Pokémon that eat metal.',70,'G','Tinkatink','102','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-103','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Tinkatink','This Pokémon will attack groups of Pawniard and Bisharp, gathering metal from them in order to create a large and sturdy hammer.',80,'G','Tinkatuff','103','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-104','sowsow',NULL,NULL,2,'Tinkatink','This Pokémon will attack groups of Pawniard and Bisharp, gathering metal from them in order to create a large and sturdy hammer.',90,'G','Tinkatuff','104','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-105','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Tinkatuff','This intelligent Pokémon has a very daring disposition. It knocks rocks into the sky with its hammer, aiming for flying Corviknight.',140,'G','Tinkaton','105','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-106','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It lives in groups in the treetops. If it loses sight of its group, it becomes infuriated by its loneliness.',60,'G','Mankey','106','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-107','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Mankey','It becomes wildly furious if it even senses someone looking at it. It chases anyone that meets its glare.',110,'G','Primeape','107','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-108','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This kind of Tauros, known as the Combat Breed, is distinguished by its thick, powerful muscles and its fierce disposition.',130,'G','Paldean Tauros','108','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-109','Jerky',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Although it always pretends to be a tree, its composition appears more similar to rock than to vegetation.',110,'G','Sudowoodo','109','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-11','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,3,'Snover','It lives a quiet life on mountains that are perpetually covered in snow. It hides itself by whipping up blizzards.',150,'G','Abomasnow','11','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-110','Haru Akasaka',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Born deep underground, this Pokémon becomes a pupa after eating enough dirt to make a mountain.',70,'G','Larvitar','110','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-111','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,'Larvitar','This pupa flies around wildly by venting with great force the gas pressurized inside its body.',90,'G','Pupitar','111','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-112','Kurata So',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It grows stronger by enduring harsh training. It is a gutsy Pokémon that can withstand any attack.',90,'G','Makuhita','112','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-113','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,3,'Makuhita','It loves challenging others to tests of strength. It has the power to stop a train with a slap.',140,'G','Hariyama','113','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-114','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Inflating its poison sacs, it fills the area with an odd sound and hits flinching opponents with a poison jab.',70,'G','Croagunk','114','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-115','Yuya Oka',NULL,NULL,1,'Croagunk','Swaying and dodging the attacks of its foes, it weaves its flexible body in close, then lunges out with its poisonous claws.',130,'G','Toxicroak','115','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-116','0313',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is very friendly when it\'s young. Its disposition becomes vicious once it matures, but it never forgets the kindness of its master.',70,'G','Rockruff','116','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-117','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,'Rockruff',NULL,260,'G','Lycanroc ex','117','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-118','Jerky',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon battles by throwing hard berries. It won\'t obey a Trainer who throws Poké Balls without skill.',110,'G','Passimian','118','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-119','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The brass, which is the one that stands at the front and issues orders, is the strongest and smartest of the six.',110,'G','Falinks','119','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-12','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its fluffy fur is similar in composition to plants. This Pokémon frequently washes its face to keep it from drying out.',60,'G','Sprigatito','12','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-120','yuu',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It was born in a layer of rock salt deep under the earth. This species was particularly treasured in the old days, as they would share precious salt.',60,'G','Nacli','120','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-121','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It was born in a layer of rock salt deep under the earth. This species was particularly treasured in the old days, as they would share precious salt.',70,'G','Nacli','121','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-122','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,3,'Nacli','This Pokémon dry cures its prey by spraying salt over them. The curing process steals away the water in the prey\'s body.',100,'G','Naclstack','122','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-123','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,3,'Naclstack','Garganacl will rub its fingertips together and sprinkle injured Pokémon with salt. Even severe wounds will promptly heal afterward.',180,'G','Garganacl','123','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-124','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It absorbs nutrients from cave walls. The petals it wears are made of crystallized poison.',40,'G','Glimmet','124','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-125','Sekio',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It absorbs nutrients from cave walls. The petals it wears are made of crystallized poison.',70,'G','Glimmet','125','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-126','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,'Glimmet','When this Pokémon detects danger, it will open up its crystalline petals and fire beams from its conical body.',130,'G','Glimmora','126','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-127','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,240,'G','Ting-Lu ex','127','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-128','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'After losing a territorial struggle, Wooper began living on land. The Pokémon changed over time, developing a poisonous film to protect its body.',60,'G','Paldean Wooper','128','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-129','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'After losing a territorial struggle, Wooper began living on land. The Pokémon changed over time, developing a poisonous film to protect its body.',60,'G','Paldean Wooper','129','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-13','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its fluffy fur is similar in composition to plants. This Pokémon frequently washes its face to keep it from drying out.',70,'G','Sprigatito','13','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-130','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,3,'Paldean Wooper',NULL,280,'G','Paldean Clodsire ex','130','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-131','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Feared and loathed by many, it is believed to bring misfortune to all those who see it at night.',60,'G','Murkrow','131','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-132','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,1,'Murkrow','It is merciless by nature. It is said that it never forgives the mistakes of its Murkrow followers.',130,'G','Honchkrow','132','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-133','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This cunning Pokémon hides under the cover of darkness, waiting to attack its prey.',70,'G','Sneasel','133','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-134','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,'Sneasel','Evolution made it even more devious. It communicates by clawing signs in boulders.',110,'G','Weavile','134','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-135','hncl',NULL,NULL,3,'Pupitar','Extremely strong, it can change the landscape. It is so insolent that it doesn\'t care about others.',180,'G','Tyranitar','135','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-136','Nagomi Nijo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It dwells in the darkness of caves. It uses its sharp claws to dig up gems to nourish itself.',70,'G','Sableye','136','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-137','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It sharpens its swordlike tail on hard rocks. It hides in tall grass and strikes unwary prey with venomous fangs.',110,'G','Seviper','137','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-138','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It can\'t see, so its first approach to examining things is to bite them. You will be covered in wounds until a Deino warms up to you.',70,'G','Deino','138','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-139','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,2,'Deino','The two heads do not get along at all. If you don\'t give each head the same amount of attention, they\'ll begin fighting out of jealousy.',100,'G','Zweilous','139','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-14','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,'Sprigatito','Floragato deftly wields the vine hidden beneath its long fur, slamming the hard flower bud against its opponents.',90,'G','Floragato','14','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-140','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,3,'Zweilous','Only the central head has a brain. It is very intelligent, but it thinks only of destruction.',180,'G','Hydreigon','140','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-141','DOM',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It always scowls in an attempt to make opponents take it seriously, but even crying children will burst into laughter when they see Maschiff\'s face.',60,'G','Maschiff','141','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-142','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It always scowls in an attempt to make opponents take it seriously, but even crying children will burst into laughter when they see Maschiff\'s face.',70,'G','Maschiff','142','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-143','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,3,'Maschiff','This Pokémon can store energy in its large dewlap. Mabosstiff unleashes this energy all at once to blow away enemies.',140,'G','Mabosstiff','143','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-144','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though usually a mellow Pokémon, it will sink its sharp, poison-soaked front teeth into any that anger it, causing paralysis in the object of its ire.',50,'G','Shroodle','144','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-145','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though usually a mellow Pokémon, it will sink its sharp, poison-soaked front teeth into any that anger it, causing paralysis in the object of its ire.',60,'G','Shroodle','145','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-146','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,'Shroodle','The color of the poisonous saliva depends on what the Pokémon eats. Grafaiai covers its fingers in its saliva and draws patterns on trees in forests.',90,'G','Grafaiai','146','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-147','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It gathers things up in an apron made from shed feathers added to the Pokémon\'s chest feathers, then drops those things from high places for fun.',120,'G','Bombirdier','147','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-148','Scav',NULL,NULL,2,'Corvisquire','Corviknight can\'t serve as a taxi service in Paldea because the Pokémon\'s natural predators will attack it while it flies, endangering the customer.',170,'G','Corviknight','148','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-149','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Using the pointy tip of its trunk, it carves off chunks of hard rocks to eat. It is very docile and helps people with physical labor.',100,'G','Cufant','149','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-15','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Floragato',NULL,310,'G','Meowscarada ex','15','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-150','Uta',NULL,NULL,4,'Cufant',NULL,300,'G','Copperajah ex','150','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-151','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'When attacked, this Pokémon will wield the tendrils on its body like fists and pelt the opponent with a storm of punches.',130,'G','Orthworm','151','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-152','chibi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon emits ultrasonic waves from its large ears to search for fruit to eat. It mistakes Applin for its food.',70,'G','Noibat','152','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-153','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Noibat',NULL,260,'G','Noivern ex','153','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-154','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Though very small, the brain in its tail is still considered an important organ because it emits powerful psychic energy.',100,'G','Girafarig','154','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-155','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Girafarig','Now that the brain waves from the head and tail are synced up, the psychic power of this Pokémon is 10 times stronger than Girafarig\'s.',140,'G','Farigiraf','155','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-156','Nagomi Nijo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It creates mazes in dark locations. When spotted, it flees into the ground by digging with its tail.',70,'G','Dunsparce','156','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-157','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,3,'Dunsparce','This Pokémon uses its hard tail to make its nest by boring holes into bedrock deep underground. The nest can reach lengths of over six miles.',140,'G','Dudunsparce','157','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-158','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It soars high in the sky, riding on updrafts like a glider. It carries food tucked in its bill.',70,'G','Wingull','158','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-159','Shinya Komatsu',NULL,NULL,2,'Wingull','It is a flying transporter that carries small Pokémon in its beak. It bobs on the waves to rest its wings.',120,'G','Pelipper','159','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-16','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The ball of threads wrapped around its body is elastic enough to deflect the scythes of Scyther, this Pokémon\'s natural enemy.',50,'G','Tarountula','16','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-160','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It sleeps for 20 hours every day. Making drowsy those that see it is one of its abilities.',70,'G','Slakoth','160','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-161','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,2,'Slakoth','Its stress level rises if it cannot keep moving constantly. Too much stress makes it feel sick.',90,'G','Vigoroth','161','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-162','Yuya Oka',NULL,NULL,4,'Vigoroth','It is the world\'s most slothful Pokémon. However, it can exert horrifying power by releasing pent-up energy all at once.',180,'G','Slaking','162','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-163','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is normally calm, but once it enters battle, its hormonal balance changes and it becomes aggressive.',60,'G','Fletchling','163','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-164','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is brave and reckless. The white markings around a Rookidee\'s eyes intimidate fainthearted Pokémon.',60,'G','Rookidee','164','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-165','sui',NULL,NULL,1,'Rookidee','It\'s said that the reason behind Corvisquire\'s high level of intelligence is the large size of its brain relative to those of other bird Pokémon.',90,'G','Corvisquire','165','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-166','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Exhibiting great teamwork, they use their incisors to cut pieces out of any material that might be useful for a nest, then make off with them.',30,'G','Tandemaus','166','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-167','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Exhibiting great teamwork, they use their incisors to cut pieces out of any material that might be useful for a nest, then make off with them.',40,'G','Tandemaus','167','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-168','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,'Tandemaus','They build huge nests with many rooms that are used for different purposes, such as eating and sleeping.',60,'G','Maushold','168','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-169','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,160,'G','Squawkabilly ex','169','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-17','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The ball of threads wrapped around its body is elastic enough to deflect the scythes of Scyther, this Pokémon\'s natural enemy.',60,'G','Tarountula','17','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-170','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon apparently ties the base of its neck into a knot so that the energy stored in its belly does not escape from its beak.',110,'G','Flamigo','170','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-171','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Artazon','171','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-172','NC Empire',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Boss\'s Orders (Ghetsis)','172','Rare','Trainer'),('sv2-173','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Bravery Charm','173','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-174','AYUMI ODASHIMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Calamitous Snowy Mountain','174','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-175','AYUMI ODASHIMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Calamitous Wasteland','175','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-176','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Choice Belt','176','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-177','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Clavell','177','Common','Trainer'),('sv2-178','inose yukie',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Delivery Drone','178','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-179','yuu',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Dendra','179','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-18','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,2,'Tarountula','It clings to branches and ceilings using its threads and moves without a sound. It takes out its prey before the prey even notices it.',110,'G','Spidops','18','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-180','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Falkner','180','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-181','Ayaka Yoshida',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Fighting Au Lait','181','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-182','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Giacomo','182','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-183','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Great Ball','183','Common','Trainer'),('sv2-184','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Grusha','184','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-185','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Iono','185','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-186','AYUMI ODASHIMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Practice Studio','186','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-187','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Saguaro','187','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-188','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Super Rod','188','Common','Trainer'),('sv2-189','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Superior Energy Retrieval','189','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv2-19','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has its third set of legs folded up. When it\'s in a tough spot, this Pokémon jumps over 30 feet using the strength of its legs.',40,'G','Nymble','19','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-190',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Jet Energy','190','Uncommon','Energy'),('sv2-191',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Luminous Energy','191','Uncommon','Energy'),('sv2-192',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Reversal Energy','192','Uncommon','Energy'),('sv2-193',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Therapeutic Energy','193','Uncommon','Energy'),('sv2-194','Kurata So',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It loves sweet nectar. To keep all the nectar to itself, it hurls rivals away with its prized horn.',130,'G','Heracross','194','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-195','Jerky',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It lives in tropical jungles. The bunch of fruit around its neck is delicious. The fruit grows twice a year.',110,'G','Tropius','195','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-196','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its fluffy fur is similar in composition to plants. This Pokémon frequently washes its face to keep it from drying out.',60,'G','Sprigatito','196','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-197','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Sprigatito','Floragato deftly wields the vine hidden beneath its long fur, slamming the hard flower bud against its opponents.',90,'G','Floragato','197','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-198','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A soul unable to move on to the afterlife was blown around by the wind until it got tangled up with dried grass and became a Pokémon.',50,'G','Bramblin','198','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-199','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,1,'Fletchling','Fletchinder scatters embers in tall grass where bug Pokémon might be hiding and then catches them as they come leaping out.',80,'G','Fletchinder','199','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-2','Yoriyuki Ikegami',NULL,NULL,1,'Hoppip','Skiploom enthusiasts can apparently tell where a Skiploom was born by the scent drifting from the flower on the Pokémon\'s head.',70,'G','Skiploom','2','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv2-20','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has its third set of legs folded up. When it\'s in a tough spot, this Pokémon jumps over 30 feet using the strength of its legs.',50,'G','Nymble','20','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-200','Po-Suzuki',NULL,NULL,2,'Litleo','The females of a pride work together to bring down prey. It\'s thanks to them that their pride doesn\'t starve.',120,'G','Pyroar','200','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-201','kantaro',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It lies on warm rocks and uses the heat absorbed by its square-shaped scales to create fire energy.',90,'G','Fuecoco','201','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-202','kantaro',NULL,NULL,3,'Fuecoco','The combination of Crocalor\'s fire energy and overflowing vitality has caused an egg-shaped fireball to appear on the Pokémon\'s head.',110,'G','Crocalor','202','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-203','Shinji Kanda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'An underpowered, pathetic Pokémon. It may jump high on rare occasions but never more than seven feet.',30,'G','Magikarp','203','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-204','Atsuya Uki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The fur on its body naturally repels water. It can stay dry even when it plays in the water.',70,'G','Marill','204','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-205','Nelnal',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'On hot days, these Pokémon press their ice cube heads together and pass the time cooling each other down.',110,'G','Eiscue','205','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-206','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon migrated to Paldea from distant lands long ago. The gel secreted by its feathers repels water and grime.',60,'G','Quaxly','206','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-207','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,'Quaxly','These Pokémon constantly run through shallow waters to train their legs, then compete with each other to see which of them kicks most gracefully.',90,'G','Quaxwell','207','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-208','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Frigibax absorbs heat through its dorsal fin and converts the heat into ice energy. The higher the temperature, the more energy Frigibax stores.',60,'G','Frigibax','208','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-209','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,2,'Frigibax','Arctibax freezes the air around it, protecting its face with an ice mask and turning its dorsal fin into a blade of ice.',90,'G','Arctibax','209','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-21','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,'Nymble','When it decides to fight all out, it stands on its previously folded legs to enter Showdown Mode. It neutralizes its enemies in short order.',120,'G','Lokix','21','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-210','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,2,'Arctibax','This Pokémon blasts cryogenic air out from its mouth. This air can instantly freeze even liquid-hot lava.',160,'G','Baxcalibur','210','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-211','Toshinao Aoki',NULL,NULL,1,'Pikachu','Its tail discharges electricity into the ground, protecting it from getting shocked.',140,'G','Raichu','211','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-212','aoki',NULL,NULL,1,'Misdreavus','Its cry sounds like an incantation. It is said the cry may rarely be imbued with happiness-giving power.',90,'G','Mismagius','212','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-213','SIE NANAHARA',NULL,NULL,1,'Gothita','This Pokémon will hypnotize children to put them to sleep before carrying them away. Be wary of nights when the starlight is bright.',90,'G','Gothorita','213','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-214','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'If it loses its shovel, it will stick something else— like a branch—in its head to make do until it finds another shovel.',90,'G','Sandygast','214','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-215','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,'Rellor','The body that supports the ball barely moves. Therefore, it is thought that the true body of this Pokémon is actually inside the ball.',70,'G','Rabsca','215','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-216','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It swings its handmade hammer around to protect itself, but the hammer is often stolen by Pokémon that eat metal.',60,'G','Tinkatink','216','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-217','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,2,'Tinkatink','This Pokémon will attack groups of Pawniard and Bisharp, gathering metal from them in order to create a large and sturdy hammer.',90,'G','Tinkatuff','217','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-218','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This kind of Tauros, known as the Combat Breed, is distinguished by its thick, powerful muscles and its fierce disposition.',130,'G','Paldean Tauros','218','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-219','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Although it always pretends to be a tree, its composition appears more similar to rock than to vegetation.',110,'G','Sudowoodo','219','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-22','Pani Kobayashi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A soul unable to move on to the afterlife was blown around by the wind until it got tangled up with dried grass and became a Pokémon.',40,'G','Bramblin','22','Common','Pokémon'),('sv2-220','Ryota Murayama',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It was born in a layer of rock salt deep under the earth. This species was particularly treasured in the old days, as they would share precious salt.',70,'G','Nacli','220','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-221','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'After losing a territorial struggle, Wooper began living on land. The Pokémon changed over time, developing a poisonous film to protect its body.',60,'G','Paldean Wooper','221','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-222','Nurikabe',NULL,NULL,3,'Pupitar','Extremely strong, it can change the landscape. It is so insolent that it doesn\'t care about others.',180,'G','Tyranitar','222','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-223','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,1,'Shroodle','The color of the poisonous saliva depends on what the Pokémon eats. Grafaiai covers its fingers in its saliva and draws patterns on trees in forests.',90,'G','Grafaiai','223','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-224','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'When attacked, this Pokémon will wield the tendrils on its body like fists and pelt the opponent with a storm of punches.',130,'G','Orthworm','224','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-225','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is brave and reckless. The white markings around a Rookidee\'s eyes intimidate fainthearted Pokémon.',60,'G','Rookidee','225','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv2-226','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,'Tandemaus','They build h