hin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The more sunlight this Pokémon bathes in, the more spicy chemicals are produced by its body, and thus the spicier its moves become.',50,'G','Capsakid','23','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-230',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Basic Fire Energy','230','Hyper Rare','Energy'),('sv3-24','Pani Kobayashi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The more sunlight this Pokémon bathes in, the more spicy chemicals are produced by its body, and thus the spicier its moves become.',70,'G','Capsakid','24','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-25','kodama',NULL,NULL,2,'Capsakid','The red head converts spicy chemicals into fire energy and blasts the surrounding area with a super spicy stream of flame.',110,'G','Scovillain','25','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-26','DOM',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'From the time it is born, a flame burns at the tip of its tail. Its life would end if the flame were to go out.',60,'G','Charmander','26','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-27','Ryota Murayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Charmander','If it becomes agitated during battle, it spouts intense flames, incinerating its surroundings.',90,'G','Charmeleon','27','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-28','0313',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'As each tail grows, its fur becomes more lustrous. When held, it feels slightly warm.',60,'G','Vulpix','28','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-29','Yoshioka',NULL,NULL,1,'Vulpix','Very smart and very vengeful. Grabbing one of its many tails could result in a 1,000-year curse.',120,'G','Ninetales','29','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-3','sui',NULL,NULL,1,'Gloom','Bellossom gather at times and appear to dance. They say that the dance is a ritual to summon the sun.',130,'G','Bellossom','3','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-30','toriyufu',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It is said that when it roars, a volcano erupts somewhere around the globe.',130,'G','Entei','30','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-31','Mizue',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Magma of almost 2,200 degrees Fahrenheit courses through its body. When it grows cold, the magma hardens and slows it.',90,'G','Numel','31','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-32','Shiburingaru',NULL,NULL,3,'Numel','It lives in the crater of a volcano. It is well known that the humps on its back erupt every 10 years.',140,'G','Camerupt','32','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-33','Saki Hayashiro',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,190,'G','Victini ex','33','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-34','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This popular symbol of good fortune will never fall over in its sleep, no matter how it\'s pushed or pulled.',80,'G','Darumaka','34','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-35','Yuya Oka',NULL,NULL,3,'Darumaka','This Pokémon\'s power level rises along with the temperature of its fire, which can reach 2,500 degrees Fahrenheit.',140,'G','Darmanitan','35','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-36','Nagomi Nijo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The younger the life this Pokémon absorbs, the brighter and eerier the flame on its head burns.',60,'G','Litwick','36','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-37','Aya Kusube',NULL,NULL,1,'Litwick','It lurks in cities, pretending to be a lamp. Once it finds someone whose death is near, it will trail quietly after them.',80,'G','Lampent','37','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-38','Haru Akasaka',NULL,NULL,2,'Lampent','In homes illuminated by Chandelure instead of lights, funerals were a constant occurrence—or so it\'s said.',150,'G','Chandelure','38','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-39','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A flame serves as its tongue, melting through the hard shell of Durant so that Heatmor can devour their insides.',110,'G','Heatmor','39','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-4','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It slashes through grass with its sharp scythes, moving too fast for the human eye to track.',80,'G','Scyther','4','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-40','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon was called the Larva That Stole the Sun. The fire Larvesta spouts from its horns can cut right through a sheet of iron.',80,'G','Larvesta','40','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-41','Yukiko Baba',NULL,NULL,2,'Larvesta','Its burning body causes it to be unpopular in hot parts of the world, but in cold ones, Volcarona is revered as an embodiment of the sun.',140,'G','Volcarona','41','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-42','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'G','Eiscue ex','42','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-43','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Burnt charcoal came to life and became a Pokémon. Possessing a fiery fighting spirit, Charcadet will battle even tough opponents.',70,'G','Charcadet','43','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-44','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,'Charcadet','Armarouge evolved through the use of a set of armor that belonged to a distinguished warrior. This Pokémon is incredibly loyal.',120,'G','Armarouge','44','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-45','matazo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Crossing icy seas is no issue for this cold-resistant Pokémon. Its smooth skin is a little cool to the touch.',110,'G','Lapras','45','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-46','Jerky',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'These Pokémon have sharp fangs and powerful jaws. Sailors avoid Carvanha dens at all costs.',50,'G','Carvanha','46','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-47','Tonji Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,'Carvanha','This Pokémon is known as the Bully of the Sea. Any ship entering the waters Sharpedo calls home will be attacked—no exceptions.',120,'G','Sharpedo','47','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-48','Jerky',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It spins its two tails like a screw to propel itself through water. The tails also slice clinging seaweed.',70,'G','Buizel','48','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-49','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Buizel','With its flotation sac inflated, it can carry people on its back. It deflates the sac before it dives.',110,'G','Floatzel','49','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-5','Kurata So',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The berries stored in its vaselike shell eventually become a thick, pulpy juice.',80,'G','Shuckle','5','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-50','OKUBO',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It uses sound waves to communicate with others of its kind. People and other Pokémon species can\'t hear its cries of warning.',70,'G','Tympole','50','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-51','sowsow',NULL,NULL,2,'Tympole','On occasion, their cries are sublimely pleasing to the ear. Palpitoad with larger lumps on their bodies can sing with a wider range of sounds.',100,'G','Palpitoad','51','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-52','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,3,'Palpitoad','This Pokémon is popular among the elderly, who say the vibrations of its lumps are great for massages.',170,'G','Seismitoad','52','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-53','Mizue',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Many of this species can be found along the shorelines of cold regions. If a Cubchoo lacks dangling snot, there\'s a chance it is sick.',70,'G','Cubchoo','53','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-54','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,3,'Cubchoo','It is a ferocious, carnivorous Pokémon. Once it captures its prey, it will breathe cold air onto the prey to freeze and preserve it.',150,'G','Beartic','54','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-55','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Cryogonal appear during cold seasons. It is said that people and Pokémon who die on snowy mountains are reborn into these Pokémon.',90,'G','Cryogonal','55','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-56','Atsuya Uki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It protects its skin by covering its body in delicate bubbles. Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it keeps a watchful eye on its surroundings.',70,'G','Froakie','56','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-57','Tonji Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,'Froakie','Its swiftness is unparalleled. It can scale a tower of more than 600 metres in a minute\'s time.',90,'G','Frogadier','57','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-58','Pani Kobayashi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand.',60,'G','Wiglett','58','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-59','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,'Wiglett','It has a vicious temperament, contrary to what its appearance may suggest. It wraps its long bodies around prey, then drags the prey into its den.',90,'G','Wugtrio','59','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-6','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They usually live on ponds, but after an evening shower, they may appear on puddles in towns.',60,'G','Surskit','6','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-60','kodama',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It likes playing with others of its kind using the water ring on its tail. It uses ultrasonic waves to sense the emotions of other living creatures.',50,'G','Finizen','60','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-61','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It likes playing with others of its kind using the water ring on its tail. It uses ultrasonic waves to sense the emotions of other living creatures.',90,'G','Finizen','61','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-62','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,'Finizen','This Pokémon\'s ancient genes have awakened. It is now so extraordinarily strong that it can easily lift a cruise ship with one fin.',150,'G','Palafin','62','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-63','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The electromagnetic waves emitted by the units at the sides of its head expel antigravity, which allows it to float.',60,'G','Magnemite','63','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-64','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,2,'Magnemite','Three Magnemite are linked by a strong magnetic force. Earaches will occur if you get too close.',90,'G','Magneton','64','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-65','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,'Magneton','As it zooms through the sky, this Pokémon seems to be receiving signals of unknown origin while transmitting signals of unknown purpose.',170,'G','Magnezone','65','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-66','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,4,'Pupitar',NULL,340,'G','Tyranitar ex','66','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-67','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'While one alone doesn\'t have much power, a chain of many Tynamo can be as powerful as lightning.',40,'G','Tynamo','67','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-68','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,'Tynamo','They coil around foes and shock them with electricity-generating organs that seem simply to be circular patterns.',90,'G','Eelektrik','68','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-69','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,3,'Eelektrik','They crawl out of the ocean using their arms. They will attack prey on shore and immediately drag it into the ocean.',160,'G','Eelektross','69','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-7','Haru Akasaka',NULL,NULL,1,'Surskit','It flaps its four wings to hover and fly freely in any direction—to and fro and sideways.',100,'G','Masquerain','7','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-70','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'As it flies around, it shoots lightning all over the place and causes forest fires. It is therefore disliked.',110,'G','Thundurus','70','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-71','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has no problem drinking dirty water. An organ inside Toxel\'s body filters such water into a poisonous liquid that is harmless to Toxel.',70,'G','Toxel','71','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-72','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,'Toxel','Many youths admire the way this Pokémon listlessly picks fights and keeps its cool no matter what opponent it faces.',140,'G','Toxtricity','72','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-73','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Pawmo',NULL,300,'G','Pawmot ex','73','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-74','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Tadbulb shakes its tail to generate electricity. If it senses danger, it will make its head blink on and off to alert its allies.',50,'G','Tadbulb','74','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-75','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Tadbulb shakes its tail to generate electricity. If it senses danger, it will make its head blink on and off to alert its allies.',60,'G','Tadbulb','75','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-76','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Tadbulb shakes its tail to generate electricity. If it senses danger, it will make its head blink on and off to alert its allies.',60,'G','Tadbulb','76','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-77','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Tadbulb','When this Pokémon expands and contracts its wobbly body, the belly-button dynamo in its stomach produces a huge amount of electricity.',130,'G','Bellibolt','77','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-78','Toshinao Aoki',NULL,NULL,3,'Tadbulb','When this Pokémon expands and contracts its wobbly body, the belly-button dynamo in its stomach produces a huge amount of electricity.',140,'G','Bellibolt','78','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-79','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,220,'G','Miraidon ex','79','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-8','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'At night, Combee sleep in a group of about a hundred, packed closely together in a lump.',50,'G','Combee','8','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-80','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Because of its unusual, starlike silhouette, people believe that it came here on a meteor.',30,'G','Cleffa','80','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-81','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its adorable behavior and cry make it highly popular. However, this cute Pokémon is rarely found.',60,'G','Clefairy','81','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-82','Satoshi Shirai',NULL,NULL,2,'Clefairy',NULL,260,'G','Clefable ex','82','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-83','Natsumi Yoshida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is considered to be a symbol of good luck. Its shell is said to be filled with happiness.',50,'G','Togepi','83','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-84','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,'Togepi','It grows dispirited if it is not with kind people. It can float in midair without moving its wings.',90,'G','Togetic','84','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-85','Cona Nitanda',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Togetic','Known as a bringer of blessings, it\'s been depicted on good-luck charms since ancient times.',150,'G','Togekiss','85','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-86','Cona Nitanda',NULL,NULL,1,'Eevee','The tip of its forked tail quivers when it is predicting its opponent\'s next move.',110,'G','Espeon','86','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-87','Sekio',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'In contrast to its appearance, it\'s quite timid. When playing with other puppy Pokémon, it sometimes gets bullied.',80,'G','Snubbull','87','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-88','Lee HyunJung',NULL,NULL,2,'Snubbull','Although it\'s popular with young people, Granbull is timid and sensitive, so it\'s totally incompetent as a watchdog.',130,'G','Granbull','88','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-89','0313',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It chomps with its gaping mouth. Its huge jaws are actually steel horns that have been transformed.',100,'G','Mawile','89','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-9','You Iribi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'There is a theory that the developer of the modern-day Poké Ball really liked Foongus, but this has not been confirmed.',50,'G','Foongus','9','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-90','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Spoink will die if it stops bouncing. The pearl on its head amplifies its psychic powers.',70,'G','Spoink','90','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-91','Scav',NULL,NULL,1,'Spoink','It can perform odd dance steps to influence foes. Its style of dancing became hugely popular overseas.',120,'G','Grumpig','91','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-92','Tetsu Kayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It was discovered at the site of a meteor strike 40 years ago. Its stare can lull its foes to sleep.',90,'G','Lunatone','92','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-93','Tetsu Kayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Solar energy is the source of its power, so it is strong during the daytime. When it spins, its body shines.',90,'G','Solrock','93','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-94','Scav',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It was discovered in ancient ruins. While moving, it constantly spins. It stands on one foot even when asleep.',70,'G','Baltoy','94','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-95','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,2,'Baltoy','It appears to have been born from clay dolls made by ancient people. It uses telekinesis to float and move.',120,'G','Claydol','95','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-96','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Combee',NULL,270,'G','Vespiquen ex','96','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3-97','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The soul of someone who died alone possessed some leftover tea. This Pokémon appears in hotels and houses.',30,'G','Sinistea','97','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3-98','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,2,'Sinistea','The tea that composes Polteageist\'s body has a distinct and enjoyable flavor. Drinking too much, however, can be fatal.',70,'G','Polteageist','98','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3-99','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It is said that a dog Pokémon that died in the wild without ever interacting with a human was reborn as this Pokémon.',70,'G','Greavard','99','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-1','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'While it is young, it uses the nutrients that are stored in the seed on its back in order to grow.',70,'G','Bulbasaur','1','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-10','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its short feet are tipped with suction pads that enable it to tirelessly climb slopes and walls.',50,'G','Caterpie','10','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-100','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It rolls to move. If the ground is uneven, a sudden jolt from hitting a bump can cause it to explode.',60,'G','Voltorb','100','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-101','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,'Voltorb','The more energy it charges up, the faster it gets. But this also makes it more likely to explode.',90,'G','Electrode','101','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-102','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'These Pokémon get nervous when they\'re not in a group of six. The minute even one member of the group goes missing, Exeggcute become cowardly.',60,'G','Exeggcute','102','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-103','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,3,'Exeggcute','When they work together, Exeggutor\'s three heads can put out powerful psychic energy. Cloudy days make this Pokémon sluggish.',140,'G','Exeggutor','103','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-104','Shinya Komatsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon wears the skull of its deceased mother. Sometimes Cubone\'s dreams make it cry, but each tear Cubone sheds makes it stronger.',70,'G','Cubone','104','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-105','Shinya Komatsu',NULL,NULL,2,'Cubone','When this Pokémon evolved, the skull of its mother fused to it. Marowak\'s temperament also turned vicious at the same time.',120,'G','Marowak','105','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-106','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The legs freely contract and stretch. The stretchy legs allow it to hit a distant foe with a rising kick.',120,'G','Hitmonlee','106','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-107','DOM',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its punches slice the air. However, it seems to need a short break after fighting for three minutes.',120,'G','Hitmonchan','107','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-108','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'Bug Pokémon are Lickitung\'s main food source. This Pokémon paralyzes its prey with a lick from its long tongue, then swallows the prey whole.',100,'G','Lickitung','108','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-109','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its body is full of poisonous gas. It floats into garbage dumps, seeking out the fumes of raw, rotting trash.',60,'G','Koffing','109','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-11','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,3,'Caterpie','Even though it is encased in a sturdy shell, the body inside is tender. It can\'t withstand a harsh attack.',90,'G','Metapod','11','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-110','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,2,'Koffing','Very rarely, a sudden mutation can result in two small Koffing twins becoming conjoined as a Weezing.',110,'G','Weezing','110','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-111','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It can remember only one thing at a time. Once it starts rushing, it forgets why it started.',100,'G','Rhyhorn','111','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-112','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,4,'Rhyhorn','Protected by an armor-like hide, it is capable of living in molten lava of 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit.',120,'G','Rhydon','112','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-113','Taiga Kayama',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This kindly Pokémon lays highly nutritious eggs and shares them with injured Pokémon or people.',110,'G','Chansey','113','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-114','Aya Kusube',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Hidden beneath a tangle of vines that grows nonstop even if the vines are torn off, this Pokémon\'s true appearance remains a mystery.',80,'G','Tangela','114','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-115','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,230,'G','Kangaskhan ex','115','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-116','aspara',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They swim with dance-like motions and cause whirlpools to form. Horsea compete to see which of them can generate the biggest whirlpool.',60,'G','Horsea','116','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-117','aspara',NULL,NULL,1,'Horsea','Seadra\'s mouth is slender, but its suction power is strong. In an instant, Seadra can suck in food that\'s larger than the opening of its mouth.',80,'G','Seadra','117','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-118','SIE NANAHARA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its dorsal and pectoral fins are strongly developed like muscles. It can swim at a speed of five knots.',70,'G','Goldeen','118','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-119','SIE NANAHARA',NULL,NULL,2,'Goldeen','Using its horn, it bores holes in riverbed boulders, making nests to prevent its eggs from washing away.',110,'G','Seaking','119','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-12','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,'Metapod','It collects honey every day. It rubs honey onto the hairs on its legs to carry it back to its nest.',130,'G','Butterfree','12','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-120','Arai Kiriko',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Fish Pokémon nibble at it, but Staryu isn\'t bothered. Its body regenerates quickly, even if part of it is completely torn off.',60,'G','Staryu','120','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-121','Arai Kiriko',NULL,NULL,1,'Staryu','Starmie swims by spinning its body at high speed. As this Pokémon cruises through the ocean, it absorbs tiny plankton.',90,'G','Starmie','121','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-122','OOYAMA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s known for its top-notch pantomime skills. It protects itself from all sorts of attacks by emitting auras from its fingers to create walls.',90,'G','Mr. Mime','122','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-123','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'It slashes through grass with its sharp scythes, moving too fast for the human eye to track.',70,'G','Scyther','123','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-124','Ayaka Yoshida',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,200,'G','Jynx ex','124','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-125','NC Empire',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'With the coming of a storm, many of these Pokémon will gather under tall trees and sit there waiting for lightning to strike.',90,'G','Electabuzz','125','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-126','Toshinao Aoki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'These Pokémon\'s bodies are constantly burning. Magmar are feared as one of the causes behind fires.',90,'G','Magmar','126','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-127','Yuya Oka',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon clamps its pincers down on its prey and then either splits the prey in half or flings it away.',120,'G','Pinsir','127','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-128','Takeshi Nakamura',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'When it targets an enemy, it charges furiously while whipping its body with its long tails.',120,'G','Tauros','128','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-129','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'An underpowered, pathetic Pokémon. It may jump high on rare occasions but never more than seven feet.',30,'G','Magikarp','129','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-13','nisimono',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its poison stinger is very powerful. Its bright-colored body is intended to warn off its enemies.',50,'G','Weedle','13','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-130','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,4,'Magikarp','Once it appears, it goes on a rampage. It remains enraged until it demolishes everything around it.',190,'G','Gyarados','130','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-131','LINNE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Crossing icy seas is no issue for this cold-resistant Pokémon. Its smooth skin is a little cool to the touch.',110,'G','Lapras','131','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-132','KIYOTAKA OSHIYAMA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its transformation ability is perfect. However, if made to laugh, it can\'t maintain its disguise.',60,'G','Ditto','132','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-133','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its ability to evolve into many forms allows it to adapt smoothly and perfectly to any environment.',70,'G','Eevee','133','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-134','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,2,'Eevee','It lives close to water. Its long tail is ridged with a fin, which is often mistaken for a mermaid\'s.',130,'G','Vaporeon','134','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-135','sui',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Eevee','It concentrates the weak electric charges emitted by its cells and launches wicked lightning bolts.',110,'G','Jolteon','135','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-136','Ryota Murayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Eevee','Inhaled air is carried to its flame sac, heated, and exhaled as fire that reaches over 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit.',130,'G','Flareon','136','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-137','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'In recent years, this species has been very helpful in cyberspace. These Pokémon will go around checking to make sure no suspicious data exists.',60,'G','Porygon','137','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-138','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Antique Helix Fossil','This Pokémon is a member of an ancient, extinct species. Omanyte paddles through water with its 10 tentacles, looking like it\'s just drifting along.',100,'G','Omanyte','138','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-139','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,3,'Omanyte','Omastar\'s sharp fangs could crush rock, but the Pokémon can attack only the prey that come within reach of its tentacles.',150,'G','Omastar','139','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-14','nisimono',NULL,NULL,3,'Weedle','While awaiting evolution, it hides from predators under leaves and in nooks of branches.',80,'G','Kakuna','14','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-140','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,'Antique Dome Fossil','While some say this species has gone extinct, Kabuto sightings are apparently fairly common in some places.',90,'G','Kabuto','140','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-141','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,'Kabuto','The cause behind the extinction of this species is unknown. Kabutops were aggressive Pokémon that inhabited warm seas.',160,'G','Kabutops','141','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-142','Shinji Kanda',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Antique Old Amber','Aerodactyl\'s sawlike fangs can shred skin to tatters—even the skin of Steel-type Pokémon.',130,'G','Aerodactyl','142','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-143','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'This Pokémon\'s stomach is so strong, even eating moldy or rotten food will not affect it.',150,'G','Snorlax','143','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-144','chibi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon can control ice at will. Articuno is said to live in snowy mountains riddled with permafrost.',120,'G','Articuno','144','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-145','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,200,'G','Zapdos ex','145','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-146','KEIICHIRO ITO',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'There are stories of this Pokémon using its radiant, flame-cloaked wings to light up paths for those lost in the mountains.',120,'G','Moltres','146','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-147','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It sheds many layers of skin as it grows larger. During this process, it is protected by a rapid waterfall.',60,'G','Dratini','147','Common','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-148','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,2,'Dratini','They say that if it emits an aura from its whole body, the weather will begin to change instantly.',100,'G','Dragonair','148','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-149','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,3,'Dragonair','It is said that somewhere in the ocean lies an island where these gather. Only they live there.',180,'G','Dragonite','149','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-15','nisimono',NULL,NULL,1,'Kakuna','May appear in a swarm. Flies at violent speeds, all the while stabbing with the toxic stinger on its rear.',130,'G','Beedrill','15','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-150','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'A Pokémon created by recombining Mew\'s genes. It\'s said to have the most savage heart among Pokémon.',130,'G','Mewtwo','150','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-151','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,180,'G','Mew ex','151','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv3pt5-152