','Iron Valiant ex','261','Hyper Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-262','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,230,'G','Roaring Moon ex','262','Hyper Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-263','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Beach Court','263','Hyper Rare','Trainer'),('sv4-264','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Counter Catcher','264','Hyper Rare','Trainer'),('sv4-265','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Luxurious Cape','265','Hyper Rare','Trainer'),('sv4-266',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Reversal Energy','266','Hyper Rare','Energy'),('sv4-27','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,2,'Charcadet',NULL,260,'G','Armarouge ex','27','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-28','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'No records exist of this species being caught. Data is lacking, but the Pokémon\'s traits match up with an object described in an old book.',130,'G','Iron Moth','28','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-29','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It controls flames burning at over 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit. It casually swims through the sea of lava it creates by melting rock and sand.',110,'G','Chi-Yu','29','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-3','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,'Snorunt',NULL,250,'G','Froslass ex','3','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-30','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They swim with dance-like motions and cause whirlpools to form. Horsea compete to see which of them can generate the biggest whirlpool.',60,'G','Horsea','30','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-31','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,'Horsea','Seadra\'s mouth is slender, but its suction power is strong. In an instant, Seadra can suck in food that\'s larger than the opening of its mouth.',90,'G','Seadra','31','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-32','Tonji Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,'Seadra','Scales shed by this Pokémon have such a splendorous gleam to them that they\'ve been given to royalty as gifts.',150,'G','Kingdra','32','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-33','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Using its dorsal fin as a suction pad, it clings to a Mantine\'s underside to scavenge for leftovers.',70,'G','Remoraid','33','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-34','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,2,'Remoraid','It traps enemies with its suction-cupped tentacles, then smashes them with its rock-hard head.',110,'G','Octillery','34','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-35','Tetsu Kayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is a shabby and ugly Pokémon. However, it is very hardy and can survive on little water.',30,'G','Feebas','35','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-36','Atsuya Uki',NULL,NULL,2,'Feebas','It\'s said that a glimpse of a Milotic and its beauty will calm any hostile emotions you\'re feeling.',120,'G','Milotic','36','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-37','satoma',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is said that several Snorunt gather under giant leaves and live together in harmony.',60,'G','Snorunt','37','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-38','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Gabite',NULL,320,'G','Garchomp ex','38','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-39','miki kudo',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'It swims along with a school of Remoraid, and they\'ll all fight together to repel attackers.',30,'G','Mantyke','39','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-4','Jerky',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s good at finding berries and gathers them from all over. It\'s kind enough to share them with friends.',70,'G','Pansage','4','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-40','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It has the ability to distort space. It is described as a deity in Sinnoh-region mythology.',130,'G','Palkia','40','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-41','Natsumi Yoshida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The water stored inside the tuft on its head is full of nutrients. Plants that receive its water grow large.',70,'G','Panpour','41','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-42','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,'Panpour','It prefers places with clean water. When its tuft runs low, it replenishes it by siphoning up water with its tail.',100,'G','Simipour','42','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-43','miki kudo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Supposedly, this Pokémon was born from an icicle. It spews out freezing air at −58 degrees Fahrenheit to make itself more comfortable.',60,'G','Vanillite','43','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-44','Lee HyunJung',NULL,NULL,2,'Vanillite','It blasts enemies with cold air reaching −148 degrees Fahrenheit, freezing them solid. But it spares their lives afterward—it\'s a kind Pokémon.',90,'G','Vanillish','44','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-45','Nelnal',NULL,NULL,2,'Vanillish','People believe this Pokémon formed when two Vanillish stuck together. Its body temperature is roughly 21 degrees Fahrenheit.',150,'G','Vanilluxe','45','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-46','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Steenee',NULL,310,'G','Tsareena ex','46','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-47','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Wimpod gather in swarms, constantly on the lookout for danger. They scatter the moment they detect an enemy\'s presence.',70,'G','Wimpod','47','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-48','sowsow',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Wimpod gather in swarms, constantly on the lookout for danger. They scatter the moment they detect an enemy\'s presence.',70,'G','Wimpod','48','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-49','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,2,'Wimpod','They live in sunken ships or in holes in the seabed. When Golisopod and Grapploct battle, the loser becomes the winner\'s meal.',140,'G','Golisopod','49','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-5','Kurata So',NULL,NULL,1,'Pansage','Ill tempered, it fights by swinging its barbed tail around wildly. The leaf growing on its head is very bitter.',100,'G','Simisage','5','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-50','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,3,'Wimpod',NULL,270,'G','Golisopod ex','50','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-51','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand.',50,'G','Wiglett','51','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-52','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand.',60,'G','Wiglett','52','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-53','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Wiglett','It has a vicious temperament, contrary to what its appearance may suggest. It wraps its long bodies around prey, then drags the prey into its den.',90,'G','Wugtrio','53','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-54','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'When Veluza discards unnecessary flesh, its mind becomes honed and its psychic power increases. The spare flesh has a mild but delicious flavor.',120,'G','Veluza','54','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-55','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'This Pokémon is a glutton, but it\'s bad at getting food. It teams up with a Tatsugiri to catch prey.',160,'G','Dondozo','55','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-56','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It resembles a mysterious object mentioned in an old book. There are only two reported sightings of this Pokémon.',100,'G','Iron Bundle','56','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-57','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The hatred of those who perished by the sword long ago has clad itself in snow and become a Pokémon.',120,'G','Chien-Pao','57','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-58','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,230,'G','Mewtwo ex','58','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-59','aoki',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'It\'s not good at storing electricity yet. This Pokémon sneaks into people\'s homes, looking for electrical outlets to eat electricity from.',30,'G','Elekid','59','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-6','Scav',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It first tries to find a rock to live in, but if there are no suitable rocks to be found, Dwebble may move in to the ports of a Hippowdon.',60,'G','Dwebble','6','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-60','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It absorbs electricity from telephone poles. It shorts out its body to create crackling noises.',70,'G','Plusle','60','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-61','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It cheers on friends. If its friends are losing, its body lets off more and more sparks.',70,'G','Minun','61','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-62','Shinji Kanda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its mane shines when it discharges electricity. They use the frequency and rhythm of these flashes to communicate.',60,'G','Blitzle','62','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-63','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,1,'Blitzle','They have lightning-like movements. When Zebstrika run at full speed, the sound of thunder reverberates.',120,'G','Zebstrika','63','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-64','Kedamahadaitai Yawarakai',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Joltik latch on to other Pokémon and suck out static electricity. They\'re often found sticking to Yamper\'s hindquarters.',40,'G','Joltik','64','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-65','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,1,'Joltik','It lays traps of electrified threads near the nests of bird Pokémon, aiming to snare chicks that are not yet good at flying.',100,'G','Galvantula','65','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-66','Shiburingaru',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Concealing itself in lightning clouds, it flies throughout the Unova region. It creates electricity in its tail.',130,'G','Zekrom','66','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-67','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The energetic, cheerful dance of these Oricorio is popular with children, but the Oricorio themselves are hard to find in Paldea.',90,'G','Oricorio','67','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-68','hncl',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,210,'G','Tapu Koko ex','68','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-69','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This selfish, attention-seeking Pokémon stores poison and electricity in two different sacs inside its body.',70,'G','Toxel','69','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-7','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,'Dwebble','Its thick claws are its greatest weapons. They\'re mighty enough to crack Rhyperior\'s carapace.',130,'G','Crustle','7','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-70','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,230,'G','Iron Hands ex','70','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-71','ryoma uratsuka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Because its wings aren\'t yet fully grown, it has to hop to get around. It is always staring at something.',50,'G','Natu','71','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-72','Tetsu Kayama',NULL,NULL,1,'Natu','This odd Pokémon can see both the past and the future. It eyes the sun\'s movement all day.',100,'G','Xatu','72','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-73','chibi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It understands human speech and is highly intelligent. It is a tender Pokémon that dislikes fighting.',110,'G','Latios','73','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-74','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'DNA from a space virus mutated and became a Pokémon. It appears where auroras are seen.',120,'G','Deoxys','74','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-75','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The spirit of a person from a bygone age became this Pokémon. It rambles through ruins, searching for someone who knows its face.',70,'G','Yamask','75','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-76','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,'Yamask',NULL,260,'G','Cofagrigus ex','76','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-77','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The light that streams out from the holes in the pumpkin can hypnotize and control the people and Pokémon that see it.',60,'G','Pumpkaboo','77','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-78','nisimono',NULL,NULL,2,'Pumpkaboo','In the darkness of a new-moon night, Gourgeist will come knocking. Whoever answers the door will be swept off to the afterlife.',110,'G','Gourgeist','78','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-79','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It spends its time running around wastelands. If anyone steals its beloved berries, it will chase them down and exact its revenge.',40,'G','Flittle','79','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-8','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its sweat is sweet, like syrup made from boiled- down fruit. Because of this, Bounsweet was highly valued in the past, when sweeteners were scarce.',60,'G','Bounsweet','8','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-80','kodama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It spends its time running around wastelands. If anyone steals its beloved berries, it will chase them down and exact its revenge.',50,'G','Flittle','80','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-81','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,1,'Flittle','It emits psychic power from the gaps between its multicolored frills and sprints at speeds greater than 120 mph.',120,'G','Espathra','81','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-82','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon pounds iron scraps together to make a hammer. It will remake the hammer again and again until it\'s satisfied with the result.',60,'G','Tinkatink','82','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-83','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon pounds iron scraps together to make a hammer. It will remake the hammer again and again until it\'s satisfied with the result.',70,'G','Tinkatink','83','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-84','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,'Tinkatink','These Pokémon make their homes in piles of scrap metal. They test the strength of each other\'s hammers by smashing them together.',80,'G','Tinkatuff','84','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-85','KEIICHIRO ITO',NULL,NULL,2,'Tinkatuff','The hammer tops 220 pounds, yet it gets swung around easily by Tinkaton as it steals whatever it pleases and carries its plunder back home.',130,'G','Tinkaton','85','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-86','Ryota Murayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'There has been only one reported sighting of this Pokémon. It resembles a mysterious creature depicted in an old expedition journal.',90,'G','Scream Tail','86','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-87','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon was born inside a treasure chest about 1,500 years ago. It sucks the life-force out of scoundrels who try to steal the treasure.',50,'G','Gimmighoul','87','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-88','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon was born inside a treasure chest about 1,500 years ago. It sucks the life-force out of scoundrels who try to steal the treasure.',70,'G','Gimmighoul','88','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-89','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'G','Iron Valiant ex','89','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-9','Kariya',NULL,NULL,2,'Bounsweet','Steenee spreads a sweet scent that makes others feel invigorated. This same scent is popular for antiperspirants.',90,'G','Steenee','9','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-90','Shiburingaru',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'It rapidly bores through the ground at 50 mph by squirming and twisting its massive, rugged body.',120,'G','Onix','90','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-91','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It flies straight at its target\'s face, then clamps down on the startled victim to inject poison.',70,'G','Gligar','91','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-92','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,'Gligar','Its flight is soundless. It uses its lengthy tail to carry off its prey... Then its elongated fangs do the rest.',120,'G','Gliscor','92','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-93','Uta',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'This legendary Pokémon is said to represent the land. It went to sleep after dueling Kyogre.',130,'G','Groudon','93','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-94','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It skulks in caves, and when prey or an enemy passes by, it leaps out and chomps them. The force of its attack sometimes chips its teeth.',70,'G','Gible','94','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-95','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,1,'Gible','In rare cases, it molts and sheds its scales. Medicine containing its scales as an ingredient will make a weary body feel invigorated.',100,'G','Gabite','95','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-96','Natsumi Yoshida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though small, Mienfoo\'s temperament is fierce. Any creature that approaches Mienfoo carelessly will be greeted with a flurry of graceful attacks.',60,'G','Mienfoo','96','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4-97','Mousho',NULL,NULL,1,'Mienfoo','Delivered at blinding speeds, kicks from this Pokémon can shatter massive boulders into tiny pieces.',100,'G','Mienshao','97','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4-98','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'G','Hoopa ex','98','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4-99','OKUBO',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This is its form when its shell has fallen off. The color of its core depends on the materials that made up the food it ate.',70,'G','Minior','99','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-1','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It likes to make its shell thicker by adding layers of tree bark. The additional weight doesn\'t bother it.',70,'G','Pineco','1','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-10','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,3,'Magmar','Living in the crater of a volcano has caused this Pokémon\'s body to resemble its environment— it has an organ similar to a magma chamber.',140,'G','Magmortar','10','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-100','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'During cold seasons, it migrates to the mountain\'s lower reaches. It returns to the snow-covered summit in the spring.',90,'G','Snover','100','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-101','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,3,'Snover','It lives a quiet life on mountains that are perpetually covered in snow. It hides itself by whipping up blizzards.',150,'G','Abomasnow','101','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-102','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It protects itself from enemies by emitting oil from the fruit on its head. This oil is bitter and astringent enough to make someone flinch.',60,'G','Smoliv','102','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-103','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,'Smoliv','Dolliv shares its tasty, fresh-scented oil with others. This species has coexisted with humans since times long gone.',90,'G','Dolliv','103','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-104','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Dolliv','This calm Pokémon is very compassionate. It will share its delicious, nutrient-rich oil with weakened Pokémon.',150,'G','Arboliva','104','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-105','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though it looks like Tentacool, Toedscool is a completely different species. Its legs may be thin, but it can run at a speed of 30 mph.',50,'G','Toedscool','105','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-106','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Traditional Paldean dishes can be extremely spicy because they include the shed front teeth of Capsakid among their ingredients.',70,'G','Capsakid','106','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-107','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Capsakid','The red head converts spicy chemicals into fire energy and blasts the surrounding area with a super spicy stream of flame.',110,'G','Scovillain','107','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-108','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon creates a mud ball by mixing sand and dirt with psychic energy. It treasures its mud ball more than its own life.',50,'G','Rellor','108','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-109','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'From the time it is born, a flame burns at the tip of its tail. Its life would end if the flame were to go out.',70,'G','Charmander','109','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-11','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Magma of almost 2,200 degrees Fahrenheit courses through its body. When it grows cold, the magma hardens and slows it.',80,'G','Numel','11','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-110','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Charmander','If it becomes agitated during battle, it spouts intense flames, incinerating its surroundings.',90,'G','Charmeleon','110','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-111','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'People call this kind of Tauros the Blaze Breed due to the hot air it snorts from its nostrils. Its three tails are intertwined.',130,'G','Paldean Tauros','111','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-112','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It is said that when it roars, a volcano erupts somewhere around the globe.',130,'G','Entei','112','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-113','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is incredibly popular, possibly because its passionate dancing is a great match with the temperament of Paldean people.',90,'G','Oricorio','113','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-114','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Burnt charcoal came to life and became a Pokémon. Possessing a fiery fighting spirit, Charcadet will battle even tough opponents.',70,'G','Charcadet','114','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-115','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Charcadet','Armarouge evolved through the use of a set of armor that belonged to a distinguished warrior. This Pokémon is incredibly loyal.',130,'G','Armarouge','115','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-116','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It is always vacantly lost in thought, but no one knows what it is thinking about. It is good at fishing with its tail.',70,'G','Slowpoke','116','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-117','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,3,'Slowpoke','If the tail-biting Shellder is thrown off in a harsh battle, this Pokémon reverts to being an ordinary Slowpoke.',100,'G','Slowbro','117','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-118','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Fish Pokémon nibble at it, but Staryu isn\'t bothered. Its body regenerates quickly, even if part of it is completely torn off.',60,'G','Staryu','118','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-119','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,'Staryu','Starmie swims by spinning its body at high speed. As this Pokémon cruises through the ocean, it absorbs tiny plankton.',90,'G','Starmie','119','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-12','satoma',NULL,NULL,3,'Numel','It lives in the crater of a volcano. It is well known that the humps on its back erupt every 10 years.',130,'G','Camerupt','12','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-120','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It swims by jetting water from its horns. The most notable characteristic of the Aqua Breed is its high body fat, which allows it to float easily.',130,'G','Paldean Tauros','120','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-121','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand.',50,'G','Wiglett','121','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-122','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,2,'Wiglett','It has a vicious temperament, contrary to what its appearance may suggest. It wraps its long bodies around prey, then drags the prey into its den.',90,'G','Wugtrio','122','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-123','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It likes playing with others of its kind using the water ring on its tail. It uses ultrasonic waves to sense the emotions of other living creatures.',50,'G','Finizen','123','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-124','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Finizen','This Pokémon\'s ancient genes have awakened. It is now so extraordinarily strong that it can easily lift a cruise ship with one fin.',150,'G','Palafin','124','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-125','Nelnal',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'When Veluza discards unnecessary flesh, its mind becomes honed and its psychic power increases. The spare flesh has a mild but delicious flavor.',130,'G','Veluza','125','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-126','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'This Pokémon is a glutton, but it\'s bad at getting food. It teams up with a Tatsugiri to catch prey.',160,'G','Dondozo','126','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-127','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This is a small dragon Pokémon. It lives inside the mouth of Dondozo to protect itself from enemies on the outside.',70,'G','Tatsugiri','127','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-128','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Frigibax absorbs heat through its dorsal fin and converts the heat into ice energy. The higher the temperature, the more energy Frigibax stores.',70,'G','Frigibax','128','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-129','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Frigibax','Arctibax freezes the air around it, protecting its face with an ice mask and turning its dorsal fin into a blade of ice.',90,'G','Arctibax','129','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-13','Scav',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'If the convection microwave oven is not working properly, then the Rotom inhabiting it will become lethargic.',90,'G','Heat Rotom','13','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-130','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,'Arctibax','This Pokémon blasts cryogenic air out from its mouth. This air can instantly freeze even liquid-hot lava.',160,'G','Baxcalibur','130','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-131','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'﻿When it is angered, it immediately discharges the energy stored in the pouches in its cheeks.',70,'G','Pikachu','131','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-132','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,1,'Pikachu','Its tail discharges electricity into the ground, protecting it from getting shocked.',120,'G','Raichu','132','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-133','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It rolls to move. If the ground is uneven, a sudden jolt from hitting a bump can cause it to explode.',60,'G','Voltorb','133','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-134','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,'Voltorb','The more energy it charges up, the faster it gets. But this also makes it more likely to explode.',90,'G','Electrode','134','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-135','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The extension and contraction of its muscles generates electricity. It glows when in trouble.',70,'G','Shinx','135','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-136','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,'Shinx','Strong electricity courses through the tips of its sharp claws. A light scratch causes fainting in foes.',90,'G','Luxio','136','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-137','kantaro',NULL,NULL,1,'Luxio','It can see clearly through walls to track down its prey and seek its lost young.',150,'G','Luxray','137','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-138','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A pair may be seen rubbing their cheek pouches together in an effort to share stored electricity.',70,'G','Pachirisu','138','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-139','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'As it flies around, it shoots lightning all over the place and causes forest fires. It is therefore disliked.',110,'G','Thundurus','139','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-14','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Burnt charcoal came to life and became a Pokémon. Possessing a fiery fighting spirit, Charcadet will battle even tough opponents.',70,'G','Charcadet','14','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-140','Lee HyunJung',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has no problem drinking dirty water. An organ inside Toxel\'s body filters such water into a poisonous liquid that is harmless to Toxel.',70,'G','Toxel','140','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-141','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,2,'Toxel','Many youths admire the way this Pokémon listlessly picks fights and keeps its cool no matter what opponent it faces.',140,'G','Toxtricity','141','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-142','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The pads of its paws are electricity-discharging organs. Pawmi fires electricity from its forepaws while standing unsteadily on its hind legs.',60,'G','Pawmi','142','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-143','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,'Pawmi','Pawmo uses a unique fighting technique in which it uses its forepaws to strike foes and zap them with electricity from its paw pads simultaneously.',90,'G','Pawmo','143','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-144','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Pawmo','Pawmot\'s fluffy fur acts as a battery. It can store the same amount of electricity as an electric car.',130,'G','Pawmot','144','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-145','Scav',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When its wings catch the wind, the bones within produce electricity. This Pokémon dives into the ocean, catching prey by electrocuting them.',60,'G','Wattrel','145','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-146','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wattrel','Kilowattrel inflates its throat sac to amplify its electricity. By riding the wind, this Pokémon can fly over 430 miles in a day.',120,'G','Kilowattrel','146','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-147','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Jigglypuff','It has a very fine fur. Take care not to make it angry, or it may inflate steadily and hit with a body slam.',110,'G','Wigglytuff','147','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-148','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Abra can teleport in its sleep. Apparently the more deeply Abra sleeps, the farther its teleportations go.',50,'G','Abra','148','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-149','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,'Abra','This Pokémon\'s telekinesis is immensely powerful. To prepare for evolution, Kadabra stores up psychic energy in the star on its forehead.',80,'G','Kadabra','149','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-15','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,2,'Charcadet','Armarouge evolved through the use of a set of armor that belonged to a distinguished warrior. This Pokémon is incredibly loyal.',130,'G','Armarouge','15','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-150','Mizue',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Because of its unusual, starlike silhouette, people believe that it came here on a meteor.',30,'G','Cleffa','150','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-151','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Because its wings aren\'t yet fully grown, it has to hop to get around. It is always staring at something.',50,'G','Natu','151','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-152','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,'Natu','This odd Pokémon can see both the past and the future. It eyes the sun\'s movement all day.',100,'G','Xatu','152','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-153','yuu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The horns on its head provide a strong power that enables it to sense people\'s emotions.',70,'G','Ralts','153','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-154','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,1,'Ralts','It has a psychic power that enables it to distort the space around it and see into the future.',90,'G','Kirlia','154','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-155','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is whispered that any child who mistakes Drifloon for a balloon and holds on to it could wind up missing.',70,'G','Drifloon','155','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-156','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,'Drifloon','It can generate and release gas within its body. That\'s how it can control the altitude of its drift.',110,'G','Drifblim','156','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-157','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'In an attempt to confuse its enemy, it mimics the enemy\'s movements. Then it wastes no time in making itself scarce!',30,'G','Mime Jr.','157','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-158','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its constant mischief and misdeeds resulted in it being bound to an Odd Keystone by a mysterious spell.',60,'G','Spiritomb','158','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-159','yuu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'In the past, noble families entrusted their vault keys to a Klefki. They passed the Klefki down through the generations, taking good care of it.',70,'G','Klefki','159','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-16','Gemi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Crossing icy seas is no issue for this cold-resistant Pokémon. Its smooth skin is a little cool to the touch.',110,'G','Lapras','16','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-160','Nelnal',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon lives in dark places untouched by sunlight. When it appears before humans, it hides itself under a cloth that resembles a Pikachu.',70,'G','Mimikyu','160','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-161','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,1,'Fidough','The pleasant aroma that emanates from this Pokémon\'s body helps wheat grow, so Dachsbun has been treasured by farming villages.',90,'G','Dachsbun','161','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-162','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Charcadet','The fiery blades on its arms burn fiercely with the lingering resentment of a sword wielder who fell before accomplishing their goal.',140,'G','Ceruledge','162','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-163','Nelnal',NULL,NULL,1,'Rellor','The body that supports the ball barely moves. Therefore, it is thought that the true body of this Pokémon is actually inside the ball.',70,'G','Rabsca','163','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-164','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Flittle\'s toes levitate about half an inch above the ground because of the psychic power emitted from the frills on the Pokémon\'s belly.',30,'G','Flittle','164','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-165','yuu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It swings its handmade hammer around to protect itself, but the hammer is often stolen by Pokémon that eat metal.',60,'G','Tinkatink','165','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-166','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,2,'Tinkatink','This Pokémon will attack groups of Pawniard and Bisharp, gathering metal from them in order to create a large and sturdy hammer.',90,'G','Tinkatuff','166','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-167','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Tinkatuff','This intelligent Pokémon has a very daring disposition. It knocks rocks into the sky with its hammer, aiming for flying Corviknight.',140,'G','Tinkaton','167','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-168','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,'Greavard','A lovingly mourned Pokémon was reborn as Houndstone. It doesn\'t like anyone touching the protuberance atop its head.',140,'G','Houndstone','168','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-169','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is extremely quick to anger. It could be docile one moment, then thrashing away the next instant.',60,'G','Mankey','169','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-17','rika',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Frigibax absorbs heat through its dorsal fin and converts the heat into ice energy. The higher the temperature, the more energy Frigibax stores.',70,'G','Frigibax','17','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-170','Scav',NULL,NULL,1,'Mankey','Some researchers theorize that Primeape remains angry even when inside a Poké Ball.',90,'G','Primeape','170','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-171','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,2,'Primeape','It imbues its fists with the power of the rage that it kept hidden in its heart. Opponents struck by these imbued fists will be shattered to their core.',140,'G','Annihilape','171','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-172','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This kind of Tauros, known as the Combat Breed, is distinguished by its thick, powerful muscles and its fierce disposition.',130,'G','Paldean Tauros','172','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-173','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They communicate with one another using their auras. They are able to run all through the night.',70,'G','Riolu','173','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-174','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Riolu','It\'s said that no foe can remain invisible to Lucario, since it can detect auras—even those of foes it could not otherwise see.',130,'G','Lucario','174','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-175','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its elegant finishing moves—performed by nimbly leaping around using its wings—are polished in the forest where it was born and raised.',70,'G','Hawlucha','175','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-176','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It was born in a layer of rock salt deep under the earth. This species was particularly treasured in the old days, as they would share precious salt.',70,'G','Nacli','176','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-177','otumami',NULL,NULL,3,'Nacli','This Pokémon dry cures its prey by spraying salt over them. The curing process steals away the water in the prey\'s body.',100,'G','Naclstack','177','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-178','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,3,'Naclstack','Garganacl will rub its fingertips together and sprinkle injured Pokémon with salt. Even severe wounds will promptly heal afterward.',180,'G','Garganacl','178','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-179','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It absorbs nutrients from cave walls. The petals it wears are made of crystallized poison.',40,'G','Glimmet','179','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-18','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'﻿When it is angered, it immediately discharges the energy stored in the pouches in its cheeks.',70,'G','Pikachu','18','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-180','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'After losing a territorial struggle, Wooper began living on land. The Pokémon changed over time, developing a poisonous film to protect its body.',60,'G','Paldean Wooper','180','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-181','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Feared and loathed by many, it is believed to bring misfortune to all those who see it at night.',60,'G','Murkrow','181','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-182','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This cunning Pokémon hides under the cover of darkness, waiting to attack its prey.',70,'G','Sneasel','182','Shiny Rare','Pokémon');
INSERT INTO `card` VALUES ('sv4pt5-183','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,'Sneasel','Evolution made it even more devious. It communicates by clawing signs in boulders.',110,'G','Weavile','183','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-184','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It dwells in the darkness of caves. It uses its sharp claws to dig up gems to nourish itself.',70,'G','Sableye','184','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-185','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Pawniard will fearlessly challenge even powerful foes. In a pinch, it will cling to opponents and pierce them with the blades all over its body.',70,'G','Pawniard','185','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-186','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,'Pawniard','This Pokémon commands a group of several Pawniard. Groups that are defeated in territorial disputes are absorbed by the winning side.',120,'G','Bisharp','186','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-187','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,'Bisharp','Only a Bisharp that stands above all others in its vast army can evolve into Kingambit.',170,'G','Kingambit','187','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-188','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,3,'Maschiff','Mabosstiff loves playing with children. Though usually gentle, it takes on an intimidating look when protecting its family.',130,'G','Mabosstiff','188','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-189','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though usually a mellow Pokémon, it will sink its sharp, poison-soaked front teeth into any that anger it, causing paralysis in the object of its ire.',50,'G','Shroodle','189','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-19','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,'Pikachu','Its tail discharges electricity into the ground, protecting it from getting shocked.',120,'G','Raichu','19','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-190','Scav',NULL,NULL,1,'Shroodle','The color of the poisonous saliva depends on what the Pokémon eats. Grafaiai covers its fingers in its saliva and draws patterns on trees in forests.',90,'G','Grafaiai','190','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-191','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,'Scyther','This Pokémon\'s pincers, which contain steel, can crush any hard object they get ahold of into bits.',140,'G','Scizor','191','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-192','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is said that this Pokémon was born when an unknown poison Pokémon entered and inspirited an engine left at a scrap-processing factory.',60,'G','Varoom','192','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-193','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,'Varoom','It creates a gas out of poison and minerals from rocks. It then detonates the gas in its cylinders— now numbering eight—to generate energy.',140,'G','Revavroom','193','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-194','Nelnal',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon emits ultrasonic waves from its large ears to search for fruit to eat. It mistakes Applin for its food.',70,'G','Noibat','194','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-195','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Apparently Cyclizar has been allowing people to ride on its back since ancient times. Depictions of this have been found in 10,000-year-old murals.',120,'G','Cyclizar','195','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-196','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is docile and prefers to avoid conflict. If disturbed, however, it can ferociously strike back.',50,'G','Pidgey','196','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-197','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Pidgey','Very protective of its sprawling territorial area, this Pokémon will fiercely peck at any intruder.',80,'G','Pidgeotto','197','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-198','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When its huge eyes waver, it sings a mysteriously soothing melody that lulls its enemies to sleep.',70,'G','Jigglypuff','198','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-199','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The brains in its two heads appear to communicate emotions to each other with a telepathic power.',70,'G','Doduo','199','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-2','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Pineco',NULL,270,'G','Forretress ex','2','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-20','yuu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'On the dark ocean floor, its only means of communication is its constantly flashing lights.',60,'G','Chinchou','20','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-200','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,'Doduo','An odd species that is rarely found. The three heads respectively represent joy, sadness, and anger.',100,'G','Dodrio','200','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-201','0313',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its transformation ability is perfect. However, if made to laugh, it can\'t maintain its disguise.',60,'G','Ditto','201','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-202','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'This Pokémon\'s stomach is so strong, even eating moldy or rotten food will not affect it.',150,'G','Snorlax','202','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-203','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It soars high in the sky, riding on updrafts like a glider. It carries food tucked in its bill.',70,'G','Wingull','203','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-204','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,2,'Wingull','It is a flying transporter that carries small Pokémon in its beak. It bobs on the waves to rest its wings.',120,'G','Pelipper','204','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-205','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'No matter how much it stuffs its belly with food, it is always anxious about getting hungry again. So, it stashes berries in its cheeks and tail.',60,'G','Skwovet','205','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-206','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Skwovet','This Pokémon makes off with heaps of fallen berries by wrapping them in its tail, which is roughly twice the length of its body.',120,'G','Greedent','206','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-207','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It searches for food all day. It possesses a keen sense of smell but doesn\'t use it for anything other than foraging.',70,'G','Lechonk','207','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-208','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,2,'Lechonk','This Pokémon sends a flowerlike scent wafting about. Well-developed muscles in its legs allow it to leap more than 16 feet with no trouble at all.',130,'G','Oinkologne','208','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-209','Lee HyunJung',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Exhibiting great teamwork, they use their incisors to cut pieces out of any material that might be useful for a nest, then make off with them.',30,'G','Tandemaus','209','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-21','aspara',NULL,NULL,2,'Chinchou','This Pokémon flashes a bright light that blinds its prey. This creates an opening for it to deliver an electrical attack.',120,'G','Lanturn','21','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-210','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,'Tandemaus','The larger pair protects the little ones during battles. When facing strong opponents, the whole group will join the fight.',70,'G','Maushold','210','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-211','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon apparently ties the base of its neck into a knot so that energy stored in its belly does not escape from its beak.',110,'G','Flamigo','211','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-212','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Pineco',NULL,270,'G','Forretress ex','212','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-213','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Toedscool',NULL,270,'G','Toedscruel ex','213','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-214','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,1,'Flittle',NULL,260,'G','Espathra ex','214','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-215','PLANETA Tsuji',NULL,NULL,1,'Kadabra',NULL,310,'G','Alakazam ex','215','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-216','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,180,'G','Mew ex','216','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-217','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,2,'Kirlia',NULL,310,'G','Gardevoir ex','217','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-218','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Glimmet',NULL,270,'G','Glimmora ex','218','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-219','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,3,'Paldean Wooper',NULL,280,'G','Paldean Clodsire ex','219','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-22','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wattrel','Kilowattrel inflates its throat sac to amplify its electricity. By riding the wind, this Pokémon can fly over 430 miles in a day.',120,'G','Kilowattrel','22','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-220','Eske Yoshinob',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Noibat',NULL,260,'G','Noivern ex','220','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-221','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Pidgeotto',NULL,280,'G','Pidgeot ex','221','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-222','Saki Hayashiro',NULL,NULL,3,'Jigglypuff',NULL,250,'G','Wigglytuff ex','222','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-223','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,160,'G','Squawkabilly ex','223','Shiny Ultra Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-224','Tetsu Kayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Wiglett','It has a vicious temperament, contrary to what its appearance may suggest. It wraps its long bodies around prey, then drags the prey into its den.',90,'G','Wugtrio','224','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-225','akagi',NULL,NULL,2,'Finizen','This Pokémon\'s ancient genes have awakened. It is now so extraordinarily strong that it can easily lift a cruise ship with one fin.',150,'G','Palafin','225','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-226','REND',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The pads of its paws are electricity-discharging organs. Pawmi fires electricity from its forepaws while standing unsteadily on its hind legs.',60,'G','Pawmi','226','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-227','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Clive','227','Ultra Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-228','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Judge','228','Ultra Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-229','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Nemona','229','Ultra Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-23','Kariya',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'These Pokémon get nervous when they\'re not in a group of six. The minute even one member of the group goes missing, Exeggcute become cowardly.',60,'G','Exeggcute','23','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-230','Cona Nitanda',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Paldean Student','230','Ultra Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-231','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Paldean Student','231','Ultra Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-232','USGMEN',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,180,'G','Mew ex','232','Special Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-233','Kuroimori',NULL,NULL,2,'Kirlia',NULL,310,'G','Gardevoir ex','233','Special Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-234','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,2,'Charmeleon',NULL,330,'G','Charizard ex','234','Special Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-235','aspara',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Arven','235','Special Illustration Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-236','Taiga Kayama',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Clive','236','Special Illustration Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-237','hanabushi',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Iono','237','Special Illustration Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-238','aspara',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Nemona','238','Special Illustration Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-239','aspara',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Penny','239','Special Illustration Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-24','Yoriyuki Ikegami',NULL,NULL,2,'Exeggcute','When they work together, Exeggutor\'s three heads can put out powerful psychic energy. Cloudy days make this Pokémon sluggish.',130,'G','Exeggutor','24','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-240','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,230,'G','Wo-Chien ex','240','Hyper Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-241','PLANETA Yamashita',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,190,'G','Chi-Yu ex','241','Hyper Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-242','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'G','Chien-Pao ex','242','Hyper Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-243','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,220,'G','Miraidon ex','243','Hyper Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-244','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,240,'G','Ting-Lu ex','244','Hyper Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-245','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,230,'G','Koraidon ex','245','Hyper Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-25','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Because its wings aren\'t yet fully grown, it has to hop to get around. It is always staring at something.',50,'G','Natu','25','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-26','DOM',NULL,NULL,1,'Natu','This odd Pokémon can see both the past and the future. It eyes the sun\'s movement all day.',100,'G','Xatu','26','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-27','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The horns on its head provide a strong power that enables it to sense people\'s emotions.',70,'G','Ralts','27','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-28','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,'Ralts','It has a psychic power that enables it to distort the space around it and see into the future.',90,'G','Kirlia','28','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-29','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,2,'Kirlia',NULL,310,'G','Gardevoir ex','29','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-3','Masako Tomii',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Once each year, this Pokémon scatters its seeds. They\'re jam-packed with nutrients, making them a precious food source out in the desert.',110,'G','Maractus','3','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-30','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Emitting ultrasonic cries, it floats on winds to travel great distances.',70,'G','Chimecho','30','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-31','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'In an attempt to confuse its enemy, it mimics the enemy\'s movements. Then it wastes no time in making itself scarce!',30,'G','Mime Jr.','31','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-32','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It emits ultrasonic waves as it flutters about, searching for its prey—bug Pokémon.',60,'G','Woobat','32','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-33','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,'Woobat','The auspicious shape of this Pokémon\'s nose apparently led some regions to consider Swoobat a symbol of good luck.',90,'G','Swoobat','33','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-34','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Weaving together the cotton of both Cottonee and Eldegoss produces exquisite cloth that\'s highly prized by many luxury brands.',60,'G','Cottonee','34','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-35','KYUPIYAMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Cottonee','As long as this Pokémon bathes in sunlight, its cotton keeps growing. If too much cotton fluff builds up, Whimsicott tears it off and scatters it.',90,'G','Whimsicott','35','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-36','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s small and its electricity-generating organ is not fully developed, so it uses its tail to absorb electricity from people\'s homes and charge itself.',70,'G','Dedenne','36','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-37','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon lives in dark places untouched by sunlight. When it appears before humans, it hides itself under a cloth that resembles a Pikachu.',70,'G','Mimikyu','37','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-38','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is smooth and moist to the touch. Yeast in Fidough\'s breath induces fermentation in the Pokémon\'s vicinity.',50,'G','Fidough','38','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-39','You Iribi',NULL,NULL,1,'Fidough','The pleasant aroma that emanates from this Pokémon\'s body helps wheat grow, so Dachsbun has been treasured by farming villages.',90,'G','Dachsbun','39','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-4','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though it looks like Tentacool, Toedscool is a completely different species. Its legs may be thin, but it can run at a speed of 30 mph.',50,'G','Toedscool','4','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-40','Ryota Murayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Charcadet','The fiery blades on its arms burn fiercely with the lingering resentment of a sword wielder who fell before accomplishing their goal.',140,'G','Ceruledge','40','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-41','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Flittle\'s toes levitate about half an inch above the ground because of the psychic power emitted from the frills on the Pokémon\'s belly.',30,'G','Flittle','41','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-42','yuu',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This friendly Pokémon doesn\'t like being alone. Pay it even the slightest bit of attention, and it will follow you forever.',70,'G','Greavard','42','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-43','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,3,'Greavard','A lovingly mourned Pokémon was reborn as Houndstone. It doesn\'t like anyone touching the protuberance atop its head.',140,'G','Houndstone','43','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-44','OKUBO',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon was born inside a treasure chest about 1,500 years ago. It sucks the life-force out of scoundrels who try to steal the treasure.',50,'G','Gimmighoul','44','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-45','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is extremely quick to anger. It could be docile one moment, then thrashing away the next instant.',60,'G','Mankey','45','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-46','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,1,'Mankey','Some researchers theorize that Primeape remains angry even when inside a Poké Ball.',90,'G','Primeape','46','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-47','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,'Primeape','It imbues its fists with the power of the rage that it kept hidden in its heart. Opponents struck by these imbued fists will be shattered to their core.',140,'G','Annihilape','47','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-48','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon lives and nests on a riverbank. After playing in the mud, it won\'t be able to settle down unless it washes its body.',80,'G','Phanpy','48','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-49','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,'Phanpy','Donphan is covered in tough hide, so even being hit by a car won\'t faze this Pokémon. However, it is extremely susceptible to rain.',150,'G','Donphan','49','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-5','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Toedscool',NULL,270,'G','Toedscruel ex','5','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-50','ryoma uratsuka',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its two whiskers provide a sensitive radar. Even in muddy waters, it can detect its prey\'s location.',70,'G','Barboach','50','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-51','Kedamahadaitai Yawarakai',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its tentacles tear off easily, but it isn\'t alarmed when that happens—it knows they\'ll grow back. It\'s about as smart as a three-year-old.',70,'G','Clobbopus','51','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-52','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,2,'Clobbopus','Searching for an opponent to test its skills against, it emerges onto land. Once the battle is over, it returns to the sea.',120,'G','Grapploct','52','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-53','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,250,'G','Great Tusk ex','53','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-54','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Charmeleon',NULL,330,'G','Charizard ex','54','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-55','Nobuhiro Imagawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It wraps its opponent in its gas-like body, slowly weakening its prey by poisoning it through the skin.',50,'G','Gastly','55','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-56','DOM',NULL,NULL,1,'Gastly','It likes to lurk in the dark and tap shoulders with a gaseous hand. Its touch causes endless shuddering.',80,'G','Haunter','56','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-57','Nelnal',NULL,NULL,1,'Haunter','To steal the life of its target, it slips into the prey\'s shadow and silently waits for an opportunity.',130,'G','Gengar','57','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-58','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'After losing a territorial struggle, Wooper began living on land. The Pokémon changed over time, developing a poisonous film to protect its body.',60,'G','Paldean Wooper','58','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-59','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,3,'Paldean Wooper',NULL,280,'G','Paldean Clodsire ex','59','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-6','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,1,'Flittle',NULL,260,'G','Espathra ex','6','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-60','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It protects itself with its durable skin. It\'s thought that this Pokémon will evolve once its skin has completely stretched out.',70,'G','Scraggy','60','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-61','Mousho',NULL,NULL,2,'Scraggy','While mostly known for having the temperament of an aggressive ruffian, this Pokémon takes very good care of its family, friends, and territory.',120,'G','Scrafty','61','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-62','DOM',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It always scowls in an attempt to make opponents take it seriously, but even crying children will burst into laughter when they see Maschiff\'s face.',60,'G','Maschiff','62','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-63','KIYOTAKA OSHIYAMA',NULL,NULL,3,'Maschiff','Mabosstiff loves playing with children. Though usually gentle, it takes on an intimidating look when protecting its family.',130,'G','Mabosstiff','63','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-64','Tetsu Kayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is said that this Pokémon was born when an unknown poison Pokémon entered and inspirited an engine left at a scrap-processing factory.',60,'G','Varoom','64','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-65','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,'Varoom','It creates a gas out of poison and minerals from rocks. It then detonates the gas in its cylinders— now numbering eight—to generate energy.',140,'G','Revavroom','65','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-66','toriyufu',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,220,'G','Iron Treads ex','66','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-67','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,'Gimmighoul','Its body seems to be made up of 1,000 coins. This Pokémon gets along well with others and is quick to make friends with anybody.',130,'G','Gholdengo','67','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-68','chibi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon emits ultrasonic waves from its large ears to search for fruit to eat. It mistakes Applin for its food.',70,'G','Noibat','68','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-69','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Noibat',NULL,260,'G','Noivern ex','69','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-7','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'From the time it is born, a flame burns at the tip of its tail. Its life would end if the flame were to go out.',70,'G','Charmander','7','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-70','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Apparently Cyclizar has been allowing people to ride on its back since ancient times. Depictions of this have been found in 10,000-year-old murals.',120,'G','Cyclizar','70','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-71','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It searches for food all day. It possesses a keen sense of smell but doesn\'t use it for anything other than foraging.',70,'G','Lechonk','71','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-72','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Lechonk','This Pokémon sends a flowerlike scent wafting about. Well-developed muscles in its legs allow it to leap more than 16 feet with no trouble at all.',130,'G','Oinkologne','72','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-73','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Exhibiting great teamwork, they use their incisors to cut pieces out of any material that might be useful for a nest, then make off with them.',30,'G','Tandemaus','73','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-74','KIYOTAKA OSHIYAMA',NULL,NULL,1,'Tandemaus','The larger pair protects the little ones during battles. When facing strong opponents, the whole group will join the fight.',70,'G','Maushold','74','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-75','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,160,'G','Squawkabilly ex','75','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-76','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Artazon','76','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-77','kantaro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Atticus','77','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-78','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Clive','78','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-79','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Electric Generator','79','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-8','Tonji Matsuno',NULL,NULL,2,'Charmander','If it becomes agitated during battle, it spouts intense flames, incinerating its surroundings.',90,'G','Charmeleon','8','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-80','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Iono','80','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-81','AYUMI ODASHIMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Moonlit Hill','81','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-82','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Nemona','82','Common','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-83','AYUMI ODASHIMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Nemona\'s Backpack','83','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-84','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Nest Ball','84','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-85','Cona Nitanda',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Paldean Student','85','Common','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-86','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Paldean Student','86','Common','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-87','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Professor\'s Research','87','Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-88','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Professor\'s Research','88','Rare','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-89','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Rare Candy','89','Common','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-9','miki kudo',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'These Pokémon\'s bodies are constantly burning. Magmar are feared as one of the causes behind fires.',80,'G','Magmar','9','Common','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-90','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Technical Machine: Crisis Punch','90','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-91','Ayaka Yoshida',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'G','Ultra Ball','91','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv4pt5-92','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'During the day, it stays in the cold underground to avoid the sun. It grows by bathing in moonlight.',60,'G','Oddish','92','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-93','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,1,'Oddish','What appears to be drool is actually sweet honey. It is very sticky and clings stubbornly if touched.',70,'G','Gloom','93','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-94','0313',NULL,NULL,2,'Gloom','The larger its petals, the more toxic pollen it contains. Its big head is heavy and hard to hold up.',140,'G','Vileplume','94','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-95','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It slashes through grass with its sharp scythes, moving too fast for the human eye to track.',80,'G','Scyther','95','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-96','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is blown across vast distances by the wind. It is unclear where the Hoppip of Paldea originally came from.',50,'G','Hoppip','96','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-97','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,'Hoppip','Skiploom enthusiasts can apparently tell where a Skiploom was born by the scent drifting from the flower on the Pokémon\'s head.',70,'G','Skiploom','97','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-98','Lee HyunJung',NULL,NULL,1,'Skiploom','Jumpluff travels on seasonal winds. Once its cotton spores run out, its journey ends, as does its life.',90,'G','Jumpluff','98','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv4pt5-99','Scav',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It likes to make its shell thicker by adding layers of tree bark. The additional weight doesn\'t bother it.',70,'G','Pineco','99','Shiny Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-1','Dsuke',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The sharp scythes on its forearms become increasingly sharp by cutting through hard objects.',90,'H','Scyther','1','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-10','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Photosynthesis occurs across its body under the sun. The shell on its back is actually hardened soil.',80,'H','Turtwig','10','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-100','Shimaris Yukichi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The older it gets, the longer it grows. At night, it wraps its long body around tree branches to rest.',60,'H','Ekans','100','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-101','Minato',NULL,NULL,2,'Ekans','The pattern on its belly appears to be a frightening face. Weak foes will flee just at the sight of the pattern.',130,'H','Arbok','101','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-102','Fujimoto Gold',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It wraps its opponent in its gas-like body, slowly weakening its prey by poisoning it through the skin.',60,'H','Gastly','102','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-103','MAHOU',NULL,NULL,1,'Gastly','It likes to lurk in the dark and tap shoulders with a gaseous hand. Its touch causes endless shuddering.',90,'H','Haunter','103','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-104','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,2,'Haunter',NULL,310,'H','Gengar ex','104','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-105','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A Pokémon with a persistent nature, it chases its chosen prey until the prey becomes exhausted.',70,'H','Poochyena','105','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-106','akagi',NULL,NULL,2,'Poochyena','It will always obey the commands of a skilled Trainer. Its behavior arises from its living in packs in ancient times.',120,'H','Mightyena','106','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-107','0313',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It dwells in the darkness of caves. It uses its sharp claws to dig up gems to nourish itself.',70,'H','Sableye','107','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-108','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Girafarig',NULL,260,'H','Farigiraf ex','108','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-109','hncl',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It is possible that this is the creature listed as Roaring Moon in an expedition journal that still holds many mysteries.',140,'H','Roaring Moon','109','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-11','Uninori',NULL,NULL,4,'Turtwig','It lives along water in forests. In the daytime, it leaves the forest to sunbathe its treed shell.',120,'H','Grotle','11','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-110','osare',NULL,NULL,3,'Pineco','Its entire body is shielded by a steel-hard shell. What lurks inside this shell is a total mystery.',130,'H','Forretress','110','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-111','toriyufu',NULL,NULL,2,'Scyther',NULL,270,'H','Scizor ex','111','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-112','aspara',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It uses its docile-looking face to lull foes into complacency, then bites with its huge, relentless jaws.',90,'H','Mawile','112','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-113','hatachu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'From its rear, Beldum emits a magnetic force that rapidly pulls opponents in. They get skewered on Beldum\'s sharp claws.',70,'H','Beldum','113','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-114','Nobuhiro Imagawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Beldum','Two Beldum have become stuck together via their own magnetic forces. With two brains, the resulting Metang has doubled psychic powers.',100,'H','Metang','114','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-115','Nurikabe',NULL,NULL,3,'Metang','Because the magnetic powers of these Pokémon get stronger in freezing temperatures, Metagross living on snowy mountains are full of energy.',180,'H','Metagross','115','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-116','Taiga Kayama',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It dissolves and eats metal. Circulating liquid metal within its body is how it generates energy.',80,'H','Meltan','116','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-117','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,4,'Meltan','At the end of its life-span, Melmetal will rust and fall apart. The small shards left behind will eventually be reborn as Meltan.',160,'H','Melmetal','117','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-118','Tonji Matsuno',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Sightings of this Pokémon have occurred in recent years. It resembles a mysterious object described in an old expedition journal.',130,'H','Iron Treads','118','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-119','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This seems to be the Winged King mentioned in an old expedition journal. It was said to have split the land with its bare fists.',140,'H','Koraidon','119','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-12','PLANETA Tsuji',NULL,NULL,4,'Grotle',NULL,340,'H','Torterra ex','12','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-120','PLANETA Igarashi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,230,'H','Koraidon ex','120','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-121','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This seems to be the Iron Serpent mentioned in an old book. The Iron Serpent is said to have turned the land to ash with its lightning.',110,'H','Miraidon','121','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-122','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,220,'H','Miraidon ex','122','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-123','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,240,'H','Raging Bolt ex','123','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-124','nisimono',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'If this Pokémon\'s sticky saliva gets on you and you don\'t clean it off, an intense itch will set in. The itch won\'t go away, either.',100,'H','Lickitung','124','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-125','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,4,'Lickitung','Lickilicky\'s strange tongue can stretch to many times the length of its body. No one has figured out how Lickilicky\'s tongue can stretch so far.',150,'H','Lickilicky','125','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-126','ryoma uratsuka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It always stands on one foot. It changes feet so fast, the movement can rarely be seen.',70,'H','Hoothoot','126','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-127','toi8',NULL,NULL,1,'Hoothoot','Its eyes are specially developed to enable it to see clearly even in murky darkness and minimal light.',110,'H','Noctowl','127','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-128','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'It creates mazes in dark locations. When spotted, it flees into the ground by digging with its tail.',60,'H','Dunsparce','128','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-129','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,3,'Dunsparce','This Pokémon uses its hard tail to make its nest by boring holes into bedrock deep underground. The nest can reach lengths of over six miles.',140,'H','Dudunsparce','129','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-13','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'It can dissolve toxins in the air to instantly transform ruined land into a lush field of flowers.',70,'H','Shaymin','13','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-130','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It can\'t stop itself from chasing moving things, and it runs in a circle, chasing its own tail.',60,'H','Skitty','130','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-131','Keisin',NULL,NULL,1,'Skitty','It dislikes dirty places. It often searches for a comfortable place in which to groom itself.',110,'H','Delcatty','131','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-132','GOTO minori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It mimics the cries of other Pokémon to trick them into thinking it\'s one of them. This way they won\'t attack it.',70,'H','Chatot','132','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-133','Mékayu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Where people go, these Pokémon follow. If you\'re scattering food for them, be careful— several hundred of them can gather at once.',50,'H','Pidove','133','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-134','Pani Kobayashi',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Pidove','It can fly moderately quickly. No matter how far it travels, it can always find its way back to its master and its nest.',80,'H','Tranquill','134','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-135','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tranquill','Unfezant are exceptional fliers. The females are known for their stamina, while the males outclass them in terms of speed.',150,'H','Unfezant','135','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-136','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The way it brushes away grime with its tail can be helpful when cleaning. But its focus on spotlessness can make cleaning more of a hassle.',70,'H','Minccino','136','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-137','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,'Minccino','Its body secretes oil that this Pokémon spreads over its nest as a coating to protect it from dust. Cinccino won\'t tolerate even a speck of the stuff.',110,'H','Cinccino','137','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-138','Toshinao Aoki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The mountains it calls home are nearly two miles in height. On rare occasions, it descends to play with the children living in the towns below.',120,'H','Drampa','138','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-139','KEIICHIRO ITO',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It\'s possible that Iron Jugulis, an object described in an old book, may actually be this Pokémon.',130,'H','Iron Jugulis','139','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-14','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It shoots cotton from its body to protect itself. If it gets caught up in hurricane-strength winds, it can get sent to the other side of the Earth.',60,'H','Cottonee','14','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-140','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Ancient Booster Energy Capsule','140','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv5-141','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Awakening Drum','141','ACE SPEC Rare','Trainer'),('sv5-142','En Morikura',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Bianca\'s Devotion','142','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv5-143','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Boxed Order','143','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv5-144','AYUMI ODASHIMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Buddy-Buddy Poffin','144','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv5-145','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Ciphermaniac\'s Codebreaking','145','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv5-146','GOSSAN