ULL,NULL,3,'Croconaw','It usually moves slowly, but it goes at blinding speed when it attacks and bites prey.',180,'H','Feraligatr','41','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-42','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It won\'t attack while it\'s alone—not even if it spots prey. Instead, it waits for other Carvanha to join it, and then the Pokémon attack as a group.',50,'H','Carvanha','42','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-43','Shinji Kanda',NULL,NULL,1,'Carvanha','As soon as it catches the scent of prey, Sharpedo will jet seawater from its backside, hurtling toward the target to attack at 75 mph.',120,'H','Sharpedo','43','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-44','satoma',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Keldeo has strengthened its resolve for battle, filling its body with power and changing its form.',110,'H','Keldeo','44','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-45','Orca',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It eats snow that has accumulated on the ground. It prefers soft, freshly fallen snow, so it will eat its way up a mountain, aiming for the peak.',50,'H','Snom','45','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-46','rika',NULL,NULL,2,'Snom','Frosmoth senses air currents with its antennae. It sends its scales drifting on frigid air, making them fall like snow.',110,'H','Frosmoth','46','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-47','OKUBO',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand.',60,'H','Wiglett','47','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-48','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It likes playing with others of its kind using the water ring on its tail. It uses ultrasonic waves to sense the emotions of other living creatures.',80,'H','Finizen','48','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-49','DOM',NULL,NULL,2,'Finizen','This Pokémon\'s ancient genes have awakened. It is now so extraordinarily strong that it can easily lift a cruise ship with one fin.',150,'H','Palafin','49','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-5','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,'Nuzleaf','A Pokémon that was feared as a forest guardian. It can read the foe\'s mind and take preemptive action.',150,'H','Shiftry','5','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-50','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,220,'H','Walking Wake ex','50','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-51','kodama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When several of these Pokémon gather, their electricity can build and cause lightning storms.',70,'H','Pikachu','51','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-52','cochi8i',NULL,NULL,1,'Pikachu','If the electric pouches in its cheeks become fully charged, both ears will stand straight up.',130,'H','Raichu','52','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-53','Uta',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Many power plants keep Ground-type Pokémon around as a defense against Electabuzz that come seeking electricity.',90,'H','Electabuzz','53','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-54','Yuya Oka',NULL,NULL,3,'Electabuzz','The amount of electrical energy this Pokémon produces is proportional to the rate of its pulse. The voltage jumps while Electivire is battling.',140,'H','Electivire','54','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-55','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,2,'Grubbin','While its durable shell protects it from attacks, Charjabug strikes at enemies with jolts of electricity discharged from the tips of its jaws.',100,'H','Charjabug','55','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-56','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,2,'Charjabug','It builds up electricity in its abdomen, focuses it through its jaws, and then fires the electricity off in concentrated beams.',160,'H','Vikavolt','56','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-57','kantaro',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It runs as fast as lightning strikes, shredding its opponents with its high-voltage claws.',120,'H','Zeraora','57','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-58','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is very popular as a herding dog in the Galar region. As it runs, it generates electricity from the base of its tail.',70,'H','Yamper','58','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-59','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,1,'Yamper','This Pokémon generates electricity and channels it into its legs to keep them going strong. Boltund can run nonstop for three full days.',120,'H','Boltund','59','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-6','Yoriyuki Ikegami',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'If it senses danger, it scatters spores from the top of its head to protect itself.',60,'H','Shroomish','6','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-60','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,'Wiglett',NULL,250,'H','Wugtrio ex','60','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-61','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'This Pokémon shares many similarities with Iron Hands, an object mentioned in a certain expedition journal.',140,'H','Iron Hands','61','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-62','Takeshi Nakamura',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Some of its notable features match those of an object named within a certain expedition journal as Iron Thorns.',140,'H','Iron Thorns','62','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-63','Nelnal',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The broadness of its hands may be no coincidence—many scientists believe its palms became enlarged specifically for pantomiming.',90,'H','Mr. Mime','63','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-64','yuu',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The fur on its body naturally repels water. It can stay dry even when it plays in the water.',70,'H','Marill','64','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-65','Makura Tami',NULL,NULL,2,'Marill','Its long ears are superb sensors. It can distinguish the movements of things in water and tell what they are.',130,'H','Azumarill','65','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-66','matazo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Girafarig\'s tail has a small head. It instinctively bites at any foe that approaches the Pokémon from behind.',90,'H','Girafarig','66','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-67','Takumi Wada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It communicates using telepathy. Its body is covered in down that refracts light to make it invisible.',110,'H','Latias','67','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-68','Kedamahadaitai Yawarakai',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Ancient people believed that the pattern on Bronzor\'s back contained a mysterious power.',80,'H','Bronzor','68','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-69','Katsunori Sato',NULL,NULL,3,'Bronzor','In ages past, this Pokémon was revered as a bringer of rain. It was found buried in the ground.',110,'H','Bronzong','69','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-7','Taiga Kasai',NULL,NULL,1,'Shroomish','The seeds on its tail are made of toxic spores. It knocks out foes with quick, virtually invisible punches.',120,'H','Breloom','7','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-70','Cona Nitanda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It communicates with others telepathically. Its body is encapsulated in liquid, but if it takes a heavy blow, the liquid will leak out.',40,'H','Solosis','70','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-71','mele',NULL,NULL,2,'Solosis','Its psychic power can supposedly cover a range of more than half a mile—but only if its two brains can agree with each other.',80,'H','Duosion','71','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-72','Gemi',NULL,NULL,2,'Duosion','While it could use its psychic abilities in battle, this Pokémon prefers to swing its powerful arms around to beat opponents into submission.',120,'H','Reuniclus','72','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-73','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'If this Pokémon stands near a TV, strange scenery will appear on the screen. That scenery is said to be from its home.',60,'H','Elgyem','73','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-74','Shinya Komatsu',NULL,NULL,1,'Elgyem','Whenever a Beheeyem visits a farm, a Dubwool mysteriously disappears.',100,'H','Beheeyem','74','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-75','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Nectar and pollen are its favorite fare. You can find Cutiefly hovering around Gossifleur, trying to get some of Gossifleur\'s pollen.',30,'H','Cutiefly','75','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-76','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Cutiefly','It makes pollen puffs from pollen and nectar. The puffs\' effects depend on the type of ingredients and how much of each one is used.',70,'H','Ribombee','76','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-77','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'There has been only one reported sighting of this Pokémon. It resembles a mysterious creature depicted in an old expedition journal.',90,'H','Scream Tail','77','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-78','kodama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon has characteristics similar to those of Flutter Mane, a creature mentioned in a certain book.',90,'H','Flutter Mane','78','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-79','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It\'s possible that this is the object listed as Iron Valiant in a certain expedition journal.',130,'H','Iron Valiant','79','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-8','Tomomi Kaneko',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its flowers give off a relaxing fragrance. The stronger its aroma, the healthier the Roselia is.',60,'H','Roselia','8','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-80','chibi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It\'s possible that this is the object listed as Iron Valiant in a certain expedition journal.',130,'H','Iron Valiant','80','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-81','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'H','Iron Crown ex','81','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-82','Natsumi Miyanose',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It meditates to heighten its inner energy and to float in the air. It eats one berry a day.',70,'H','Meditite','82','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-83','Masako Tomii',NULL,NULL,1,'Meditite','It elegantly avoids attacks with dance-like steps, then launches a devastating blow in the same motion.',120,'H','Medicham','83','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-84','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Rock-hard scales and oil-filled swim bladders allow this Pokémon to survive the intense water pressure of the deep sea.',100,'H','Relicanth','84','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv5-85','Kariya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It brings its claws together and whirls around at high speed before rushing toward its prey.',70,'H','Drilbur','85','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-86','Bun Toujo',NULL,NULL,2,'Drilbur','It\'s not uncommon for tunnels that appear to have formed naturally to actually be a result of Excadrill\'s rampant digging.',130,'H','Excadrill','86','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-87','miki kudo',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'They were sculpted from clay in ancient times. No one knows why, but some of them are driven to continually line up boulders.',90,'H','Golett','87','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-88','Oku',NULL,NULL,4,'Golett','Artillery platforms built into the walls of ancient castles served as perches from which Golurk could fire energy beams.',160,'H','Golurk','88','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-89','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is very friendly when it\'s young. Its disposition becomes vicious once it matures, but it never forgets the kindness of its master.',70,'H','Rockruff','89','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-9','matazo',NULL,NULL,2,'Roselia','After captivating opponents with its sweet scent, it lashes them with its thorny whips.',130,'H','Roserade','9','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-90','Yoshioka',NULL,NULL,1,'Rockruff','Lycanroc attacks its prey with its sharp claws and fangs. It loyally obeys the instructions of a Trainer it trusts.',120,'H','Lycanroc','90','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-91','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon covers itself in mud that it has regurgitated. The mud won\'t dry out even if it\'s exposed to the sun for a long time.',80,'H','Mudbray','91','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-92','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,3,'Mudbray','This Pokémon has been treasured not just for its physical labor but also because it produces high-quality mud used for making pottery.',150,'H','Mudsdale','92','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-93','Aya Kusube',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'On sunny days, Rolycoly will come out onto grassy plains and roll around. Then it will eat the grass that gets tangled in its wheel-like leg.',80,'H','Rolycoly','93','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-94','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,4,'Rolycoly','The temperature inside its body increases when it experiences strong emotions. It rolls around frantically while spewing flames.',110,'H','Carkol','94','Common','Pokémon'),('sv5-95','Shiburingaru',NULL,NULL,4,'Carkol','To intimidate its opponents, Coalossal will vigorously shake its body, scattering coal from its smoldering back.',180,'H','Coalossal','95','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-96','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'Sightings of this Pokémon have occurred in recent years. The name Great Tusk was taken from a creature listed in a certain book.',140,'H','Great Tusk','96','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-97','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Sightings of this Pokémon have occurred in recent years. The name Great Tusk was taken from a creature listed in a certain book.',140,'H','Great Tusk','97','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-98','DOM',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'No records exist of this Pokémon being caught. Data is lacking, but the Pokémon\'s traits match up with a creature shown in an expedition journal.',120,'H','Sandy Shocks','98','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv5-99','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,240,'H','Iron Boulder ex','99','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-1','Yoriyuki Ikegami',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Hidden beneath a tangle of vines that grows nonstop even if the vines are torn off, this Pokémon\'s true appearance remains a mystery.',80,'H','Tangela','1','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-10','Orca',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It guides Volbeat to draw signs in the night sky. There are scholars who research the meaning of these signs.',70,'H','Illumise','10','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-100','SIE NANAHARA',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Growlithe','Snaps at its foes with fangs cloaked in blazing flame. Despite its bulk, it deftly feints every which way, leading opponents on a deceptively merry chase as it all but dances around them.',130,'H','Hisuian Arcanine','100','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-101','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'When endangered, it may protect itself by increasing its magnetism and drawing nearby iron objects to its body.',80,'H','Nosepass','101','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-102','OKUBO',NULL,NULL,3,'Nosepass','Probopass radiates such a powerful magnetic field that nearby electrical appliances are rendered useless while it\'s around.',140,'H','Probopass','102','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-103','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It fights by swinging a piece of lumber around. It is close to evolving when it can handle heavy lumber without difficulty.',80,'H','Timburr','103','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-104','Aya Kusube',NULL,NULL,2,'Timburr','This Pokémon is so muscular and strongly built that even a group of wrestlers could not make it budge an inch.',100,'H','Gurdurr','104','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-105','Takeshi Nakamura',NULL,NULL,3,'Gurdurr','Rather than rely on their strength, they master moves that make good use of centrifugal force to swing around concrete.',180,'H','Conkeldurr','105','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-106','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,'Frogadier',NULL,310,'H','Greninja ex','106','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-107','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Hawlucha live quietly without flocking together. They fight constantly with their natural enemies: noisy groups of Primeape.',70,'H','Hawlucha','107','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-108','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Glimmet\'s toxic mineral crystals look just like flower petals. This Pokémon scatters poisonous powder like pollen to protect itself.',60,'H','Glimmet','108','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-109','Kazumasa Yasukuni',NULL,NULL,3,'Glimmet','Glimmora\'s petals are made of crystallized poison energy. It has recently become evident that these petals resemble Tera Jewels.',130,'H','Glimmora','109','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-11','Kuroimori',NULL,NULL,1,'Eevee','The younger they are, the more they smell like fresh grass. With age, their fragrance takes on the odor of fallen leaves.',120,'H','Leafeon','11','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-110','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It slowly brings its exceedingly heavy head down upon the ground, splitting the earth open with huge fissures that run over 160 feet deep.',140,'H','Ting-Lu','110','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-111','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Okidogi is a ruffian with a short temper. It can pulverize anything by swinging around the chain on its neck.',130,'H','Okidogi','111','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-112','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,210,'H','Cornerstone Mask Ogerpon ex','112','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-113','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Poochyena pursue their prey in packs. Once the prey is exhausted, the pack finishes it off. But sometimes the prey retaliates, and the pack flees.',70,'H','Poochyena','113','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-114','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,'Poochyena','Once it\'s caught the scent of faraway prey, the leader gives a signal, and the whole pack moves out.',120,'H','Mightyena','114','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-115','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Venipede and Sizzlipede are similar species, but when the two meet, a huge fight ensues.',80,'H','Venipede','115','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-116','Krgc',NULL,NULL,3,'Venipede','This Pokémon spins itself rapidly and charges into its opponents. Its top speed is just over 60 mph.',100,'H','Whirlipede','116','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-117','Shiburingaru',NULL,NULL,3,'Whirlipede','Scolipede latches on to its prey with the claws on its neck before slamming them into the ground and jabbing them with its claws\' toxic spikes.',170,'H','Scolipede','117','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-118','danciao',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It is possible that the creature listed as Brute Bonnet in a certain book could actually be this Pokémon.',120,'H','Brute Bonnet','118','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-119','toi8',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'People fashion swords from Skarmory\'s shed feathers, so this Pokémon is a popular element in heraldic designs.',120,'H','Skarmory','119','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-12','Katsunori Sato',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon came to be when the spirit of a deceased child possessed a tree stump. It now wanders the forest searching for friends.',70,'H','Phantump','12','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-120','Gapao',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It eats iron ore—and sometimes railroad tracks— to build up the steel armor that protects its body.',70,'H','Aron','120','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-121','takashi shiraishi',NULL,NULL,3,'Aron','Lairon live in mountains brimming with spring water and iron ore, so these Pokémon often came into conflict with humans in the past.',110,'H','Lairon','121','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-122','Dsuke',NULL,NULL,3,'Lairon','Aggron has a horn sharp enough to perforate thick iron sheets. It brings down its opponents by ramming into them horn first.',180,'H','Aggron','122','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-123','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'It dwells in volcanic caves. It digs in with its cross-shaped feet to crawl on ceilings and walls.',140,'H','Heatran','123','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-124','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The steel section is Varoom\'s actual body. This Pokémon clings to rocks and converts the minerals within into energy to fuel its activities.',70,'H','Varoom','124','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-125','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,2,'Varoom','Revavroom viciously threatens others with the sound of its exhaust. It sticks its tongue out from its cylindrical mouth and sprays toxic fluids.',140,'H','Revavroom','125','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-126','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Applin lives inside an apple. When an Applin is separated from its apple, its body loses moisture and the Pokémon grows weak.',40,'H','Applin','126','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-127','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,2,'Applin','The head sticking out belongs to the fore-wyrm, while the tail belongs to the core-wyrm. The two share one apple and help each other out.',80,'H','Dipplin','127','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-128','Scav',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has a habit of biting at Clauncher even though it doesn\'t feed on them. This is said to be vestigial behavior from when Dreepy was alive.',70,'H','Dreepy','128','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-129','cochi8i',NULL,NULL,1,'Dreepy','This Pokémon stores up energy in its lungs, then shoots it out. It takes care of Dreepy and battles alongside them until they\'re all grown up.',90,'H','Drakloak','129','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-13','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,3,'Phantump','Trevenant is very kind to Pokémon living in the forest. It doesn\'t even care if these Pokémon take up residence in the greenery on its head.',120,'H','Trevenant','13','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-130','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,'Drakloak',NULL,320,'H','Dragapult ex','130','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-131','Jerky',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Tatsugiri is an extremely cunning Pokémon. It feigns weakness to lure in prey, then orders its partner to attack.',70,'H','Tatsugiri','131','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-132','miki kudo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The stalk this Pokémon carries in its wings serves as a sword to cut down opponents. In a dire situation, the stalk can also serve as food.',70,'H','Farfetch\'d','132','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-133','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It walks carefully to prevent its egg from breaking. However, it is extremely fast at running away.',120,'H','Chansey','133','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-134','Iwamoto05',NULL,NULL,4,'Chansey',NULL,300,'H','Blissey ex','134','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-135','satoma',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its genetic code is irregular. It may mutate if it is exposed to radiation from element stones.',50,'H','Eevee','135','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-136','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'Its stomach\'s digestive juices can dissolve any kind of poison. Eating things off the ground doesn\'t bother it at all.',160,'H','Snorlax','136','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-137','Mugi Hamada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its tail moves with greater dexterity than its hands. Making deft use of this tail, Aipom lives high among the treetops.',60,'H','Aipom','137','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-138','KEIICHIRO ITO',NULL,NULL,1,'Aipom','Split into two, the tails are so adept at handling and doing things that Ambipom rarely uses its hands.',110,'H','Ambipom','138','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-139','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It strengthens its body by diving into the depths of ponds, swimming around while looking for bog moss to eat.',60,'H','Ducklett','139','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-14','Tomomi Ozaki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When it uses its special stick to strike up a beat, the sound waves produced carry revitalizing energy to the plants and flowers in the area.',70,'H','Grookey','14','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-140','Susumu Maeya',NULL,NULL,1,'Ducklett','It\'s said that many artists have taken inspiration from the sight of a Swanna performing a beautiful dance in the light of dawn.',110,'H','Swanna','140','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-141','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,260,'H','Bloodmoon Ursaluna ex','141','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-142','AYUMI ODASHIMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Accompanying Flute','142','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-143','AYUMI ODASHIMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Bug Catching Set','143','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-144','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Caretaker','144','Common','Trainer'),('sv6-145','kantaro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Carmine','145','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-146','MARINA Chikazawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Community Center','146','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-147','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Cook','147','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-148','Eske Yoshinob',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Enhanced Hammer','148','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-149','MARINA Chikazawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Festival Grounds','149','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-15','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,'Grookey','The faster a Thwackey can beat out a rhythm with its two sticks, the more respect it wins from its peers.',100,'H','Thwackey','15','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-150','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Handheld Fan','150','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-151','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Hassel','151','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-152','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Hyper Aroma','152','ACE SPEC Rare','Trainer'),('sv6-153','AYUMI ODASHIMA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Jamming Tower','153','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-154','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Kieran','154','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-155','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Lana\'s Aid','155','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-156','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Love Ball','156','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-157','hncl',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Lucian','157','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-158','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Lucky Helmet','158','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-159','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Ogre\'s Mask','159','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-16','toriyufu',NULL,NULL,4,'Thwackey','By drumming, it taps into the power of its special tree stump. The roots of the stump follow its direction in battle.',180,'H','Rillaboom','16','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-160','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Perrin','160','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-161','hncl',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Raifort','161','Uncommon','Trainer'),('sv6-162','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Scoop Up Cyclone','162','ACE SPEC Rare','Trainer'),('sv6-163','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Secret Box','163','ACE SPEC Rare','Trainer'),('sv6-164','inose yukie',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Survival Brace','164','ACE SPEC Rare','Trainer'),('sv6-165','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Unfair Stamp','165','ACE SPEC Rare','Trainer'),('sv6-166',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Boomerang Energy','166','Uncommon','Energy'),('sv6-167',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'H','Legacy Energy','167','ACE SPEC Rare','Energy'),('sv6-168','Yukihiro Tada',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'These Pokémon judge one another based on pincers. Thicker, more impressive pincers make for more popularity with the opposite gender.',110,'H','Pinsir','168','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-169','Shinya Komatsu',NULL,NULL,1,'Sunkern','Since it converts sunlight into energy, it is always looking in the direction of the sun.',100,'H','Sunflora','169','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-17','OKUBO',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Applin lives inside an apple. When an Applin is separated from its apple, its body loses moisture and the Pokémon grows weak.',40,'H','Applin','17','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-170','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Applin','The head sticking out belongs to the fore-wyrm, while the tail belongs to the core-wyrm. The two share one apple and help each other out.',80,'H','Dipplin','170','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-171','Saboteri',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Poltchageist looks like a regional form of Sinistea, but it was recently discovered that the two Pokémon are entirely unrelated.',30,'H','Poltchageist','171','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-172','Masa',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Coal is the source of Torkoal\'s energy. Large amounts of coal can be found in the mountains where they live.',130,'H','Torkoal','172','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-173','Krgc',NULL,NULL,1,'Monferno','Its crown of fire is indicative of its fiery nature. It is beaten by none in terms of quickness.',140,'H','Infernape','173','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-174','matazo',NULL,NULL,1,'Snorunt','It freezes prey by blowing its −58 degree Fahrenheit breath. It is said to then secretly display its prey.',90,'H','Froslass','174','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-175','takashi shiraishi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When the water warms, they inflate the flotation sac on their heads and drift languidly on the sea in packs.',70,'H','Phione','175','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-176','Fujimoto Gold',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s an incredibly poor learner because it uses the bare minimum amount of energy for its brain. It focuses on battling instead.',110,'H','Cramorant','176','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-177','Tonji Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,'Helioptile','A now-vanished desert culture treasured these Pokémon. Appropriately, when Heliolisk came to the Galar region, treasure came with them.',100,'H','Heliolisk','177','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-178','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'These Pokémon make their nests on coastal cliffs. The nests have a strange, crackling texture, and they\'re a popular delicacy.',60,'H','Wattrel','178','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-179','REND',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its cries echo inside its hollow body to emerge as beautiful notes for startling and repelling foes.',70,'H','Chimecho','179','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-18','Saboteri',NULL,NULL,2,'Applin','The head sticking out belongs to the fore-wyrm, while the tail belongs to the core-wyrm. The two share one apple and help each other out.',80,'H','Dipplin','18','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-180','GOTO minori',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When it flies to this land from across the sea, the bitter winter comes to an end. According to legend, this Pokémon\'s love gives rise to the budding of fresh life across Hisui.',120,'H','Enamorus','180','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-181','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'They patrol their territory in pairs. I believe the igneous rock components in the fur of this species are the result of volcanic activity in its habitat.',80,'H','Hisuian Growlithe','181','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-182','Kariya',NULL,NULL,3,'Nosepass','Probopass radiates such a powerful magnetic field that nearby electrical appliances are rendered useless while it\'s around.',140,'H','Probopass','182','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-183','Yuriko Akase',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It fights by swinging a piece of lumber around. It is close to evolving when it can handle heavy lumber without difficulty.',80,'H','Timburr','183','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-184','Dsuke',NULL,NULL,3,'Aron','Lairon live in mountains brimming with spring water and iron ore, so these Pokémon often came into conflict with humans in the past.',110,'H','Lairon','184','Illustration Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-185','Katsunori Sato',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Applin lives inside an apple. When an Applin is separated from its apple, its body loses moisture and the Pokémon grows weak.',40,'H','Applin','185','Illustration Rare','Pokémon