'sv6-44','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its dorsal, pectoral, and tail fins wave elegantly in water. That is why it is known as the Water Dancer.',50,'H','Goldeen','44','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-45','Gemi',NULL,NULL,1,'Goldeen','In autumn, its body becomes more fatty in preparing to propose to a mate. It takes on beautiful colors.',90,'H','Seaking','45','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-46','Gapao',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'In certain parts of Galar, Jynx was once feared and worshiped as the Queen of Ice.',90,'H','Jynx','46','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-47','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It can live in impure water, where it doesn\'t need to compete with other water Pokémon for food, so its numbers have steadily increased.',80,'H','Corphish','47','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-48','Kurata So',NULL,NULL,3,'Corphish','A rough customer that wildly flails its giant claws. It is said to be extremely hard to raise.',130,'H','Crawdaunt','48','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-49','Scav',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is the shabbiest Pokémon of all. It forms schools and lives at the bottom of rivers that teem with plant life.',30,'H','Feebas','49','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-5','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,'Spinarak','It wanders in search of food after darkness falls, never nesting in a specific place.',90,'H','Ariados','5','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-50','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,1,'Feebas','It lives at the bottom of clear lakes. In times of war, it shows itself, which soothes people\'s minds and hearts.',120,'H','Milotic','50','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-51','Mékayu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is said that a home visited by a Snorunt will prosper. It can withstand cold of −150 degrees Fahrenheit.',60,'H','Snorunt','51','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-52','Oku',NULL,NULL,2,'Snorunt','It prevents prey from escaping by instantaneously freezing moisture in the air.',120,'H','Glalie','52','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-53','Makura Tami',NULL,NULL,1,'Snorunt','It freezes prey by blowing its −58 degree Fahrenheit breath. It is said to then secretly display its prey.',90,'H','Froslass','53','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-54','rika',NULL,NULL,1,'Eevee','It lowers its body heat to freeze its fur. The hairs then become like needles it can fire.',120,'H','Glaceon','54','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-55','aspara',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When the water warms, they inflate the flotation sac on their heads and drift languidly on the sea in packs.',70,'H','Phione','55','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-56','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It secretes flexible bubbles from its chest and back. The bubbles reduce the damage it would otherwise take when attacked.',60,'H','Froakie','56','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-57','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,1,'Froakie','It can throw bubble-covered pebbles with precise control, hitting empty cans up to a hundred feet away.',90,'H','Frogadier','57','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-58','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s an incredibly poor learner because it uses the bare minimum amount of energy for its brain. It focuses on battling instead.',110,'H','Cramorant','58','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-59','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its water ring is made from seawater mixed with a sticky fluid that Finizen secretes from its blowhole.',70,'H','Finizen','59','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-6','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is very weak. Its only means of defense is to shake its leaves desperately at its attacker.',40,'H','Sunkern','6','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-60','Ligton',NULL,NULL,1,'Finizen','Its physical capabilities are no different than a Finizen\'s, but when its allies are in danger, it transforms and powers itself up.',100,'H','Palafin','60','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-61','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,2,'Finizen',NULL,340,'H','Palafin ex','61','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-62','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It resembles a mysterious object mentioned in an old book. There are only two reported sightings of this Pokémon.',90,'H','Iron Bundle','62','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-63','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This ferocious creature is shrouded in mystery. It\'s named after an aquatic monster mentioned in an old expedition journal.',130,'H','Walking Wake','63','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-64','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,210,'H','Wellspring Mask Ogerpon ex','64','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-65','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon has complete control over electricity. There are tales of Zapdos nesting in the dark depths of pitch-black thunderclouds.',120,'H','Zapdos','65','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-66','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The extension and contraction of its muscles generates electricity. Its fur glows when it\'s in trouble.',60,'H','Shinx','66','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-67','Takumi Wada',NULL,NULL,1,'Shinx','By gathering their tails together, they collectively generate powerful electricity from their claws.',90,'H','Luxio','67','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-68','PLANETA Yamashita',NULL,NULL,1,'Luxio',NULL,310,'H','Luxray ex','68','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-69','Shimaris Yukichi',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'As Emolga flutters through the air, it crackles with electricity. This Pokémon is cute, but it can cause a lot of trouble.',60,'H','Emolga','69','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-7','Ounishi',NULL,NULL,1,'Sunkern','Since it converts sunlight into energy, it is always looking in the direction of the sun.',100,'H','Sunflora','7','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-70','Taiga Kayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When spread, the frills on its head act like solar panels, generating the power behind this Pokémon\'s electric moves.',60,'H','Helioptile','70','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-71','Atsuya Uki',NULL,NULL,1,'Helioptile','A now-vanished desert culture treasured these Pokémon. Appropriately, when Heliolisk came to the Galar region, treasure came with them.',100,'H','Heliolisk','71','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-72','kodama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has a small stomach. If it isn\'t constantly eating the seeds it keeps in its pockets, it will get hungry immediately.',70,'H','Morpeko','72','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-73','nisimono',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It floats using the electricity stored in its body. When thunderclouds are around, Tadbulb will float higher off the ground.',50,'H','Tadbulb','73','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-74','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,3,'Tadbulb','What appear to be eyeballs are actually organs for discharging the electricity generated by Bellibolt\'s belly-button dynamo.',140,'H','Bellibolt','74','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-75','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'These Pokémon make their nests on coastal cliffs. The nests have a strange, crackling texture, and they\'re a popular delicacy.',60,'H','Wattrel','75','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-76','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,'Wattrel','It uses its throat sac to store electricity generated by its wings. There\'s hardly any oil in its feathers, so it is a poor swimmer.',120,'H','Kilowattrel','76','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-77','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,230,'H','Iron Thorns ex','77','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-78','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'On nights with a full moon, they gather together and dance. The surrounding area is enveloped in an abnormal magnetic field.',60,'H','Clefairy','78','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-79','satoma',NULL,NULL,2,'Clefairy','It has an acute sense of hearing. It can easily hear a pin being dropped nearly 1,100 yards away.',120,'H','Clefable','79','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-8','Toshinao Aoki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'With its herculean powers, it can easily throw around an object that is 100 times its own weight.',120,'H','Heracross','8','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-80','Kariya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon uses its psychic powers while it sleeps. The contents of Abra\'s dreams affect the powers that the Pokémon wields.',40,'H','Abra','80','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-81','Uninori',NULL,NULL,1,'Abra','Using its psychic power, Kadabra levitates as it sleeps. It uses its springy tail as a pillow.',80,'H','Kadabra','81','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-82','Masako Tomii',NULL,NULL,1,'Kadabra','It has an incredibly high level of intelligence. Some say that Alakazam remembers everything that ever happens to it, from birth till death.',140,'H','Alakazam','82','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-83','Shinji Kanda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Girafarig\'s tail has a small head. It instinctively bites at any foe that approaches the Pokémon from behind.',100,'H','Girafarig','83','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-84','Dsuke',NULL,NULL,2,'Girafarig','The hardened head from the tail protects the head of the main body as Farigiraf whips its long neck around to headbutt enemies.',140,'H','Farigiraf','84','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-85','Mousho',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its cries echo inside its hollow body to emerge as beautiful notes for startling and repelling foes.',70,'H','Chimecho','85','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-86','Yukiko Baba',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Flabébé rides a red flower. Immediately after birth, this Pokémon begins flying around in search of a flower it likes.',40,'H','Flabébé','86','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-87','mingo',NULL,NULL,1,'Flabébé','This Pokémon uses red wavelengths of light to pour its own energy into flowers and draw forth their latent potential.',70,'H','Floette','87','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-88','Ligton',NULL,NULL,2,'Floette','They say that flower gardens created by Florges are constantly showered with a power that can heal both body and spirit.',140,'H','Florges','88','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-89','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It eats its own weight in sugar every day. If it doesn\'t get enough sugar, it becomes incredibly grumpy.',50,'H','Swirlix','89','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-9','Orca',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It flashes the light on its rear to communicate with other Volbeat. It loves the sweet aroma given off by Illumise.',70,'H','Volbeat','9','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-90','mingo',NULL,NULL,2,'Swirlix','By taking in a person\'s scent, it can sniff out their mental and physical condition. It\'s hoped that this skill will have many medical applications.',120,'H','Slurpuff','90','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-91','Asako Ito',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It flings sand into the eyes of its prey and tries to close in on them while they\'re blinded, but since Sandygast is so slow, the prey tends to escape.',90,'H','Sandygast','91','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-92','Uta',NULL,NULL,4,'Sandygast','From the hollows in its arms, it fires the bones of its victims, which are all dried up after being drained of their vitality.',150,'H','Palossand','92','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-93','DOM',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When it flies to this land from across the sea, the bitter winter comes to an end. According to legend, this Pokémon\'s love gives rise to the budding of fresh life across Hisui.',120,'H','Enamorus','93','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-94','akagi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,190,'H','Scream Tail ex','94','Double Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-95','kodama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Munkidori keeps itself somewhere safe while it toys with its foes, using psychokinesis to induce intense dizziness.',110,'H','Munkidori','95','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-96','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Fezandipiti beats its glossy wings to scatter pheromones that captivate people and Pokémon.',120,'H','Fezandipiti','96','Rare','Pokémon'),('sv6-97','Tetsu Kayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'No matter how high a place it falls from, this Pokémon can save itself by rolling into a ball and bouncing.',60,'H','Sandshrew','97','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6-98','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,1,'Sandshrew','The spikes on its body are made up of its hardened hide. It rolls up and attacks foes with its spikes.',120,'H','Sandslash','98','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('sv6-99','Whisker',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'They patrol their territory in pairs. I believe the igneous rock components in the fur of this species are the result of volcanic activity in its habitat.',80,'H','Hisuian Growlithe','99','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6pt5-1',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,40,'H','Joltik','1','Common','Pokémon'),('sv6pt5-10',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,60,'H','Horse