esaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This seems to be the Winged King mentioned in an old expedition journal. It was said to have split the land with its bare fists.',140,'H','Koraidon','91','Promo','Pokémon'),('svp-92','akagi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This seems to be the Iron Serpent mentioned in an old book. The Iron Serpent is said to have turned the land to ash with its lightning.',110,'H','Miraidon','92','Promo','Pokémon'),('svp-93','Tonji Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'These Pokémon have sharp fangs and powerful jaws. Sailors avoid Carvanha dens at all costs.',50,'G','Carvanha','93','Promo','Pokémon'),('svp-94','Mizue',NULL,NULL,3,'Tadbulb','When this Pokémon expands and contracts its wobbly body, the belly-button dynamo in its stomach produces a huge amount of electricity.',130,'G','Bellibolt','94','Promo','Pokémon'),('svp-95','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'Because of its unusual, starlike silhouette, people believe that it came here on a meteor.',30,'G','Cleffa','95','Promo','Pokémon'),('svp-96','Hasuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Apparently Cyclizar has been allowing people to ride on its back since ancient times. Depictions of this have been found in 10,000-year-old murals.',120,'G','Cyclizar','96','Promo','Pokémon'),('svp-97','Takumi Wada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon has characteristics similar to those of Flutter Mane, a creature mentioned in a certain book.',90,'H','Flutter Mane','97','Promo','Pokémon'),('svp-98','Tonji Matsuno',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Some of its notable features match those of an object named within a certain expedition journal as Iron Thorns.',140,'H','Iron Thorns','98','Promo','Pokémon'),('svp-99','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though usually a mellow Pokémon, it will sink its sharp, poison-soaked front teeth into any that anger it, causing paralysis in the object of its ire.',50,'G','Shroodle','99','Promo','Pokémon'),('swsh1-1','PLANETA Igarashi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,180,'D','Celebi V','1','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh1-10','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When it uses its special stick to strike up a beat, the sound waves produced carry revitalizing energy to the plants and flowers in the area.',60,'D','Grookey','10','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-100','Yukiko Baba',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'If a tree branch shakes when there is no wind, it\'s a Sudowoodo, not a tree. It hides from the rain.',100,'D','Sudowoodo','100','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh1-101','Uta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It moves while spinning around on its single foot. Some Baltoy have been seen spinning on their heads.',70,'D','Baltoy','101','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-102','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It moves while spinning around on its single foot. Some Baltoy have been seen spinning on their heads.',60,'D','Baltoy','102','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-103','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,2,'Baltoy','This mysterious Pokémon started life as an ancient clay figurine made over 20,000 years ago.',120,'D','Claydol','103','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-104','PLANETA Tsuji',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,220,'D','Regirock V','104','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh1-105','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Loads weighing up to 50 times as much as its own body weight pose no issue for this Pokémon. It\'s skilled at making use of mud.',80,'D','Mudbray','105','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-106','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,3,'Mudbray','Mud that hardens around a Mudsdale\'s legs sets harder than stone. It\'s so hard that it allows this Pokémon to scrap a truck with a single kick.',150,'D','Mudsdale','106','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-107','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It spews sand from its nostrils. While the enemy is blinded, it burrows into the ground to hide.',80,'D','Silicobra','107','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-108','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'As it digs, it swallows sand and stores it in its neck pouch. The pouch can hold more than 17 pounds of sand.',70,'D','Silicobra','108','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-109','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Silicobra','Its unique style of coiling allows it to blast sand out of its sand sac more efficiently.',140,'D','Sandaconda','109','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-11','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When it uses its special stick to strike up a beat, the sound waves produced carry revitalizing energy to the plants and flowers in the area.',70,'D','Grookey','11','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-110','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,2,'Silicobra','When it contracts its body, over 220 pounds of sand sprays from its nose. If it ever runs out of sand, it becomes disheartened.',130,'D','Sandaconda','110','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh1-111','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It\'s very curious, but its means of investigating things is to try to punch them with its tentacles. The search for food is what brings it onto land.',60,'D','Clobbopus','111','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-112','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It\'s very curious, but its means of investigating things is to try to punch them with its tentacles. The search for food is what brings it onto land.',80,'D','Clobbopus','112','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-113','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Clobbopus','A body made up of nothing but muscle makes the grappling moves this Pokémon performs with its tentacles tremendously powerful.',130,'D','Grapploct','113','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-114','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It stands in grasslands, watching the sun\'s descent from zenith to horizon. This Pokémon has a talent for delivering dynamic kicks.',120,'D','Stonjourner','114','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-115','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,220,'D','Stonjourner V','115','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh1-116','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Stonjourner V',NULL,330,'D','Stonjourner VMAX','116','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh1-117','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Thought to be the oldest form of Zigzagoon, it moves in zigzags and wreaks havoc upon its surroundings.',70,'D','Galarian Zigzagoon','117','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-118','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,2,'Galarian Zigzagoon','This very aggressive Pokémon will recklessly challenge opponents stronger than itself.',100,'D','Galarian Linoone','118','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh1-119','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Galarian Linoone','It evolved after experiencing numerous fights. While crossing its arms, it lets out a shout that would make any opponent flinch.',160,'D','Galarian Obstagoon','119','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh1-12','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,2,'Grookey','The faster a Thwackey can beat out a rhythm with its two sticks, the more respect it wins from its peers.',100,'D','Thwackey','12','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh1-120','Eske Yoshinob',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,170,'D','Sableye V','120','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh1-121','sowsow',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It attacks using the claws on its tail. Once locked in its grip, its prey is unable to move as this Pokémon\'s poison seeps in.',80,'D','Skorupi','121','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-122','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,3,'Skorupi','It\'s so vicious that it\'s called the Sand Demon. Yet when confronted by Hippowdon, Drapion keeps a low profile and will never pick a fight.',140,'D','Drapion','122','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-123','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It makes frightening noises with its poison-filled cheek sacs. When opponents flinch, Croagunk hits them with a poison jab.',70,'D','Croagunk','123','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-124','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,1,'Croagunk','It bounces toward opponents and gouges them with poisonous claws. No more than a scratch is needed to knock out its adversaries.',110,'D','Toxicroak','124','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh1-125','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Aided by the soft pads on its feet, it silently raids the food stores of other Pokémon. It survives off its ill-gotten gains.',70,'D','Nickit','125','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-126','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Nickit','It secretly marks potential targets with a scent. By following the scent, it stalks its targets and steals from them when they least expect it.',100,'D','Thievul','126','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-127','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Living with a savage, seafaring people has toughened this Pokémon\'s body so much that parts of it have turned to iron.',70,'D','Galarian Meowth','127','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-128','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,'Galarian Meowth','What appears to be an iron helmet is actually hardened hair. This Pokémon lives for the thrill of battle.',120,'D','Galarian Perrserker','128','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh1-129','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It chomps with its gaping mouth. Its huge jaws are actually steel horns that have been transformed.',90,'D','Mawile','129','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-13','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Grookey','The faster a Thwackey can beat out a rhythm with its two sticks, the more respect it wins from its peers.',100,'D','Thwackey','13','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh1-130','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It defends itself by launching spikes, but its aim isn\'t very good at first. Only after a lot of practice will it improve.',70,'D','Ferroseed','130','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-131','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,2,'Ferroseed','This Pokémon scrapes its spikes across rocks, and then uses the tips of its feelers to absorb the nutrients it finds within the stone.',130,'D','Ferrothorn','131','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh1-132','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Living in mud with a high iron content has given it a strong steel body.',120,'D','Galarian Stunfisk','132','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh1-133','Motofumi Fujiwara',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A pack of these Pokémon forms to serve a Bisharp boss. Each Pawniard trains diligently, dreaming of one day taking the lead.',70,'D','Pawniard','133','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-134','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,'Pawniard','Violent conflicts erupt between Bisharp and Fraxure over places where sharpening stones can be found.',120,'D','Bisharp','134','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh1-135','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Corvisquire','This Pokémon reigns supreme in the skies of the Galar region. The black luster of its steel body could drive terror into the heart of any foe.',170,'D','Corviknight','135','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-136','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'If a job requires serious strength, this Pokémon will excel at it. Its copper body tarnishes in the rain, turning a vibrant green color.',100,'D','Cufant','136','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-137','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,4,'Cufant','These Pokémon live in herds. Their trunks have incredible grip strength, strong enough to crush giant rocks into powder.',190,'D','Copperajah','137','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh1-138','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'D','Zacian V','138','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh1-139','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,230,'D','Zamazenta V','139','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh1-14','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,3,'Thwackey','By drumming, it taps into the power of its special tree stump. The roots of the stump follow its direction in battle.',170,'D','Rillaboom','14','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh1-140','chibi',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'It is not satisfied unless it eats over 880 pounds of food every day. When it is done eating, it goes promptly to sleep.',150,'D','Snorlax','140','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-141','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,220,'D','Snorlax V','141','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh1-142','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,4,'Snorlax V',NULL,340,'D','Snorlax VMAX','142','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh1-143','Yumi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It begins to hoot at the same time every day. Some Trainers use them in place of clocks.',70,'D','Hoothoot','143','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-144','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,'Hoothoot','When it needs to think, it rotates its head 180 degrees to sharpen its intellectual power.',110,'D','Noctowl','144','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-145','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The way it brushes away grime with its tail can be helpful when cleaning. But its focus on spotlessness can make cleaning more of a hassle.',70,'D','Minccino','145','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-146','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The way it brushes away grime with its tail can be helpful when cleaning. But its focus on spotlessness can make cleaning more of a hassle.',60,'D','Minccino','146','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-147','sui',NULL,NULL,1,'Minccino','Its body secretes oil that this Pokémon spreads over its nest as a coating to protect it from dust. Cinccino won\'t tolerate even a speck of the stuff.',90,'D','Cinccino','147','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-148','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It knows the forest inside and out. If it comes across a wounded Pokémon, Oranguru will gather medicinal herbs to treat it.',120,'D','Oranguru','148','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh1-149','tetsuya koizumi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The mountains it calls home are nearly two miles in height. On rare occasions, it descends to play with the children living in the towns below.',130,'D','Drampa','149','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-15','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,4,'Thwackey','By drumming, it taps into the power of its special tree stump. The roots of the stump follow its direction in battle.',190,'D','Rillaboom','15','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh1-150','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It will bravely challenge any opponent, no matter how powerful. This Pokémon benefits from every battle—even a defeat increases its strength a bit.',60,'D','Rookidee','150','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-151','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,1,'Rookidee','Smart enough to use tools in battle, these Pokémon have been seen picking up rocks and flinging them or using ropes to wrap up enemies.',80,'D','Corvisquire','151','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh1-152','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'If its fleece grows too long, Wooloo won\'t be able to move. Cloth made with the wool of this Pokémon is surprisingly strong.',70,'D','Wooloo','152','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh1-153','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its curly fleece is such an effective cushion that this Pokémon could fall off a cliff and stand right back up a