NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Zisu','189','Rare Ultra','Trainer'),('swsh10-19','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Flies noiselessly on delicate wings. It has mastered the art of deftly launching dagger-sharp feathers from those same wings.',60,'F','Rowlet','19','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-190','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,'Hisuian Lilligant V',NULL,260,'F','Hisuian Lilligant VSTAR','190','Rare Rainbow','Pokémon'),('swsh10-191','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,4,'Heatran V',NULL,330,'F','Heatran VMAX','191','Rare Rainbow','Pokémon'),('swsh10-192','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,'Origin Forme Palkia V',NULL,280,'F','Origin Forme Palkia VSTAR','192','Rare Rainbow','Pokémon'),('swsh10-193','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Typhlosion V',NULL,260,'F','Hisuian Typhlosion VSTAR','193','Rare Rainbow','Pokémon'),('swsh10-194','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,3,'Machamp V',NULL,330,'F','Machamp VMAX','194','Rare Rainbow','Pokémon'),('swsh10-195','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Decidueye V',NULL,270,'F','Hisuian Decidueye VSTAR','195','Rare Rainbow','Pokémon'),('swsh10-196','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Kleavor V',NULL,270,'F','Kleavor VSTAR','196','Rare Rainbow','Pokémon'),('swsh10-197','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Samurott V',NULL,270,'F','Hisuian Samurott VSTAR','197','Rare Rainbow','Pokémon'),('swsh10-198','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Origin Forme Dialga V',NULL,280,'F','Origin Forme Dialga VSTAR','198','Rare Rainbow','Pokémon'),('swsh10-199','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Adaman','199','Rare Rainbow','Trainer'),('swsh10-2','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'An enigmatic Pokémon that happens to bear a resemblance to a Poké Ball. When excited, it discharges the electric current it has stored in its belly, then lets out a great, uproarious laugh.',50,'F','Hisuian Voltorb','2','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-20','0313',NULL,NULL,1,'Rowlet','Regularly basks in sunlight to gather power—presumably due to the frigid climate. Nonetheless, the edges of the blade quills set into its wings are keen as ever.',90,'F','Dartrix','20','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-200','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Choy','200','Rare Rainbow','Trainer'),('swsh10-201','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Cyllene','201','Rare Rainbow','Trainer'),('swsh10-202','En Morikura',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Gardenia\'s Vigor','202','Rare Rainbow','Trainer'),('swsh10-203','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Grant','203','Rare Rainbow','Trainer'),('swsh10-204','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Irida','204','Rare Rainbow','Trainer'),('swsh10-205','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Kamado','205','Rare Rainbow','Trainer'),('swsh10-206','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Roxanne','206','Rare Rainbow','Trainer'),('swsh10-207','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Zisu','207','Rare Rainbow','Trainer'),('swsh10-208','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,'Origin Forme Palkia V',NULL,280,'F','Origin Forme Palkia VSTAR','208','Rare Secret','Pokémon'),('swsh10-209','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Samurott V',NULL,270,'F','Hisuian Samurott VSTAR','209','Rare Secret','Pokémon'),('swsh10-21','Jiro Sasumo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'These Pokémon live in herds out in the grassland. Newborn foals lack their fiery manes, which will develop about an hour after birth.',60,'F','Ponyta','21','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-210','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,3,'Origin Forme Dialga V',NULL,280,'F','Origin Forme Dialga VSTAR','210','Rare Secret','Pokémon'),('swsh10-211','Studio Bora Inc.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Choice Belt','211','Rare Secret','Trainer'),('swsh10-212','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Jubilife Village','212','Rare Secret','Trainer'),('swsh10-213','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'E','Path to the Peak','213','Rare Secret','Trainer'),('swsh10-214','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Temple of Sinnoh','214','Rare Secret','Trainer'),('swsh10-215','Toyste Beach',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Trekking Shoes','215','Rare Secret','Trainer'),('swsh10-216',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Double Turbo Energy','216','Rare Secret','Energy'),('swsh10-22','Ligton',NULL,NULL,1,'Ponyta','This Pokémon can be seen galloping through fields at speeds of up to 150 mph, its fiery mane fluttering in the wind.',100,'F','Rapidash','22','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-23','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Hails from the Johto region. Though usually curled into a ball due to its timid disposition, it harbors tremendous firepower.',60,'F','Cyndaquil','23','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-24','Pani Kobayashi',NULL,NULL,1,'Cyndaquil','This creature\'s fur is most mysterious—it is wholly impervious to the burning touch of flame. Should Quilava turn its back to you, take heed! Such a posture indicates a forthcoming attack.',90,'F','Quilava','24','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-25','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Heatran V','25','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-26','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,4,'Heatran V',NULL,330,'F','Heatran VMAX','26','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh10-27','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Boiling blood, like magma, circulates through its body. It makes its dwelling place in volcanic caves.',160,'F','Radiant Heatran','27','Radiant Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-28','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Suffers perpetual headaches. If the agony grows too great, Psyduck\'s latent power erupts, contrary to Psyduck\'s intent. Ergo, I am exploring ways to ease the pain.',60,'F','Psyduck','28','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-29','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,'Psyduck','This Pokémon lives in gently flowing rivers. It paddles through the water with its long limbs, putting its graceful swimming skills on display.',100,'F','Golduck','29','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-3','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,'Hisuian Voltorb','The tissue on the surface of its body is curiously similar in composition to an Apricorn. When irritated, this Pokémon lets loose an electric current equal to 20 lightning bolts.',90,'F','Hisuian Electrode','3','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-30','Eske Yoshinob',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,190,'F','Starmie V','30','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-31','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Swinub excels at sniffing out mushrooms buried beneath grass or snow. Since ancient times, the people of Hisui have often relied upon this skill.',60,'F','Swinub','31','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-32','yuu',NULL,NULL,3,'Swinub','If it charges at an enemy, the hairs on its back stand up straight. It is very sensitive to sound.',90,'F','Piloswine','32','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-33','Uta',NULL,NULL,4,'Piloswine','This Pokémon can be spotted in wall paintings from as far back as 10,000 years ago. For a while, it was thought to have gone extinct.',180,'F','Mamoswine','33','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-34','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This calm and gentle Pokémon swims gracefully through the sea. After building speed, it can leap out of the water. It is often misidentified as a bird Pokémon due to this behavior.',110,'F','Mantine','34','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-35','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Makes its home in swamps with murky water. The poor visibility hides this Pokémon from predators, and the slime on its body makes grasping it difficult.',60,'F','Barboach','35','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-36','Shinji Kanda',NULL,NULL,3,'Barboach','It makes its nest at the bottom of swamps. It will eat anything—if it is alive, Whiscash will eat it.',120,'F','Whiscash','36','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-37','aoki',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'With cold air that can reach temperatures as low as −328 degrees Fahrenheit, Regice instantly freezes any creature that approaches it.',130,'F','Regice','37','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-38','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,'Eevee','Glaceon is able to lower its body temperature very quickly. It freezes the atmosphere, creating diamond dust that glitters like gems while it flutters and dances around.',110,'F','Glaceon','38','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-39','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Origin Forme Palkia V','39','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-4','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The large, wickedly sharp scythes on its forearms are truly fearsome weapons. Prey\'s attempts to flee are unfailingly thwarted by this Pokémon\'s nimble motions.',90,'F','Scyther','4','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-40','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,'Origin Forme Palkia V',NULL,280,'F','Origin Forme Palkia VSTAR','40','Rare Holo VSTAR','Pokémon'),('swsh10-41','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon from the Unova region uses the shell on its belly as a weapon to cut down its foes. Thus, I\'ve conferred upon this shell the name \"scalchop.\".',70,'F','Oshawott','41','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-42','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,1,'Oshawott','Its exquisite double-scalchop technique is likely the result of daily training, and it can send even masters of the blade fleeing in defeat.',90,'F','Dewott','42','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-43','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though it differs from other Basculin in several respects, including demeanor—this one is gentle—I have categorized it as a regional form given the vast array of shared qualities.',50,'F','Hisuian Basculin','43','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-44','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Basculin','Clads itself in the souls of comrades that perished before fulfilling their goals of journeying upstream. No other species throughout all Hisui\'s rivers is Basculegion\'s equal.',120,'F','Hisuian Basculegion','44','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-45','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When it is resolute, its body fills with power and it becomes swifter. Its jumps are then too fast to follow.',110,'F','Keldeo','45','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-46','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It appears and vanishes with a ninja\'s grace. It toys with its enemies using swift movements, while slicing them with throwing stars of sharpest water.',130,'F','Radiant Greninja','46','Radiant Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-47','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Lives on mountains blanketed in perennial snow. It freezes water vapor in the air to make the ice helmet that it dons for defense.',70,'F','Bergmite','47','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-48','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,3,'Bergmite','The armor of ice covering its lower jaw puts steel to shame and can shatter rocks with ease. This Pokémon barrels along steep mountain paths, cleaving through the deep snow.',140,'F','Hisuian Avalugg','48','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-49','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'E','Galarian Mr. Rime V','49','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-5','Uta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The large, wickedly sharp scythes on its forearms are truly fearsome weapons. Prey\'s attempts to flee are unfailingly thwarted by this Pokémon\'s nimble motions.',80,'F','Scyther','5','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-50','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Luxray V','50','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-51','Shiburingaru',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'This Pokémon is a cluster of electrical energy. It\'s said that removing the rings on Regieleki\'s body will unleash the Pokémon\'s latent power.',130,'F','Regieleki','51','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-52','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Quilava','Said to purify lost, forsaken souls with its flames and guide them to the afterlife. I believe its form has been influenced by the energy of the sacred mountain towering at Hisui\'s center.',150,'F','Hisuian Typhlosion','52','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-53','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Hisuian Typhlosion V','53','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-54','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Typhlosion V',NULL,260,'F','Hisuian Typhlosion VSTAR','54','Rare Holo VSTAR','Pokémon'),('swsh10-55','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This ovate creature is frequently mistaken for a moving egg when encountered out in the fields or in the mountains. Its guileless smile soothes the soul.',50,'F','Togepi','55','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-56','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,'Togepi','They say that it will appear before kindhearted, caring people and shower them with happiness.',80,'F','Togetic','56','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-57','sui',NULL,NULL,1,'Togetic','These Pokémon are never seen anywhere near conflict or turmoil. In recent times, they\'ve hardly been seen at all.',130,'F','Togekiss','57','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-58','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It conceals itself in darkness, sending chills up travelers\' spines with its childlike weeping. As it observes the frightened travelers with glee, the red orbs upon its chest let off an eerie light.',60,'F','Misdreavus','58','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-59','Ligton',NULL,NULL,1,'Misdreavus','Its muttered curses can cause awful headaches or terrifying visions that torment others.',90,'F','Mismagius','59','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-6','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Its frail wings are so thin that one can see clear through them. However, during flight these wings exhibit the power to churn air with force enough to launch a house skyward.',60,'F','Yanma','6','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-60','Hataya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Tends to prefer people with a chipper disposition to those who are gloomy, but it has shown no discrimination with regard to age or gender. Needs more research.',70,'F','Ralts','60','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-61','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,'Ralts','If its Trainer becomes happy, it overflows with energy, dancing joyously while spinning about.',90,'F','Kirlia','61','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-62','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Kirlia','True to its honorable-warrior image, it uses the blades on its elbows only in defense of something or someone.',160,'F','Gallade','62','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-63','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Said to lure away young children and carry them off to the afterlife. Some whisper that Drifloon are formed of reincarnated human souls, but these rumors are as yet unconfirmed.',60,'F','Drifloon','63','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-64','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,'Drifloon','Some say this Pokémon is a collection of souls burdened with regrets, silently drifting through the dusk.',110,'F','Drifblim','64','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-65','sui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is said that its emergence gave humans the intelligence to improve their quality of life.',70,'F','Uxie','65','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-66','zig',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It sleeps at the bottom of a lake. Its spirit is said to leave its body to fly on the lake\'s surface.',70,'F','Mesprit','66','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-67','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is thought that Uxie, Mesprit, and Azelf all came from the same egg.',70,'F','Azelf','67','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-68','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It can instantly create many diamonds by compressing the carbon in the air between its hands.',90,'F','Diancie','68','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-69','Mizue',NULL,NULL,2,'Stantler','The black orbs shine with an uncanny light when the Pokémon is erecting invisible barriers. The fur shed from its beard retains heat well and is a highly useful material for winter clothing.',140,'F','Wyrdeer','69','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-7','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Yanma','This six-legged Pokémon is easily capable of transporting an adult in flight. The wings on its tail help it stay balanced.',120,'F','Yanmega','7','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-70','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'They patrol their territory in pairs. I believe the igneous rock components in the fur of this species are the result of volcanic activity in its habitat.',80,'F','Hisuian Growlithe','70','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-71','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Growlithe','Snaps at its foes with fangs cloaked in blazing flame. Despite its bulk, it deftly feints every which way, leading opponents on a deceptively merry chase as it all but dances around them.',150,'F','Hisuian Arcanine','71','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-72','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Machamp V','72','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-73','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,3,'Machamp V',NULL,330,'F','Machamp VMAX','73','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh10-74','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Though it pretends to be a tree, it fails to fool even children. To the touch, its body feels more like rock than tree bark. Sudowoodo\'s extreme aversion to water merits special note.',110,'F','Sudowoodo','74','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-75','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Every bit of Regirock\'s body is made of stone. As parts of its body erode, this Pokémon sticks rocks to itself to repair what\'s been lost.',130,'F','Regirock','75','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-76','Hataya',NULL,NULL,2,'Unidentified Fossil','Its hard skull is its distinguishing feature. It snapped trees by headbutting them, and then it fed on their ripe berries.',90,'F','Cranidos','76','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-77','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,2,'Cranidos','This ancient Pokémon used headbutts skillfully. Its brain was really small, so some theories suggest that its stupidity led to its extinction.',170,'F','Rampardos','77','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-78','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Lucario V','78','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-79','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'Though large and languid, Hippopotas is difficult to detect due to its tendency to burrow into and lurk beneath the soil. When agitated or excited, it expels sand from its nostrils.',100,'F','Hippopotas','79','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-8','aoki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon has an unparalleled horn. Heracross itself demonstrates tremendous power—it\'s capable of throwing several people trained in the traditional arts of war at once.',110,'F','Heracross','8','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-80','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,4,'Hippopotas','Stones can get stuck in the ports on their bodies. Dwebble help dislodge such stones, so Hippowdon look after these Pokémon.',150,'F','Hippowdon','80','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-81','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It drives its opponents to exhaustion with its agile maneuvers, then ends the fight with a flashy finishing move.',90,'F','Radiant Hawlucha','81','Radiant Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-82','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Dartrix','The air stored inside the rachises of Decidueye\'s feathers insulates the Pokémon against Hisui\'s extreme cold. This is firm proof that evolution can be influenced by environment.',160,'F','Hisuian Decidueye','82','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-83','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Hisuian Decidueye V','83','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-84','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Decidueye V',NULL,270,'F','Hisuian Decidueye VSTAR','84','Rare Holo VSTAR','Pokémon'),('swsh10-85','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Scyther','A violent creature that fells towering trees with its crude axes and shields itself with hard stone. If one should chance upon this Pokémon in the wilds, one\'s only recourse is to flee.',140,'F','Kleavor','85','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-86','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,'Scyther','A violent creature that fells towering trees with its crude axes and shields itself with hard stone. If one should chance upon this Pokémon in the wilds, one\'s only recourse is to flee.',140,'F','Kleavor','86','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-87','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Kleavor V','87','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-88','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Fishers detest this troublesome Pokémon because it sprays poison from its spines, getting it everywhere. A different form of Qwilfish lives in other regions.',80,'F','Hisuian Qwilfish','88','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-89','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Fishers detest this troublesome Pokémon because it sprays poison from its spines, getting it everywhere. A different form of Qwilfish lives in other regions.',80,'F','Hisuian Qwilfish','89','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-9','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'When its antennae hit each other, it sounds like the music of a xylophone.',60,'F','Kricketot','9','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-90','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Qwilfish','Its lancelike spikes and savage temperament have earned it the nickname \"sea fiend.\" It slurps up poison to nourish itself.',130,'F','Hisuian Overqwil','90','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh10-91','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Qwilfish','Its lancelike spikes and savage temperament have earned it the nickname \"sea fiend.\" It slurps up poison to nourish itself.',130,'F','Hisuian Overqwil','91','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-92','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its sturdy, curved claws are ideal for traversing precipitous cliffs. From the tips of these claws drips a venom that infiltrates the nerves of any prey caught in Sneasel\'s grasp.',70,'F','Hisuian Sneasel','92','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-93','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Hisuian Sneasel','Because of Sneasler\'s virulent poison and daunting physical prowess, no other species could hope to best it on the frozen highlands. Preferring solitude, this species does not form packs.',120,'F','Hisuian Sneasler','93','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-94','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,190,'F','Hisuian Sneasler V','94','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-95','KIYOTAKA OSHIYAMA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It has a very tenacious nature. Its acute sense of smell lets it chase a chosen prey without ever losing track.',60,'F','Poochyena','95','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh10-96','otumami',NULL,NULL,2,'Poochyena','It chases down prey in a pack of around ten. They defeat foes with perfectly coordinated teamwork.',110,'F','Mightyena','96','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh10-97','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Swift as the wind, Absol races through fields and mountains. Its curved, bow-like horn is acutely sensitive to the warning signs of natural disasters.',100,'F','Absol','97','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10-98','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Darkrai V','98','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10-99','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Darkrai V',NULL,270,'F','Darkrai VSTAR','99','Rare Holo VSTAR','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG01','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,3,'Snover','The Pokémon is known to bring blizzards. A shake of its massive body is enough to cause whiteout conditions.',140,'E','Abomasnow','TG01','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG02','Misaki Hashimoto',NULL,NULL,1,'Applin','It ate a sour apple, and that induced its evolution. In its cheeks, it stores an acid capable of causing chemical burns.',80,'D','Flapple','TG02','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG03','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,1,'Seadra','It stores energy by sleeping at underwater depths at which no other life forms can survive.',150,'E','Kingdra','TG03','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG04','aoki',NULL,NULL,2,'Snom','It shows no mercy to any who desecrate fields and mountains. It will fly around on its icy wings, causing a blizzard to chase offenders away.',90,'D','Frosmoth','TG04','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG05','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,2,'Kirlia','To protect its Trainer, it will expend all its psychic power to create a small black hole.',140,'E','Gardevoir','TG05','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG06','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,2,'Stantler','The black orbs shine with an uncanny light when the Pokémon is erecting invisible barriers. The fur shed from its beard retains heat well and is a highly useful material for winter clothing.',140,'F','Wyrdeer','TG06','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG07','Kinu Nishimura',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The six of them work together as one Pokémon. Teamwork is also their battle strategy, and they constantly change their formation as they fight.',110,'E','Falinks','TG07','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG08','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,'Scyther','A violent creature that fells towering trees with its crude axes and shields itself with hard stone. If one should chance upon this Pokémon in the wilds, one\'s only recourse is to flee.',140,'F','Kleavor','TG08','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG09','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,'Poochyena','It chases down prey in a pack of around ten. They defeat foes with perfectly coordinated teamwork.',110,'F','Mightyena','TG09','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG10','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,2,'Galarian Linoone','It evolved after experiencing numerous fights. While crossing its arms, it lets out a shout that would make any opponent flinch.',160,'D','Galarian Obstagoon','TG10','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG11','Hataya',NULL,NULL,3,'Bronzor','Many scientists suspect that this Pokémon originated outside the Galar region, based on the patterns on its body.',110,'E','Bronzong','TG11','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG12','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It always stands on one foot. It changes feet so fast, the movement can rarely be seen.',50,'F','Hoothoot','TG12','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG13','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,190,'F','Starmie V','TG13','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG14','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'E','Ice Rider Calyrex V','TG14','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG15','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,2,'Ice Rider Calyrex V',NULL,320,'E','Ice Rider Calyrex VMAX','TG15','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG16','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'E','Galarian Articuno V','TG16','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG17','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'E','Shadow Rider Calyrex V','TG17','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG18','chibi',NULL,NULL,2,'Shadow Rider Calyrex V',NULL,320,'E','Shadow Rider Calyrex VMAX','TG18','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh10tg-TG19','kirisAki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,200,'E','Galarian Zapdos V','TG19','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('