ody slightly warm. This Pokémon takes lost children by the hand to guide them to the spirit world.',60,'F','Litwick','24','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-25','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,'Litwick','This Pokémon appears just before someone passes away, so it\'s feared as an emissary of death.',80,'F','Lampent','25','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-26','sui',NULL,NULL,2,'Lampent','This Pokémon haunts dilapidated mansions. It sways its arms to hypnotize opponents with the ominous dancing of its flames.',150,'F','Chandelure','26','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-27','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Delphox V','27','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11-28','Sekio',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This hot-blooded Pokémon is filled with curiosity. When it gets angry or starts fighting, its short mane gets hot.',70,'F','Litleo','28','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-29','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,2,'Litleo','The temperature of its breath is over 10,000 degrees Fahrenheit, but Pyroar doesn\'t use it on its prey. This Pokémon prefers to eat raw meat.',120,'F','Pyroar','29','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-3','Jiro Sasumo',NULL,NULL,2,'Gloom','It has the world\'s largest petals. With every step, the petals shake out heavy clouds of toxic pollen.',150,'F','Vileplume','3','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-30','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'For Poliwag, swimming is easier than walking. The swirl pattern on its belly is actually part of the Pokémon\'s innards showing through the skin.',60,'F','Poliwag','30','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-31','Scav',NULL,NULL,2,'Poliwag','Staring at the swirl on its belly causes drowsiness. This trait of Poliwhirl\'s has been used in place of lullabies to get children to go to sleep.',90,'F','Poliwhirl','31','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-32','ryoma uratsuka',NULL,NULL,2,'Poliwhirl','At nightfall, these Pokémon appear on the shores of lakes. They announce their territorial claims by letting out cries that sound like shouting.',140,'F','Politoed','32','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-33','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Thanks to its thick fat, cold seas don\'t bother it at all, but it gets tired pretty easily in warm waters.',70,'F','Seel','33','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-34','chibi',NULL,NULL,2,'Seel','It sunbathes on the beach after meals. The rise in its body temperature helps its digestion.',120,'F','Dewgong','34','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-35','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Horsea makes its home in oceans with gentle currents. If this Pokémon is under attack, it spits out pitch-black ink and escapes.',50,'F','Horsea','35','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-36','sui',NULL,NULL,1,'Horsea','It\'s the males that raise the offspring. While Seadra are raising young, the spines on their backs secrete thicker and stronger poison.',80,'F','Seadra','36','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-37','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,1,'Seadra','With the arrival of a storm at sea, this Pokémon will show itself on the surface. When a Kingdra and a Dragonite meet, a fierce battle ensues.',150,'F','Kingdra','37','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-38','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Luvdisc makes its home in coral reefs in warm seas. It especially likes sleeping in the space between Corsola\'s branches.',70,'F','Luvdisc','38','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-39','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'There\'s speculation that its appearance is determined by what it eats, but the truth remains elusive.',70,'F','Shellos','39','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-4','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The mushrooms, known as tochukaso, are controlling the bug. Even if the bug bugs the mushrooms, they tell it to bug off.',70,'F','Paras','4','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-40','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It lures in prey with its shining tail fins. It stays near the surface during the day and moves to the depths when night falls.',50,'F','Finneon','40','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-41','zig',NULL,NULL,1,'Finneon','They traverse the deep waters as if crawling over the seafloor. The fantastic lights of its fins shine like stars in the night sky.',90,'F','Lumineon','41','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-42','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'One is likely to encounter this Pokémon while out in the snow. There are stories of Snover appearing in human settlements but doing no harm—rather, they bond with the children.',80,'F','Snover','42','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-43','kodama',NULL,NULL,4,'Snover','If it sees any packs of Darumaka going after Snover, it chases them off, swinging its sizable arms like hammers.',140,'F','Abomasnow','43','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-44','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though it differs from other Basculin in several respects, including demeanor—this one is gentle—I have categorized it as a regional form given the vast array of shared qualities.',50,'F','Hisuian Basculin','44','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-45','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,1,'Hisuian Basculin','Clads itself in the souls of comrades that perished before fulfilling their goals of journeying upstream. No other species throughout all Hisui\'s rivers is Basculegion\'s equal.',110,'F','Hisuian Basculegion','45','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-46','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They are better at swimming than flying, and they happily eat their favorite food, peat moss, as they dive underwater.',60,'F','Ducklett','46','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-47','Sekio',NULL,NULL,2,'Ducklett','Swanna start to dance at dusk. The one dancing in the middle is the leader of the flock.',120,'F','Swanna','47','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-48','takuyoa',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Kyurem V','48','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11-49','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,3,'Kyurem V',NULL,330,'F','Kyurem VMAX','49','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh11-5','Pani Kobayashi',NULL,NULL,2,'Paras','The bug is mostly dead, with the mushroom on its back having become the main body. If the mushroom comes off, the bug stops moving.',120,'F','Parasect','5','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-50','Midori Harada',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s so strong that it can knock out some opponents in a single hit, but it also may forget what it\'s battling midfight.',110,'F','Cramorant','50','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-51','Jiro Sasumo',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Glastrier emits intense cold from its hooves. It\'s also a belligerent Pokémon—anything it wants, it takes by force.',130,'F','Glastrier','51','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-52','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Pikachu that can generate powerful electricity have cheek sacs that are extra soft and super stretchy.',60,'F','Pikachu','52','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-53','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,1,'Pikachu','Its long tail serves as a ground to protect itself from its own high-voltage power.',120,'F','Raichu','53','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-54','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It stores static electricity in its fur for discharging. It gives off sparks if a storm approaches.',60,'F','Electrike','54','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-55','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,1,'Electrike','It stimulates its own muscles with electricity, so it can move quickly. It eases its soreness with electricity, too, so it can recover quickly as well.',120,'F','Manectric','55','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-56','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Magnezone V','56','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11-57','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,2,'Magnezone V',NULL,270,'F','Magnezone VSTAR','57','Rare Holo VSTAR','Pokémon'),('swsh11-58','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,190,'F','Rotom V','58','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11-59','Yukiko Baba',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'One alone can emit only a trickle of electricity, so a group of them gathers to unleash a powerful electric shock.',30,'F','Tynamo','59','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-6','ryoma uratsuka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It lives among the tall grass and in forests. It repels attacks by raising up the spikes on its rear.',60,'F','Wurmple','6','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-60','Uta',NULL,NULL,2,'Tynamo','These Pokémon have a big appetite. When they spot their prey, they attack it and paralyze it with electricity.',80,'F','Eelektrik','60','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-61','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,3,'Eelektrik','They crawl out of the ocean using their arms. They will attack prey on shore and immediately drag it into the ocean.',160,'F','Eelektross','61','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-62','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It can be found in quiet mountain areas on a full moon\'s night. Its dancing and its tiny, faintly glowing wings confer upon it a lovely fairylike quality.',60,'F','Clefairy','62','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-63','Sekio',NULL,NULL,2,'Clefairy','A timid fairy Pokémon that is rarely seen, it will run and hide the moment it senses people.',100,'F','Clefable','63','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-64','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Born from gases, anyone would faint if engulfed by its gaseous body, which contains poison.',40,'F','Gastly','64','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-65','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Gastly','This frightful, malevolent spirit can glide through walls, appearing wherever it likes. According to rumor, victims of a Haunter\'s lick will wither to death day by day.',70,'F','Haunter','65','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-66','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,2,'Haunter','On the night of a full moon, if shadows move on their own and laugh, it must be Gengar\'s doing.',120,'F','Gengar','66','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-67','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The behavior of this clown-like Pokémon reminds one of pantomime. It creates invisible walls using a force emitted from its fingertips.',90,'F','Mr. Mime','67','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-68','Nagomi Nijo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its strange cries sound like human language. There are some musicians who compose songs for Jynx to sing.',100,'F','Jynx','68','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-69','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It has the power to predict the future. Its power peaks when it is protecting its Trainer.',130,'F','Radiant Gardevoir','69','Radiant Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-7','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,3,'Wurmple','It drinks dew that collects on its silk and waits for evolution. Its hard cocoon repels attacks.',80,'F','Silcoon','7','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-70','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'This Pokémon is feared. When its gemstone eyes begin to glow with a sinister shine, it\'s believed that Sableye will steal people\'s spirits away.',80,'F','Sableye','70','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-71','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It uses its docile-looking face to lull foes into complacency, then bites with its huge, relentless jaws.',90,'F','Mawile','71','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-72','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'There\'s a proverb that says, \"Shun the house where Shuppet gather in the growing dusk.\"',60,'F','Shuppet','72','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-73','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,'Shuppet','Resentment at being cast off made it spring into being. Some say that treating it well will satisfy it, and it will once more become a stuffed toy.',100,'F','Banette','73','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-74','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Those who sleep holding Cresselia\'s feather are assured of joyful dreams. It is said to represent the crescent moon.',120,'F','Cresselia','74','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-75','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A once-departed soul, returned to life in Hisui. Derives power from resentment, which rises as energy atop its head and takes on the forms of foes. In this way, Zorua vents lingering malice.',60,'F','Hisuian Zorua','75','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-76','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Zorua','With its disheveled white fur, it looks like an embodiment of death. Heedless of its own safety, Zoroark attacks its nemeses with a bitter energy so intense, it lacerates Zoroark\'s own body.',120,'F','Hisuian Zoroark','76','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-77','miki kudo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It spins while making its luminescent spots flash. These spots allow it to communicate with others by using different patterns of light.',60,'F','Inkay','77','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-78','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,2,'Inkay','Gazing at its luminescent spots will quickly induce a hypnotic state, putting the observer under Malamar\'s control.',110,'F','Malamar','78','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-79','Aya Kusube',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Comfey picks flowers with its vine and decorates itself with them. For some reason, flowers won\'t wither once they\'re attached to a Comfey.',70,'F','Comfey','79','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-8','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,'Silcoon','It has an aggressive nature. It stabs prey with its long, narrow mouth to drain the prey\'s fluids.',130,'F','Beautifly','8','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-80','Ligton',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It wears a rag fashioned into a Pikachu costume in an effort to look less scary. Unfortunately, the costume only makes it creepier.',70,'F','Mimikyu','80','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-81','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It probes its surroundings with all its senses save one—it doesn\'t use its sense of sight. Spectrier\'s kicks are said to separate soul from body.',120,'F','Spectrier','81','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-82','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Enamorus V','82','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11-83','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'They patrol their territory in pairs. I believe the igneous rock components in the fur of this species are the result of volcanic activity in its habitat.',70,'F','Hisuian Growlithe','83','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-84','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Growlithe','Snaps at its foes with fangs cloaked in blazing flame. Despite its bulk, it deftly feints every which way, leading opponents on a deceptively merry chase as it all but dances around them.',130,'F','Hisuian Arcanine','84','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-85','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,2,'Poliwhirl','Its body is solid muscle. When swimming through cold seas, Poliwrath uses its impressive arms to smash through drift ice and plow forward.',160,'F','Poliwrath','85','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-86','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its whole body is composed of muscles. Even though it\'s the size of a human child, it can hurl 100 grown-ups.',70,'F','Machop','86','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-87','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,'Machop','A sturdy creature boasting a robust physique and boundless stamina. Loves training above all else and voluntarily assists with tasks such as construction and clearing land.',100,'F','Machoke','87','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-88','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,2,'Machoke','It quickly swings its four arms to rock its opponents with ceaseless punches and chops from all angles.',150,'F','Machamp','88','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11-89','Scav',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'Strong, but not too bright, this Pokémon can shatter even a skyscraper with its charging tackles.',100,'F','Rhyhorn','89','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-9','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,3,'Wurmple','It never forgets any attack it endured while in the cocoon. After evolution, it seeks payback.',80,'F','Cascoon','9','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-90','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,3,'Rhyhorn','It begins walking on its hind legs after evolution. It can punch holes through boulders with its horn.',120,'F','Rhydon','90','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-91','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,4,'Rhydon','It can load up to three projectiles per arm into the holes in its hands. What launches out of those holes could be either rocks or Roggenrola.',190,'F','Rhyperior','91','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-92','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Aerodactyl V','92','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11-93','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Aerodactyl V',NULL,260,'F','Aerodactyl VSTAR','93','Rare Holo VSTAR','Pokémon'),('swsh11-94','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Though it pretends to be a tree, it fails to fool even children. To the touch, its body feels more like rock than tree bark. Sudowoodo\'s extreme aversion to water merits special note.',110,'F','Sudowoodo','94','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-95','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It flies straight at its target\'s face, then clamps down on the startled victim to inject poison.',60,'F','Gligar','95','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-96','Shiburingaru',NULL,NULL,2,'Gligar','Its flight is soundless. It uses its lengthy tail to carry off its prey... Then its elongated fangs do the rest.',120,'F','Gliscor','96','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh11-97','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'There\'s a rumor of a traditional recipe for stew that Trainers can use to raise strong Makuhita.',80,'F','Makuhita','97','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11-98','Scav',NULL,NULL,3,'Makuhita','Hariyama that are big and fat aren\'t necessarily strong. There are some small ones that move nimbly and use moves skillfully.',140,'F','Hariyama','98','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh11-99','0313',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It eats just one berry a day. By enduring hunger, its spirit is tempered and made sharper.',70,'F','Meditite','99','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG01','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,2,'Paras','Mushroom-lacking specimens of this Pokémon lie unmoving in the forest, lending credence to the hypothesis that the large mushroom is in control of Parasect\'s actions.',120,'F','Parasect','TG01','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG02','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,'Roselia','After captivating opponents with its sweet scent, it lashes them with its thorny whips.',120,'F','Roserade','TG02','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG03','GIDORA',NULL,NULL,3,'Charmeleon','It spits fire that is hot enough to melt boulders. It may cause forest fires by blowing flames.',170,'D','Charizard','TG03','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG04','chibi',NULL,NULL,2,'Lampent','This Pokémon haunts dilapidated mansions. It sways its arms to hypnotize opponents with the ominous dancing of its flames.',150,'F','Chandelure','TG04','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG05','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Possesses cheek sacs in which it stores electricity. This clever forest-dweller roasts tough berries with an electric shock before consuming them.',60,'F','Pikachu','TG05','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG06','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,2,'Haunter','Possesses potential victims\' shadows in an effort to steal away the victims\' lives. If your shadow begins to laugh, you must take hold of a protective charm posthaste!',120,'F','Gengar','TG06','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG07','Tomomi Kaneko',NULL,NULL,1,'Shuppet','Resentment at being cast off made it spring into being. Some say that treating it well will satisfy it, and it will once more become a stuffed toy.',80,'E','Banette','TG07','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG08','You Iribi',NULL,NULL,2,'Hisuian Growlithe','Snaps at its foes with fangs cloaked in blazing flame. Despite its bulk, it deftly feints every which way, leading opponents on a deceptively merry chase as it all but dances around them.',130,'F','Hisuian Arcanine','TG08','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG09','Hitoshi Ariga',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It lays curses by thinking wicked thoughts. Writings tell that this Pokémon was born out of the assembly of five score and eight malevolent spirits.',60,'F','Spiritomb','TG09','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG10','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'This glutton appears in villages without warning and devours the entirety of their rice granaries—such occurrences have long been counted among the gravest of disasters.',150,'F','Snorlax','TG10','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG11','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Its form changes depending on the weather. The rougher conditions get, the rougher Castform\'s disposition!',70,'E','Castform','TG11','Trainer Gallery Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG12','Nisota Niso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,180,'D','Orbeetle V','TG12','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG13','Teeziro',NULL,NULL,1,'Orbeetle V',NULL,310,'D','Orbeetle VMAX','TG13','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG14','Yuya Oka',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,210,'D','Centiskorch V','TG14','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG15','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,3,'Centiskorch V',NULL,320,'D','Centiskorch VMAX','TG15','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG16','Ryota Murayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,190,'D','Pikachu V','TG16','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG17','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,'Pikachu V',NULL,310,'D','Pikachu VMAX','TG17','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG18','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Enamorus V','TG18','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG19','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Gallade V','TG19','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG20','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,180,'D','Crobat V','TG20','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG21','kodama',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'D','Eternatus V','TG21','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG22','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,3,'Eternatus V',NULL,340,'D','Eternatus VMAX','TG22','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG23','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'E','Adventurer\'s Discovery','TG23','Rare Ultra','Trainer'),('swsh11tg-TG24','NC Empire',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Lysandre',NULL,'D','Boss\'s Orders','TG24','Rare Ultra','Trainer'),('swsh11tg-TG25','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'E','Cook','TG25','Rare Ultra','Trainer'),('swsh11tg-TG26','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'D','Kabu','TG26','Rare Ultra','Trainer'),('swsh11tg-TG27','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'D','Nessa','TG27','Rare Ultra','Trainer'),('swsh11tg-TG28','Taira Akitsu',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'D','Opal','TG28','Rare Ultra','Trainer'),('swsh11tg-TG29','aky CG Works',NULL,NULL,2,'Pikachu V',NULL,310,'D','Pikachu VMAX','TG29','Rare Secret','Pokémon'),('swsh11tg-TG30','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mew V',NULL,310,'E','Mew VMAX','TG30','Rare Secret','Pokémon'),('swsh12-1','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Lives in the shadows of tall trees where it eats bugs. It is attracted by light at night.',60,'F','Venonat','1','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-10','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,1,'Petilil','I suspect that its well-developed legs are the result of a life spent on mountains covered in deep snow. The scent it exudes from its flower crown heartens those in proximity.',120,'F','Hisuian Lilligant','10','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh12-100','sui',NULL,NULL,3,'Sandygast','Palossand is known as the Beach Nightmare. It pulls its prey down into the sand by controlling the sand itself, and then it sucks out their souls.',140,'F','Palossand','100','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-101','Hataya',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'It stands in grasslands, watching the sun\'s descent from zenith to horizon. This Pokémon has a talent for delivering dynamic kicks.',130,'F','Stonjourner','101','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-102','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,230,'F','Ursaluna V','102','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh12-103','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'It emits ultrasonic waves from its mouth to check its surroundings. Even in tight caves, Zubat flies around with skill.',40,'F','Zubat','103','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-104','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Zubat','It loves to drink other creatures\' blood. It\'s said that if it finds others of its kind going hungry, it sometimes shares the blood it\'s gathered.',70,'F','Golbat','104','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-105','Yuya Oka',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Golbat','Both of its legs have turned into wings. Without a sound, Crobat flies swiftly toward its prey and sinks its fangs into the nape of its target\'s neck.',130,'F','Crobat','105','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh12-106','Ligton',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It searches for shiny things for its boss. Murkrow\'s presence is said to be unlucky, so many people detest it.',60,'F','Murkrow','106','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-107','aoki',NULL,NULL,2,'Murkrow','Its goons take care of most of the fighting for it. The only time it dirties its own hands is in delivering a final blow to finish off an opponent.',120,'F','Honchkrow','107','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-108','MUGENUP',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Skuntank V','108','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh12-109','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It makes frightening noises with its poison-filled cheek sacs. When opponents flinch, Croagunk hits them with a poison jab.',80,'F','Croagunk','109','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-11','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'No one knows what the Poké Ball–like pattern on Foongus means or why Foongus has it.',50,'F','Foongus','11','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-110','Uta',NULL,NULL,2,'Croagunk','It bounces toward opponents and gouges them with poisonous claws. No more than a scratch is needed to knock out its adversaries.',120,'F','Toxicroak','110','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-111','0313',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The desert gets cold at night, so when the sun sets, this Pokémon burrows deep into the sand and sleeps until sunrise.',70,'F','Sandile','111','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-112','Pani Kobayashi',NULL,NULL,3,'Sandile','Krokorok has specialized eyes that enable it to see in the dark. This ability lets Krokorok hunt in the dead of night without getting lost.',100,'F','Krokorok','112','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-113','Shiburingaru',NULL,NULL,3,'Krokorok','This Pokémon is known as the Bully of the Sands. Krookodile\'s mighty jaws can bite through heavy plates of iron with almost no effort at all.',160,'F','Krookodile','113','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh12-114','Yuu Nishida',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The first symptom of its sting is numbness. The next is an itching sensation so intense that it\'s impossible to resist the urge to claw at your skin.',60,'F','Mareanie','114','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-115','Ligton',NULL,NULL,2,'Mareanie','To survive in the cold waters of Galar, this Pokémon forms a dome with its legs, enclosing its body so it can capture its own body heat.',120,'F','Toxapex','115','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-116','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Intense hunger drives it to extremes of violence, and the electricity in its cheek sacs has converted into a Dark-type energy.',60,'F','Morpeko','116','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-117','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'From its rear, Beldum emits a magnetic force that rapidly pulls opponents in. They get skewered on Beldum\'s sharp claws.',60,'F','Beldum','117','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-118','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,'Beldum','Two Beldum have become stuck together via their own magnetic forces. With two brains, the resulting Metang has doubled psychic powers.',100,'F','Metang','118','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-119','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,3,'Metang','Because the magnetic powers of these Pokémon get stronger in freezing temperatures, Metagross living on snowy mountains are full of energy.',170,'F','Metagross','119','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh12-12','GOSSAN',NULL,NULL,3,'Foongus','This Pokémon puffs poisonous spores at its foes. If the spores aren\'t washed off quickly, they\'ll grow into mushrooms wherever they land.',90,'F','Amoonguss','12','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh12-120','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It is said to have the ability to grant any wish for just one week every thousand years.',90,'F','Radiant Jirachi','120','Radiant Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh12-121','ryoma uratsuka',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It defends itself by launching spikes, but its aim isn\'t very good at first. Only after a lot of practice will it improve.',60,'F','Ferroseed','121','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-122','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,'Ferroseed','This Pokémon scrapes its spikes across rocks, and then uses the tips of its feelers to absorb the nutrients it finds within the stone.',130,'F','Ferrothorn','122','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-123','Kyoko Umemoto',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The two minigears that compose this Pokémon are closer than twins. They mesh well only with each other.',50,'F','Klink','123','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-124','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,3,'Klink','When Klang goes all out, the minigear links up perfectly with the outer part of the big gear, and this Pokémon\'s rotation speed increases sharply.',90,'F','Klang','124','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-125','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,3,'Klang','From its spikes, it launches powerful blasts of electricity. Its red core contains an enormous amount of energy.',160,'F','Klinklang','125','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh12-126','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'This Pokémon appears in a legend alongside Terrakion and Virizion, fighting against humans in defense of the Unova region\'s Pokémon.',120,'F','Cobalion','126','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh12-127','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'With the long hairs on its back, this Pokémon takes in electricity from other electric Pokémon. It stores what it absorbs in an electric sac.',80,'F','Togedemaru','127','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-128','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,210,'F','Magearna V','128','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh12-129','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Dratini dwells near bodies of rapidly flowing water, such as the plunge pools of waterfalls. As it grows, Dratini will shed its skin many times.',70,'F','Dratini','129','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-13','Yuya Oka',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'They lay their eggs deep inside their nests. When attacked by Heatmor, they retaliate using their massive mandibles.',110,'F','Durant','13','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-130','Shinya Komatsu',NULL,NULL,2,'Dratini','This Pokémon lives in pristine oceans and lakes. It can control the weather, and it uses this power to fly into the sky, riding on the wind.',100,'F','Dragonair','130','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-131','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,2,'Dragonair','It\'s a kindhearted Pokémon. If it spots a drowning person or Pokémon, Dragonite simply must help them.',160,'F','Dragonite','131','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh12-132','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'After nightfall, they emerge from the caves they nest in during the day. Using their ultrasonic waves, they go on the hunt for ripened fruit.',60,'F','Noibat','132','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-133','aoki',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Noibat','Aggressive and cruel, this Pokémon will ruthlessly torment enemies that are helpless in the dark.',110,'F','Noivern','133','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh12-134','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Born when around 10% of Zygarde\'s cells have been gathered from all over, this form is skilled in close-range combat.',90,'F','Zygarde','134','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh12-135','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Regidrago V','135','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh12-136','PLANETA Yamashita',NULL,NULL,3,'Regidrago V',NULL,280,'F','Regidrago VSTAR','136','Rare Holo VSTAR','Pokémon'),('swsh12-137','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It draws symbols with the fluid that oozes from the tip of its tail. Depending on the symbol, Smeargle fanatics will pay big money for them.',70,'F','Smeargle','137','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-138','Mitsuhiro Arita',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Lugia V','138','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh12-139','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,2,'Lugia V',NULL,280,'F','Lugia VSTAR','139','Rare Holo VSTAR','Pokémon'),('swsh12-14','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'A legend tells of this Pokémon working together with Cobalion and Terrakion to protect the Pokémon of the Unova region.',110,'F','Virizion','14','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh12-140','AKIRA EGAWA',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,230,'F','Ho-Oh V','140','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh12-141','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Each Spinda\'s spot pattern is different. With its stumbling movements, it evades opponents\' attacks brilliantly!',90,'F','Spinda','141','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-142','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its cottony wings are full of air, making them light and fluffy to the touch. Swablu takes diligent care of its wings.',50,'F','Swablu','142','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-143','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,1,'Swablu','As it flies in a calm and relaxed manner, Altaria performs a humming song that would enrapture any audience.',110,'F','Altaria','143','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-144','saino misaki',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'If both of Buneary\'s ears are rolled up, something is wrong with its body or mind. It\'s a sure sign the Pokémon is in need of care.',60,'F','Buneary','144','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-145','Ryuta Fuse',NULL,NULL,1,'Buneary','Lopunny is constantly monitoring its surroundings. If danger approaches, this Pokémon responds with superdestructive kicks.',110,'F','Lopunny','145','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-146','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,'Unidentified Fossil','This Pokémon was successfully restored from a fossil. As research suggested, Archen is unable to fly. But it\'s very good at jumping.',80,'F','Archen','146','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh12-147','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,1,'Archen','It needs a running start to take off. If Archeops wants to fly, it first needs to run nearly 25 mph, building speed over a course of about 2.5 miles.',150,'F','Archeops','147','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh12-148','kurumitsu',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its chick-like looks belie its hotheadedness. It challenges its parents at every opportunity, desperate to prove its strength.',70,'F','Rufflet','148','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-149','Jiro Sasumo',NULL,NULL,1,'Rufflet','Screaming a bloodcurdling battle cry, this huge and ferocious bird Pokémon goes out on the hunt. It blasts lakes with shock waves, then scoops up any prey that float to the water\'s surface.',120,'F','Hisuian Braviary','149','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh12-15','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,230,'F','Chesnaught V','15','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh12-150','Shibuzoh.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Its melodious cries are actually warnings. Fletchling will mercilessly peck at anything that enters its territory.',40,'F','Fletchling','150','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh12-151','Ken Sugimori',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'F','Brandon','151','Uncommon','Trainer'),('swsh