Yukiko Baba',NULL,NULL,2,'Shroomish','It scatters poisonous spores and throws powerful punches while its foe is hampered by inhaled spores.',120,'E','Breloom','5','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-50','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Its hard shell repels any kind of attack. It is vulnerable only when its shell is open.',70,'E','Shellder','50','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-51','nagimiso',NULL,NULL,2,'Shellder','Once it slams its shell shut, it is impossible to open, even by those with superior strength.',130,'E','Cloyster','51','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh8-52','tetsuya koizumi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'No number of injuries can bother Staryu. Its amazing regenerative powers return it to its previous state in half a day!',60,'E','Staryu','52','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-53','Megumi Mizutani',NULL,NULL,1,'Staryu','It rotates its geometrically shaped body to swim through the water. It always seems to be sending out mysterious radio waves.',90,'E','Starmie','53','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh8-54','Naoki Saito',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Crossing icy seas is no issue for this cold-resistant Pokémon. Its smooth skin is a little cool to the touch.',120,'E','Lapras','54','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-55','Mizue',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its powerful, well-developed jaws are capable of crushing anything. Even its Trainer must be careful.',70,'E','Totodile','55','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-56','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,2,'Totodile','Once it bites down, it won\'t let go until it loses its fangs. New fangs quickly grow into place.',100,'E','Croconaw','56','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-57','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,3,'Croconaw','When it bites with its massive and powerful jaws, it shakes its head and savagely tears its victim up.',170,'E','Feraligatr','57','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh8-58','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Even after Marill swims in a cold sea, its water- repellent fur dries almost as soon as Marill leaves the water. That\'s why this Pokémon is never cold.',50,'E','Marill','58','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-59','Sanosuke Sakuma',NULL,NULL,2,'Marill','The bubble-like pattern on its stomach helps it camouflage itself when it\'s in the water.',120,'E','Azumarill','59','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh8-6','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'E','Breloom V','6','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh8-60','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The small spikes covering its body developed from scales. They inject a toxin that causes fainting.',80,'E','Qwilfish','60','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-61','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'As it majestically swims, it doesn\'t care if Remoraid attach to it to scavenge for its leftovers.',110,'E','Mantine','61','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-62','KIYOTAKA OSHIYAMA',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'To alert it, the fin on its head senses the flow of water. It has the strength to heft boulders.',70,'E','Mudkip','62','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-63','tetsuya koizumi',NULL,NULL,2,'Mudkip','Living on muddy ground that provides poor footing has made its legs sturdy.',90,'E','Marshtomp','63','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-64','Masakazu Fukuda',NULL,NULL,3,'Marshtomp','It can swim while towing a large ship. It bashes down foes with a swing of its thick arms.',170,'E','Swampert','64','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh8-65','Anesaki Dynamic',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Clamperl\'s pearls are exceedingly precious. They can be more than 10 times as costly as Shellder\'s pearls.',60,'E','Clamperl','65','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-66','otumami',NULL,NULL,1,'Clamperl','Deep seas are their habitat. According to tradition, when Huntail wash up onshore, something unfortunate will happen.',110,'E','Huntail','66','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh8-67','Misa Tsutsui',NULL,NULL,1,'Clamperl','It sucks bodily fluids out of its prey. The leftover meat sinks to the seafloor, where it becomes food for other Pokémon.',110,'E','Gorebyss','67','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh8-68','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The water stored inside the tuft on its head is full of nutrients. Plants that receive its water grow large.',60,'E','Panpour','68','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-69','Shin Nagasawa',NULL,NULL,1,'Panpour','It prefers places with clean water. When its tuft runs low, it replenishes it by siphoning up water with its tail.',100,'E','Simipour','69','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-7','Nagomi Nijo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s good at finding berries and gathers them from all over. It\'s kind enough to share them with friends.',60,'E','Pansage','7','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-70','Souichirou Gunjima',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Known for their violence, these Pokémon have the most fights with schools of red-striped Basculin.',80,'E','Basculin','70','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-71','Atsuko Nishida',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'The colder they get, the more energetic they are. They freeze their breath to make snowballs, using them as ammo for playful snowball fights.',80,'E','Galarian Darumaka','71','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-72','SATOSHI NAKAI',NULL,NULL,2,'Galarian Darumaka','Though it has a gentle disposition, it\'s also very strong. It will quickly freeze the snowball on its head before going for a headbutt.',130,'E','Galarian Darmanitan','72','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-73','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,210,'E','Greninja V','73','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh8-74','Pani Kobayashi',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It moves around by jetting water from its right pincer. It has a poor sense of balance, so it\'s terrible at swimming straight.',70,'E','Clauncher','74','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-75','tetsuya koizumi',NULL,NULL,2,'Clauncher','Its right arm is packed with meat. When its pincer falls off, it\'s exported to be used as a cooking ingredient.',110,'E','Clawitzer','75','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-76','MUGENUP',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,NULL,220,'E','Crabominable V','76','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh8-77','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It\'s covered in a slime that keeps its skin moist, allowing it to stay on land for days without drying up.',80,'E','Pyukumuku','77','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-78','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,200,'E','Inteleon V','78','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh8-79','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Inteleon V',NULL,320,'E','Inteleon VMAX','79','Rare Holo VMAX','Pokémon'),('swsh8-8','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,'Pansage','Ill tempered, it fights by swinging its barbed tail around wildly. The leaf growing on its head is very bitter.',100,'E','Simisage','8','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-80','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It starts off battles by attacking with its rock-hard horn, but as soon as the opponent flinches, this Pokémon bites down and never lets go.',80,'E','Chewtle','80','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-81','kodama',NULL,NULL,4,'Chewtle','This Pokémon rapidly extends its retractable neck to sink its sharp fangs into distant enemies and take them down.',140,'E','Drednaw','81','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-82','Miki Tanaka',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'After it\'s eaten its fill, its movements become extremely sluggish. That\'s when Cramorant swallows it up.',60,'E','Arrokuda','82','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-83','Hideki Ishikawa',NULL,NULL,1,'Arrokuda','It spins its tail fins to propel itself, surging forward at speeds of over 100 knots before ramming prey and spearing into them.',120,'E','Barraskewda','83','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-84','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It eats snow that piles up on the ground. The more snow it eats, the bigger and more impressive the spikes on its back grow.',40,'E','Snom','84','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-85','chibi',NULL,NULL,1,'Snom','It shows no mercy to any who desecrate fields and mountains. It will fly around on its icy wings, causing a blizzard to chase offenders away.',90,'E','Frosmoth','85','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-86','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,200,'E','Pikachu V','86','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh8-87','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Usually found in power plants. Easily mistaken for a Poké Ball, it has zapped many people.',60,'E','Voltorb','87','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-88','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Voltorb','It stores an overflowing amount of electric energy inside its body. Even a small shock makes it explode.',90,'E','Electrode','88','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh8-89','Megumi Higuchi',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It absorbs electricity from telephone poles. It shorts out its body to create crackling noises.',70,'E','Plusle','89','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-9','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Since this Pokémon makes its own clothes out of leaves, it is a popular mascot for fashion designers.',50,'E','Sewaddle','9','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-90','HYOGONOSUKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'It cheers on friends. If its friends are losing, its body lets off more and more sparks.',70,'E','Minun','90','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-91','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'All of its fur dazzles if danger is sensed. It flees while the foe is momentarily blinded.',50,'E','Shinx','91','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-92','Tika Matsuno',NULL,NULL,1,'Shinx','Strong electricity courses through the tips of its sharp claws. A light scratch causes fainting in foes.',90,'E','Luxio','92','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-93','Atsushi Furusawa',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Luxio','Luxray\'s ability to see through objects comes in handy when it\'s scouting for danger.',160,'E','Luxray','93','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh8-94','Sekio',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'With a body made of plasma, it can inhabit all sorts of machines. It loves to surprise others.',80,'E','Rotom','94','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-95','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'One alone can emit only a trickle of electricity, so a group of them gathers to unleash a powerful electric shock.',40,'E','Tynamo','95','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-96','Shigenori Negishi',NULL,NULL,2,'Tynamo','These Pokémon have a big appetite. When they spot their prey, they attack it and paralyze it with electricity.',90,'E','Eelektrik','96','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh8-97','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,3,'Eelektrik','They crawl out of the ocean using their arms. They will attack prey on shore and immediately drag it into the ocean.',160,'E','Eelektross','97','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh8-98','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The sun powers this Pokémon\'s electricity generation. Interruption of that process stresses Helioptile to the point of weakness.',70,'E','Helioptile','98','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh8-99','Kagemaru Himeno',NULL,NULL,1,'Helioptile','One Heliolisk basking in the sun with its frill outspread is all it would take to produce enough electricity to power a city.',110,'E','Heliolisk','99','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh9-1','0313',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Though it may look like it\'s just a bunch of eggs, it\'s a proper Pokémon. Exeggcute communicates with others of its kind via telepathy, apparently.',50,'F','Exeggcute','1','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh9-10','Yuka Morii',NULL,NULL,2,'Burmy','When Burmy evolved, its cloak became a part of this Pokémon\'s body. The cloak is never shed.',110,'F','Wormadam','10','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh9-100','Yuya Oka',NULL,NULL,4,NULL,'Boiling blood, like magma, circulates through its body. It makes its dwelling place in volcanic caves.',140,'F','Heatran','100','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh9-101','Nurikabe',NULL,NULL,2,'Karrablast','They use shells they\'ve stolen from Shelmet to arm and protect themselves. They\'re very popular Pokémon in the Galar region.',120,'F','Escavalier','101','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh9-102','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The two minigears that compose this Pokémon are closer than twins. They mesh well only with each other.',50,'F','Klink','102','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh9-103','Hataya',NULL,NULL,2,'Klink','When Klang goes all out, the minigear links up perfectly with the outer part of the big gear, and this Pokémon\'s rotation speed increases sharply.',90,'F','Klang','103','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh9-104','Megumi Higuchi',NULL,NULL,3,'Klang','From its spikes, it launches powerful blasts of electricity. Its red core contains an enormous amount of energy.',150,'F','Klinklang','104','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh9-105','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Zamazenta V','105','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh9-106','PLANETA Mochizuki',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Flygon V','106','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh9-107','sowsow',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Gible prefers to stay in narrow holes in the sides of caves heated by geothermal energy. This way, Gible can stay warm even during a blizzard.',70,'F','Gible','107','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh9-108','hatachu',NULL,NULL,1,'Gible','This Pokémon emits ultrasonic waves from a protrusion on either side of its head to probe pitch-dark caves.',90,'F','Gabite','108','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh9-109','Nurikabe',NULL,NULL,1,'Gabite','Garchomp makes its home in volcanic mountains. It flies through the sky as fast as a jet airplane, hunting down as much prey as it can.',160,'F','Garchomp','109','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh9-11','Akira Komayama',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Burmy','It flutters around at night and steals honey from the Combee hive.',110,'F','Mothim','11','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh9-110','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'These Pokémon nest in the ground and use their tusks to crush hard berries. Crushing berries is also how they test each other\'s strength.',60,'F','Axew','110','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh9-111','Hataya',NULL,NULL,2,'Axew','After battle, this Pokémon carefully sharpens its tusks on river rocks. It needs to take care of its tusks—if one breaks, it will never grow back.',100,'F','Fraxure','111','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh9-112','Uta',NULL,NULL,2,'Fraxure','Its resilient tusks are its pride and joy. It licks up dirt to take in the minerals it needs to keep its tusks in top condition.',170,'F','Haxorus','112','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh9-113','Ryo Ueda',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'Druddigon are vicious and cunning. They take up residence in nests dug out by other Pokémon, treating the stolen nests as their own lairs.',120,'E','Druddigon','113','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh9-114','Satoshi Shirai',NULL,NULL,3,NULL,NULL,220,'E','Dracovish V','114','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh9-115','Tomokazu Komiya',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The stalk this Pokémon carries in its wings serves as a sword to cut down opponents. In a dire situation, the stalk can also serve as food.',80,'F','Farfetch\'d','115','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh9-116','kawayoo',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'Its form changes depending on the weather. The rougher conditions get, the rougher Castform\'s disposition!',70,'F','Castform','116','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh9-117','Saya Tsuruta',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'They flock around mountains and fields, chasing after bug Pokémon. Their singing is noisy and annoying.',60,'F','Starly','117','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh9-118','Kouki Saitou',NULL,NULL,1,'Starly','It lives in forests and fields. Squabbles over territory occur when flocks collide.',90,'F','Staravia','118','Uncommon','Pokémon'),('swsh9-119','Narumi Sato',NULL,NULL,1,'Staravia','When Staravia evolve into Staraptor, they leave the flock to live alone. They have sturdy wings.',150,'F','Staraptor','119','Rare','Pokémon'),('swsh9-12','Naoyo Kimura',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The deeper a Cherubi\'s red, the more nutrients it has stockpiled in its body. And the sweeter and tastier its small ball!',40,'E','Cherubi','12','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh9-120','Oswaldo KATO',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'It constantly gnaws on logs and rocks to whittle down its front teeth. It nests alongside water.',70,'F','Bidoof','120','Common','Pokémon'),('swsh9-121','OKACHEKE',NULL,NULL,2,'Bidoof','It makes its nest by damming streams with bark and mud. It is known as an industrious worker.',120,'F','Bibarel','121','Rare Holo','Pokémon'),('swsh9-122','N-DESIGN Inc.',NULL,NULL,2,NULL,NULL,220,'F','Arceus V','122','Rare Holo V','Pokémon'),('swsh9-123','5ban Graphics',NULL,NULL,2,'Arceus V',NULL,280,'F','Arceus VSTAR','123','Rare Holo VSTAR','Pokémon'),('swsh9-124','Mina Nakai',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,'The way it brushes away grime with its tail can be helpful when cleaning. But its focus on spotlessness can make cleaning more of a hassle.'